#: ./fork_powers.json
msgid "[Ψ]Circuit Sense (C)"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Circuit Sense (C)
#: ./fork_powers.json
msgid ""
"Extend your electrokinetic senses into the flow of current itself, feeling how electrons want to move through wire and silicon.  While maintained, you understand electronics as though far more practiced: your effective Electronics skill is raised by 3 for crafting, repair, and anything else that tests it.  It does NOT make you craft faster -- only more capable, and only at electronics.\n"
"\n"
"This power <color_yellow>is maintained by concentration</color> and <color_red>may fail</color> if <color_yellow>concentration is interrupted</color>."
msgstr ""

#: ./fork_powers.json
msgid "Circuit Sense"
msgstr ""

#. ~ desc of effect 'effect_electrokinetic_circuit_sense'
#: ./fork_powers.json
msgid ""
"Your electrokinetic senses are tuned to the flow of current; you read "
"electronics with a practiced eye (+3 effective Electronics skill)."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Remove message for effect(s) 'Circuit Sense'.
#: ./fork_powers.json
msgid "Your sense of the current fades; electronics look ordinary again."
msgstr ""

#: ./fork_powers.json
msgid "[Ψ]Lightning Strike"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Lightning Strike
#: ./fork_powers.json
msgid ""
"Call down a focused bolt of lightning onto a single target you can see, dealing heavy electric damage at long range.  As your skill grows the strike broadens: at power level 9 and beyond it also lashes everything in the ring of tiles immediately around the point of impact.  The thunderclap is louder than a gunshot.\n"
"\n"
"Range, damage, and (from level 9 on) blast radius all increase with power level."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for the sound of spell '[Ψ]Lightning Strike'
#: ./fork_powers.json
msgid "KRAKA-THOOM!"
msgstr ""

#: ./fork_powers.json
msgid "[Ψ]No Go Zone (C)"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]No Go Zone (C)
#: ./fork_powers.json
msgid ""
"Project a telekinetic cordon that refuses to let anything crowd you.  While maintained, creatures cannot hold a tile adjacent to you -- the field shoves them back a step the instant they close.  They can still lurk one tile beyond and reach or shoot at you; they simply cannot get in your face.\n"
"\n"
"This power is maintained by concentration and may fail if concentration is interrupted."
msgstr ""

#: ./fork_powers.json
msgid "No Go Zone"
msgstr ""

#. ~ desc of effect 'effect_telekinetic_nogozone'
#: ./fork_powers.json
msgid ""
"A telekinetic exclusion field holds enemies at bay, preventing them from "
"closing to melee range."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Remove message for effect(s) 'No Go Zone'.
#: ./fork_powers.json
msgid "The exclusion field collapses; the space around you is open again."
msgstr ""

#: ./fork_powers.json
msgid "[Ψ]See Mechanisms"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]See Mechanisms
#: ./fork_powers.json
msgid ""
"Open your inner eye to the hidden workings of a lock: the pins of a deadbolt, the wards of a padlock, the tumblers turning behind a safe's dial.  Seeing the answer isn't the same as acting on it, though -- picking a lock still takes a lockpick in your hand and a few moments' work, guided so surely it can never fail or trip an alarm.  A dial safe is the one exception: once you've read the wheels inside, your hand alone can turn it the right way the first time -- no tool, no time at all.\n"
"\n"
"Affects one MECHANICAL lock at a time, right next to you: a keyed or deadbolt door, a barred door, a chain gate, a pickable metal door, a mechanical gun safe, or a locked display case -- all of these need a lockpick in hand.  A dial safe needs nothing but your hand.  It has no purchase on electronic locks and card readers -- a circuit has no moving mechanism to see."
msgstr ""

#: ./fork_powers.json
msgid "[Ψ]Mass Hydrothermosis"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Mass Hydrothermosis
#: ./fork_powers.json
msgid ""
"Reach out with your mind and, in a single instant, bring the fluids inside every creature you can see to a violent boil.  Blood, lymph, insect ichor, hydraulic fluid, coolant, machine oil -- if it flows, it flashes to steam.  Nothing burns and no ground catches fire; the heat happens entirely INSIDE your targets, all at once.\n"
"\n"
"This strikes <color_yellow>every hostile creature in your line of sight</color> -- however far you can see is however far it reaches, which is what makes it a capstone.  It has no purchase only on the truly fluidless (see-through drones like eyebots are borderline) and on nether-null horrors your power cannot touch at all.  Your own companions are spared.  Damage grows with your mastery.\n"
"\n"
"The cost is punishing; you will not cast this twice in a row.\n"
"\n"
"Level 6 leads to Crucible with Conflagration 10 + Mass Hydrothermosis 6 + Molten Land 14 OR Conflagration 10 + Flamethrower 10 + Mass Hydrothermosis 6."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for the sound of spell '[Ψ]Mass Hydrothermosis'
#: ./fork_powers.json
msgid "the wet sizzle and burst of boiling fluids!"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Message for SPELL '[Ψ]Mass Hydrothermosis'
#: ./fork_powers.json
msgid "You reach into every creature in sight and boil them from within!"
msgstr ""

#: ./fork_powers.json
msgid "[Ψ]Kinetic Trap"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Kinetic Trap
#: ./fork_powers.json
msgid ""
"Pour kinetic energy into a pile of scrap metal and wind it tighter and tighter, until the metal is holding far more force than it should and is only barely stable.  Leave it on the ground beside you.  The next enemy to disturb it gets the whole store at once: a hammer-blow of force and a spray of shredded metal.\n"
"\n"
"Consumes <color_yellow>4 scrap metal</color> each cast.  The trap is visible to you, and <color_yellow>you and your allies can walk over it safely</color>.  Below level 5 it leaves a Kinetic Trap (20 bash + 20 shrapnel); from level 5 a Strong Kinetic Trap (35 + 35); from level 10 a Powerful Kinetic Trap (50 + 50)."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Message for SPELL '[Ψ]Kinetic Trap'
#: ./fork_powers.json
msgid "You wind force into the scrap until it trembles."
msgstr ""

#: ./fork_powers.json
msgid "[Ψ]Pyrolytic Trap"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Pyrolytic Trap
#: ./fork_powers.json
msgid ""
"Soak a splash of fuel or oil with heat, far past the point where it should have ignited, and hold it there, a hair's breadth from bursting into flame.  Leave it on the ground beside you.  The next enemy to disturb it is caught in a flash of heat and left standing in the fire that follows.\n"
"\n"
"Consumes <color_yellow>50 mL of fuel, oil or alcohol fuel</color> each cast (gasoline, diesel, biodiesel, avgas, JP8, lamp oil, motor oil, ethanol, methanol, denatured alcohol, or vegetable or animal cooking oil).  The trap is visible to you, and <color_yellow>you and your allies can walk over it safely</color>.  Below level 5 it leaves a Pyrolytic Trap (20 heat, small fire); from level 5 a Strong Pyrolytic Trap (35 heat, fire); from level 10 a Powerful Pyrolytic Trap (50 heat, large fire)."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Message for SPELL '[Ψ]Pyrolytic Trap'
#: ./fork_powers.json
msgid "You pour heat into the fuel until it shimmers on the edge of igniting."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'Kinetic trap trigger', '//~': 'NO_I18N'}
#. ~ Description for {'str': 'Pyrolytic trap trigger', '//~': 'NO_I18N'}
#: ./fork_powers.json
msgid ""
"Cast by a primed psionic trap on whatever set it off.  Applies "
"mom_primed_trap_hit; mom_hooks' handler spares the caster and allies and "
"detonates for everyone else."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for {'str': 'mom_kinetic_trap_noise', '//~': 'NO_I18N'}
#. ~ Description for {'str': 'mom_pyrolytic_trap_noise', '//~': 'NO_I18N'}
#: ./fork_powers.json
msgid ""
"Detonation noise for a primed psionic trap; cast from Lua with the victim as"
" source."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for the sound of spell '{'str': 'mom_kinetic_trap_noise',
#. '//~': 'NO_I18N'}'
#: ./fork_powers.json
