msgstr ""

#: ./furniture_and_terrain/psi_enclave.json
msgid "thump."
msgstr ""

#: ./furniture_and_terrain/terrain_alien.json
msgid "black stone"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for black stone
#: ./furniture_and_terrain/terrain_alien.json
msgid ""
"A perfectly smooth patch of black stone, like carved and polished obsidian."
msgstr ""

#: ./furniture_and_terrain/terrain_alien.json
msgid "black water"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for black water
#: ./furniture_and_terrain/terrain_alien.json
msgid ""
"An expanse of some sort of black liquid.  The air nearby is chill, and its "
"surface is perfectly smooth and undisturbed by ripples or wind.  You have no"
" idea how deep it is."
msgstr ""

#: ./furniture_and_terrain/terrain_alien.json
msgid "alien grass"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for alien grass
#: ./furniture_and_terrain/terrain_alien.json
msgid ""
"An area of something that almost looks like grass.  The blades are rolled up"
" into curls, similar to ferns, but they seem to all unroll at once and then "
"roll up again in a steady pattern.  They're a color you can only describe as"
" \"purplish-yellow\"."
msgstr ""

#: ./furniture_and_terrain/terrain_alien.json
msgid "thump"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for alien grass
#: ./furniture_and_terrain/terrain_alien.json
msgid ""
"An area of something that almost looks like grass.  The blades are less than"
" an inch high and a blue so dark it's almost black.  When you look closer, "
"many blades seemed to be fused together at the top, forming small clusters."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for alien grass
#: ./furniture_and_terrain/terrain_alien.json
msgid ""
"An area of something that almost looks like grass.  It's the familiar green "
"of terrestrial grass, but each blade has a large pink bulb at the top that "
"bobs and moves in the breeze."
msgstr ""

#: ./furniture_and_terrain/terrain_alien.json
msgid "alien vines"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for alien vines
#: ./furniture_and_terrain/terrain_alien.json
msgid ""
"An area of something that almost looks like vines, or perhaps tree roots.  A"
" thick ropy cluster of white tendrils streaked with red, twining around each"
" other and branching off in all directions before meeting up in new "
"clusters.  Sometimes, one of the vines twitches."
msgstr ""

#: ./furniture_and_terrain/terrain_alien.json
msgid "alien moss"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for alien moss
#: ./furniture_and_terrain/terrain_alien.json
msgid ""
"An area of something that almost looks like moss.  It's a pale bluish color "
"and clumps of it seem to be very slowly moving across the ground."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for alien moss
#: ./furniture_and_terrain/terrain_alien.json
msgid ""
"An area of something that almost looks like moss.  It's close to an inch "
"thick, a dark yellowish-red, and glistens wetly."
msgstr ""

#: ./furniture_and_terrain/terrain_alien.json
msgid "alien tree"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for alien tree
#: ./furniture_and_terrain/terrain_alien.json
msgid ""
"A short tree, or something that's vaguely shaped like one.  It has long, "
"needle-like leaves that twitch rhythmically and its dark reddish-purple "
"bark(?) has a scale-like pattern, with glowing nodules irregularly spaced "
"along its trunk.  Bluish-green globules hang from the end of some of the "
"branches."
msgstr ""

#: ./furniture_and_terrain/terrain_alien.json
msgid "poof!"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for alien tree
#: ./furniture_and_terrain/terrain_alien.json
msgid ""
"A tall alien plant.  It has long, needle-like leaves that twitch "
"rhythmically and its dark reddish-purple bark(?) has a scale-like pattern, "
"with glowing nodules irregularly spaced along its trunk."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for alien tree
#: ./furniture_and_terrain/terrain_alien.json
msgid ""
"A tall, thin alien plant.  From a distance it seems more like a column than "
"a tree, but when you get closer you can see that it's made up of a series of"
" broad, serrated leaves all folded so closely together that they form a "
"single stalk."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for alien tree
#: ./furniture_and_terrain/terrain_alien.json
msgid ""
"A large alien plant.  It looks like a series of bulbous mushrooms that have "
"all grown together at the base, rising into a flaring series of branches "
"that curve up before hanging down and ending in reddish-brown spheres."
msgstr ""

#: ./furniture_and_terrain/terrain_doors.json
msgid "reinforced concrete wall"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for reinforced concrete wall
#: ./furniture_and_terrain/terrain_doors.json
msgid ""
"An extremely resilient wall, filled with concrete and rebar.  Best suited "
"for supporting multi-level buildings, only serious explosives and high-speed"
" impacts would be capable of damaging this wall."
msgstr ""

#: ./furniture_and_terrain/terrain_doors.json
msgid "scrrrash!"
msgstr ""

#: ./furniture_and_terrain/terrain_doors.json
msgid "whump!"
msgstr ""

#: ./furniture_and_terrain/terrain_doors.json
msgid "open secret door"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for open secret door
#: ./furniture_and_terrain/terrain_doors.json
msgid ""
"This apparently normal segment of reinforced concrete wall has opened to "
"reveal a secret passage."
msgstr ""

#: ./furniture_and_terrain/terrain_flora.json
msgid "oak tree"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for oak tree
#: ./furniture_and_terrain/terrain_flora.json
msgid ""
"A massive deciduous tree belonging to the 'Quercus' genus, commonly found "
"throughout the New England region.  If you look closely, you can see some "
"acorns the squirrels haven't gotten yet.  If you look near the top, you can "
"see a gigantic birds nest.  There are large bones sticking out of the edges "
"of the nest."
msgstr ""

#: ./furniture_and_terrain/terrain_tanks.json
msgid "Osiris chamber"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for Osiris chamber
#: ./furniture_and_terrain/terrain_tanks.json
msgid ""
"A vat full of faintly-glowing solution, large enough to hold an adult human "
"with room to spare.  It was obviously used for some kind of scientific "
"experiments, and, based on the glowing lights on the base and the still-"
"active computer terminal next to it, could be used for such again."
msgstr ""

#: ./furniture_and_terrain/terrain_tanks.json
msgid "ker-rash!"
msgstr ""

#: ./furniture_and_terrain/terrain_tanks.json
msgid "plunk."
