#: ./npcs/dialogue/portal_future_you.json
#: ./npcs/dialogue/refugee_guards_generic.json
#: ./npcs/dialogue/refugee_guards_traitor.json
msgid "[Premonition] *Check for anything amiss*"
msgstr ""

#: ./npcs/dialogue/portal_future_you.json
msgid "[Premonition 8+] *Check for anything amiss*"
msgstr ""

#: ./npcs/dialogue/portal_future_you.json
msgid "[Sense Hostility] *Determine if the voice is a threat*"
msgstr ""

#: ./npcs/dialogue/portal_future_you.json
msgid "[Telepath] *Read the voice's mind(?)*"
msgstr ""

#: ./npcs/dialogue/portal_future_you.json
msgid ""
"&You reach out to the voice's location(?) and try to touch its thoughts.  In"
" an instant, your mind is filled by a babble of your *own* thoughts, at "
"exactly the moment you think them, which then repeat again as you realize "
"what is happening and your thoughts about the experience are reflected back "
"at you and your brain is filled with an agonizing cacophony until you break "
"the connection."
msgstr ""

#: ./npcs/dialogue/portal_future_you.json
msgid "Well, that was a mistake."
msgstr ""

#: ./npcs/dialogue/portal_future_you.json
msgid ""
"&You extend your senses, alert for danger, and are immediately almost "
"blinded.  In the heart of the portal storm, there's danger everywhere.  In "
"the air and ground, in the things half-glimpsed that vanish when you look at"
" them, and in yourself, just waiting for the right conditions to be "
"unleashed.  If there's anything sinister in the voice's offer, you cannot "
"tell."
msgstr ""

#: ./npcs/dialogue/portal_future_you.json
msgid "*Close your inner eye*"
msgstr ""

#: ./npcs/dialogue/portal_future_you.json
msgid ""
"&You extend your senses, alert for danger.  Shutting out the ever-present "
"danger of the post-Cataclysmic world and the portal storm, you focus on your"
" immediate surroundings.  There is danger there, but not directly.  Whatever"
" the outcome of its offer, it is not meant as a trap."
msgstr ""

#: ./npcs/dialogue/portal_future_you.json
msgid ""
"&You focus on the voice, trying to determine its intentions, and are surprised.  The voice, at least, does not mean you any harm.\n"
"\n"
"As you withdraw your senses, however, you can't help but realize that in these circumstances, that doesn't necessarily mean you won't come to any harm."
msgstr ""

#: ./npcs/dialogue/portal_future_you.json
msgid "[Clarity 3+] *Is the voice lying?*"
msgstr ""

#: ./npcs/dialogue/portal_future_you.json
msgid ""
"&You open your inner eye and in its light you see the truth.  This *is* you."
"  Was you.  Might be you.  You know it like you know yourself.  Whatever "
"game it's playing, its intentions are not malicious.  They are your own."
msgstr ""

#: ./npcs/dialogue/portal_future_you.json
msgid "What do I need to do?"
msgstr ""

#: ./npcs/dialogue/portal_future_you.json
msgid "Leave me alone."
msgstr ""

#: ./npcs/dialogue/portal_future_you.json
msgid ""
"[Gateway 8+] Thanks, but here I can leave without your help.  Be seeing you."
"  (End your story)"
msgstr ""

#: ./npcs/dialogue/portal_future_you.json
msgid ""
"&Normally you need to have been to your destination to teleport to it, but here in the heart of the chaos you can sense other worlds.  Other times.  An endless torrent of possibility, flowing continuously around and over and through you.  None of it lasts long enough for you to get a good glimpse, but almost anywhere has to be better than here.  With a simple act of will, you reach out and grasp one chance as it floats by, open a doorway, and leave your dying world behind.\n"
"\n"
"And what happens to you afterwards, well, that's another story."
msgstr ""

#: ./npcs/dialogue/portal_future_you.json
msgid "That's what life's about: making the right choice at the right time."
msgstr ""

#: ./npcs/dialogue/portal_interdimensional_traveler.json
msgid "[Telepath] *Read the strange person's mind*"
msgstr ""

#: ./npcs/dialogue/portal_interdimensional_traveler.json
msgid "«Jasz vata aralas mat!  On de farah shatan!  Mazeh jast ond!»"
msgstr ""

#: ./npcs/dialogue/portal_interdimensional_traveler.json
msgid "Well, that didn't help either."
msgstr ""

#: ./npcs/dialogue/refugee_guards_generic.json
#: ./npcs/dialogue/refugee_guards_traitor.json
msgid "[Sense Hostility] *Determine if they're a threat*"
msgstr ""

#: ./npcs/dialogue/refugee_guards_generic.json
msgid ""
"&You open your senses to any dangers.  You have a faint sense of foreboding,"
" but that's it."
msgstr ""

#: ./npcs/dialogue/refugee_guards_generic.json
msgid ""
"&A quick check reveals nothing out of the ordinary.  To them, you're just "
"another face in the crowd."
msgstr ""

#: ./npcs/dialogue/refugee_guards_generic.json
msgid "<telepathy_refugee_guard>"
msgstr ""

#: ./npcs/dialogue/refugee_guards_generic.json
msgid "[Premonition] *Determine if they're a threat*"
msgstr ""

#: ./npcs/dialogue/refugee_guards_generic.json
msgid ""
"&You open your senses, alert for danger, but don't sense anything.  They "
"bear you no ill will at all."
msgstr ""

#: ./npcs/dialogue/refugee_guards_generic.json
msgid "«Oh great.  Another one.»"
msgstr ""

#: ./npcs/dialogue/refugee_guards_generic.json
msgid "«Idle hands make a waste of time.»"
msgstr ""

#: ./npcs/dialogue/refugee_guards_generic.json
msgid ""
"«We need to post sentries outside that'll turn some of these people away.»"
msgstr ""

#: ./npcs/dialogue/refugee_guards_generic.json
msgid ""
"«We really should start locking the doors at night so these people can't get"
" in.»"
msgstr ""

#: ./npcs/dialogue/refugee_guards_generic.json
msgid "«Wow, I'm amazed he's lived this long.»"
msgstr ""

#: ./npcs/dialogue/refugee_guards_generic.json
msgid "«Wow, I'm amazed she's lived this long.»"
msgstr ""

#: ./npcs/dialogue/refugee_guards_generic.json
msgid "«No point in learning his name.  He'll probably be dead soon anyway.»"
msgstr ""

#: ./npcs/dialogue/refugee_guards_generic.json
msgid "«No point in learning her name.  She'll probably be dead soon anyway.»"
msgstr ""

#: ./npcs/dialogue/refugee_guards_generic.json
msgid ""
"&You open your senses, alert for danger, but don't sense anything.  They are"
" sincere in their friendliness, or at least aren't hiding a dagger behind "
"their back."
msgstr ""

#: ./npcs/dialogue/refugee_guards_generic.json
msgid "«Not bad playing tour guide.  Better than having to fight.»"
msgstr ""

#: ./npcs/dialogue/refugee_guards_generic.json
msgid "«Another day after <the_cataclysm>.  One foot in front of the other.»"
msgstr ""

#: ./npcs/dialogue/refugee_guards_generic.json
msgid "«So tired.  That's what I get for drawing the night shift.»"
msgstr ""

#: ./npcs/dialogue/refugee_guards_generic.json
msgid "«At least in here I can see them coming.  If I were out there…»"
msgstr ""

#: ./npcs/dialogue/refugee_guards_generic.json
msgid "«How much did it take to get here?  What has he lost?»"
msgstr ""

#: ./npcs/dialogue/refugee_guards_generic.json
msgid "«How much did it take to get here?  What has she lost?»"
msgstr ""

#: ./npcs/dialogue/refugee_guards_traitor.json
msgid "It's you."
msgstr ""

#: ./npcs/dialogue/refugee_guards_traitor.json
msgid ""
"&You open up your senses and the hair on the back of your neck immediately "
"stands up.  Something could go very wrong for you at any moment."
msgstr ""

#: ./npcs/dialogue/refugee_guards_traitor.json
msgid ""
"&You barely open up your senses before you're met with an overpowering sense"
" of menace.  They aren't planning to kill you at this exact second but that "
"could change at any moment."
msgstr ""

#: ./npcs/dialogue/refugee_guards_traitor.json
msgid "«Just what I need.  Come on, leave me alone.»"
msgstr ""

#: ./npcs/dialogue/refugee_guards_traitor.json
msgid "«How am I supposed to…ugh, just go away.»"
msgstr ""

#: ./npcs/dialogue/refugee_guards_traitor.json
msgid "«Who does this asshole think he is?»"
msgstr ""

#: ./npcs/dialogue/refugee_guards_traitor.json
msgid "[Telepathy 8+] *Go deeper*."
msgstr ""

#: ./npcs/dialogue/refugee_guards_traitor.json
msgid ""
"&It's only a moment, but that's enough.  You are looking from behind a tree "
"onto a road where a crude roadblock has been set up.  There's a refugee bus,"
" one of the same ones parked outside the refugee center, stopped at the "
"roadblock, and as the driver gets out to look at the roadblock, there's a "
"loud crack and two spots of red appear on his chest and leg.  As he begins "
"to fall and the people in the bus start screaming, the raiders emerge from "
"the trees, already running with guns raised."
msgstr ""

#: ./npcs/dialogue/refugee_guards_traitor.json
msgid "*Withdraw from their mind*."
msgstr ""

#: ./npcs/dialogue/refugee_guards_traitor.json
msgid "&Only a few moments have passed.  They haven't noticed anything amiss."
msgstr ""

#: ./npcs/dialogue/refugee_guards_traitor.json
msgid "What the hell are you talking about?"
msgstr ""

#: ./npcs/dialogue/refugee_guards_traitor.json
msgid ""
"He was only a child, and you killed him.  Do you remember the blood on his "
"Superman shirt?"
msgstr ""

#: ./npcs/dialogue/refugee_guards_traitor.json
msgid ""
"I didn't tell you my na-\"  Their face goes white.  \"What the fuck!  You "
"some kind of freak?"
msgstr ""

#: ./npcs/dialogue/refugee_guards_traitor.json
msgid "It's over.  Give up."
msgstr ""

#: ./npcs/dialogue/refugee_guards_traitor.json
msgid "[Telekinesis Check] *Try to rip their weapon away*"
msgstr ""

#: ./npcs/dialogue/refugee_guards_traitor.json
msgid "[Transposition Check] *Teleport away their weapon*."
msgstr ""

#: ./npcs/dialogue/refugee_guards_traitor.json
msgid "[Oubliette Check] *Banish them to another dimension*."
msgstr ""

#: ./npcs/dialogue/refugee_guards_traitor.json
msgid ""
"*stares at you with eyes wide as their weapon vanishes into thin air.  Their"
" mouth works silently but no sounds come out."
msgstr ""

#: ./npcs/dialogue/refugee_guards_traitor.json
msgid "Get out of here or you'll be next."
msgstr ""

#: ./npcs/dialogue/refugee_guards_traitor.json
msgid ""
"*starts as the weapon is ripped out of their hands and falls to the floor.  "
"\"Holy shit!  What the fuck?!\""
msgstr ""

#: ./npcs/dialogue/refugee_guards_traitor.json
msgid "Leave or I'll do the same to you."
msgstr ""

#: ./npcs/dialogue/refugee_guards_traitor.json
msgid "Alright, alright, I'm leaving.  Holy shit."
msgstr ""

#: ./npcs/dialogue/refugee_guards_traitor.json
msgid "Good."
msgstr ""

#: ./npcs/dialogue/refugee_guards_traitor.json
msgid "I changed my mind.  You're better off in the ground."
msgstr ""

#: ./npcs/dialogue/refugee_guards_traitor.json
msgid ""
"*immediately backs away.  They never turn their back on you, but in a few "
"moments they go out the door and are gone."
msgstr ""

