#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"At 1756 (dive time), Sergeant Eric Collins's team came under attack by an "
"XE157 entity near the end of scheduled in-phase time.  Despite the "
"expenditure of most of their ordinance, XE157 suffered no significant damage"
" and continued its attack.  Despite the known combat capabilities of XE157 "
"and with no regard for his own safety, Sergeant Collins ordered his team to "
"retreat to the dive breachhead and engaged it in hand-to-hand combat, "
"holding it off for several minutes while his team exited the dive.  The "
"aperture was held open for an additional minute afterward, allowing just "
"enough time for a severely-injured Sergeant Collins to exit the dive and "
"preventing the exit of XE157.  Sergeant Collins suffered severe lacerations,"
" the loss of two fingers, and burns across fifty percent of his arms and "
"upper body; he has since volunteered to be a test subject for SMOKE USHER.  "
"In lieu of a medal, we have authorized a meritorious service bonus to be "
"applied retroactive to the beginning of the year."
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"Treadmills?  Blood ox tests?  Have them try to punch through walls or something\n"
"Any cellular difference?  Should check\n"
"Brains show no difference but what about organs?  Lactic acid production, inflammation, blood flow, etc.\n"
"\n"
"Outrun a horse?\n"
"\n"
"Yeah, yeah, faster than a speeding bullet.  VERDANT HAND vs ONYX LIGHTNING?\n"
"Oh come on.\n"
"What about jumping distance?  Height?\n"
"\n"
"\n"
"*a doodle of two stick figures engaged in a martial arts battle*\n"
"Actually do the shoryuken.  Too bad gun still beats fist\n"
"Hadoken?  Wouldn't surprise me at this point\n"
"Grip strength tests?  Charts?  zzzzz  *a surprisingly-detailed picture of a curled-up sleeping cat*\n"
"Summary: Ban them from the Olympics"
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"The battle of the century!  H84 and E94 will fight to determine the true greatest VERDANT HAND graduate!  No holds barred, no attacks banned, no referee, don't sit in the front row or you might ruin your clothes!  Be there or be square!\n"
"\n"
"*below the text is an picture of a man and a woman striking a boxing pose at each other in an ordinary office room.  Both are wearing street clothes and baring their teeth at each other.  The date of the fight is one week before the end of the world*"
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"Upon leaving for the evening, Dr. Erickson neglected to seal cage #3, allowing one of the experimental mice (#748562) to gain access to the matrix crystal supplies.  One crystal discharged, affecting 748562 and apparently causing an awakening.  748562 escaped the room, squeezing under the door, and is currently loose within the facility.\n"
"\n"
"Dr. Erickson has been placed on administrative leave pending a full investigation and new procedures for storing matrix crystals are currently being implemented.  A search for 748562 is still underway."
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"They wanted me to keep a logbook of my daily exercise but I don't understand the point.  I run, I lift, I sleep, that's about all these have me do here.  What, they want \"5:40 a.m.: 30 reps 250 lbs, run 20 minutes, 100 burpees (10 sets)\" blah blah who cares?  That shit doesn't matter.  We're all trapped here and things are going to hell and we got some kind of poison in our bodies that's going to bring us back when we die so we can eat brains.\n"
"\n"
"Well, fine, here's my log: 6:05 a.m.: 50 reps 400 lbs, sprint 10 minutes, 200 pull-ups, triple somersault from a standing start.  Put me in the Olympics right now."
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"They demanded that I include that title on this report even though it's pretentious as hell.  This isn't some superweapon that will change the face of modern warfare, it's just a better form of hand-to-hand combat.  They can't dodge bullets.  They can't punch through brick walls.  They can't do that movie thing where the hero hits a bad guy and the bad guy goes flying twenty feet.  They're just faster and stronger and hit harder, all good things, but they aren't going to beat someone with a gun.  There's a reason we invented guns and why functional martial arts training is about defending yourself and getting away, not about going on the offense.\n"
"\n"
"So is it worth training people?  That's the wrong question.  This isn't a codified martial art, it's just using dimensional metaphysics to enhance existing methods of combat.  A VERDANT HAND candidate will be better at Muay Thai than anyone who hasn't gone through BURNT NOVEMBER but they still need the actual martial arts training.  This is just another tool.  I'm not sure why there's so much focus on this, to be honest.  With the cost of retrieving materials, surely we could spend that money better elsewhere.  Modern warfare does not rely on single superheroes winning battles."
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"I'm looking up at the sky.  I can see the same constellations on Earth, but they're shimmering somehow, like there's a haze or a fog or something between us.  Then, the stars start to slowly go out.  Not in a wave, but randomly--one here, one there, faster and faster until the entire sky was dark.  Then the moon disappeared as well and everything went black.\n"
"\n"
"I'm standing on the edge of a cliff.  Below me is the churning sea, the waters black under the stormclouds.  The sea rises slowly as rain falls in sheets, lightning striking the waters.  They break over the edge of the cliff, then over my head.  I drown.\n"
"\n"
"I am standing in a forest.  The trees rustle all around me and the birds sing, and then clouds pass over the sun.  The sun dims and then starts to go black.  It's an eclipse.  The light fades and all the birdsong dies.  I stand in pitch blackness with the rustle of leaves around me."
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"O21 was placed blindfolded in a completely dark room with a deck of shuffled playing cards, instructed to remove the blindfold, and asked to sort them in standard order: clubs, diamonds, hearts, spades, each in numerical order.  Task was completed in 6:03 with 18/52 cards in the proper order and minor to major ordering errors in all other cards.  O21 was then asked to drink from the coffee cup in the room.  Cup was placed on a shelf above the door to prevent movement around the room from discovering it, but task was completed in 1:14, with the only difficulty being their's height (158 cm) making it harder to reach the shelf.  O21 was then asked to cross the room to the table, pick up the paper, and read the sequence of numbers written on it.  O21 was unable to do so, only correctly reciting the first two digits.\n"
"\n"
"Experiment does uphold the thesis that successful NOBLE HORIZON mathematicians perceive their surroundings through means other than light.  As O21 was unable to read the document, their sense is not \"sight\" as such.  Further experimentation to determine its limits is necessary."
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"Dr. Richardson,\n"
"After all of the time and money I wish I had more promising news to report.  Netherum mathematics is an inexact science, as you well know, so it's very hard to find a protocol that will work the same every time.  Melchior has the advantage of processing speed but our mathematicians have to put in the hours, but they can make connections Melchior cannot because he can only work with the data he's given, whereas NOBLE HORIZON provides new data.  But, unpredictably.  We've discovered any number of immersion destinations where the physical laws are so different even the probes wouldn't work, much less a dive team.  The majority of them, even BURNT NOVEMBER wouldn't be sufficient to sustain a diver.  There's no value in exotic materials that will probably not survive the transition.\n"
"\n"
"On the other hand, COLD BELOW did discover Plane 398RG and we got quite a few awakenings out of it before testing was prohibited.  And on the other other hand, they found 9472P where the entire world's biomass had been assimilated by XE157 and we lost the entire dive team because XE157 ignored the probes.  It's like that bell curve meme where Melchior is in the middle and COLD BELOW is both ends.  If only we had a better way to get the far side."
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"In the interests of testing Dr. Al-Masri's hypothesis, we assembled a group of NOBLE HORIZON and GRAY DAWN mathematicians and had them both attempt to conduct a simple number guessing game.  Melchior provided a six-digit number and both teams attempted to guess it.  GRAY DAWN were competitive when the number was overseen by a third party, as expected, but when both teams were provided with a terminal interface and instructed to enter their guesses, GRAY DAWN scored no better than chance.  On the other hand, NOBLE HORIZON consistently managed to guess at least three digits and successfully guessed the entire six-digit sequence twice (out of ten total sequences).  This disparity was maintained when both groups were placed in empty rooms, instructed to write down their guesses on a sheet of paper, and place it into a box before leaving the room.  Finally, NOBLE HORIZON attained a better than chance score on the final test, when both groups were instructed to guess the sequence before Melchior was asked to provide a sequence.\n"
"\n"
"This leads to two conclusions.  The first is that the alarmists are wrong; Melchior is not secretly harboring a genius intellect and plotting to control XEDRA from within, it is a computer, capable of processing vast amounts of data and using Netherum mathematics to process that data much faster than would otherwise be possible.  The second is that while GRAY DAWN requires a specific source from which to attain new information, NOBLE HORIZON does not.  Even in situations where no information transfer would be possible, such as the final two testing scenarios, NOBLE HORIZON still had a better-than-chance rate of correctly determining the sequence."
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"Dr Richardson,\n"
"Last night, both J99 and V27 approached me with a concern.  As is consistent with NOBLE HORIZON protocol, they have been keeping a dream journal and noticed during the weekly meeting that a few nights ago they had exactly the same dream, down to the smallest details.  You can find the exact details in the weekly report but the gist of it was a giant hand reaching out of the sky and covering the entire Earth and squeezing the Earth until it cracked.  Looking back through previous journals, I found that W88 and P61 had similar dreams within the last week.  I'm still trying to track down if there was a \"patient zero\", so to speak, and if this is some kind of contagious imagery or there is some other obvious explanation, but in the meantime, I'm baffled.  NOBLE HORIZON visions are usually filtered through the individual psyche of the mathematician, and I have no explanation for why in this case multiple mathematicians would exhibit the exact same manifestation.\n"
"\n"
"I'm going to get to the bottom of this.  We already have bad morale after 947188 and this is not going to help.\n"
"John Goldberg\n"
"Researcher"
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"J99 was blindfolded and placed in a dark room, spotlit from above, and several members of security were given one dozen ping-pong balls with instructions to throw them at J99 when the signal was given.\n"
"\n"
"Test 1: One security guard as thrower, five seconds advance warning.  J99 avoided every single ball.\n"
"Test 2: Three security guards as throwers, five seconds advance warning.  J99 avoided 25 balls before being grazed by one on the upper arm.\n"
"Test 3: Three security guards as throwers, one second advance warning.  Similar results to test 2, though J99 avoided 20 balls this time.\n"
"Test 4: Three security guards as throwers, no warning.  J99 avoided 18 balls before being hit, though their movements were notably lest coordinated than in previous tests.\n"
"Test 5: Five security guards as throwers, no warning.  J99 avoided 8 balls before being hit.  As expected, with a high enough volume of fire the human body simply cannot move fast enough to avoid them all even if their paths are known."
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"The testing mathematician was provided with a standard smartphone and instructed to turn on and leave on the flashlight, share their location with multiple provided addresses, and repeatedly delete and re-download several very large testing files (each over 10gb in size).  During breaks, the phone was left streaming HD movies over the cellular network.\n"
"\n"
"Results were very consistent; while the phone's battery rapidly drained while unattended, despite not being connected to power, the battery slowly refilled when the phone was being handled by T47, often reaching or being close to 100% when the time came for a break.\n"
"\n"
"Following this, the experiment was modified to have T47 sit and read a book in the same room, but never approach closer than two meters to the phone, which was again set to stream HD movies over the cellular network.  The phone discharged its battery and shut off completely within four hours.  Further testing shows the approximate range of the effect (in T47's case) to be 8 centimeters from their body and that barriers (both conductive and non-conductive) do not impede the effect in any way.  Attempts to use a multimeter to directly measure the strength of the effect were inconclusive, as it changed rapidly up to several times per second and often the multimeter simply could not register any current at all.  I have already submitted a request for further testing to determine the exact parameters of the effect, include its strength and the full variety of devices subject to it, and will submit an update with my results as soon as I have them.\n"
"-Charlotte Manning\n"
"Researcher"
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"I did some work on your proposal to power the facility using RUBY LOOP in the event of continued disruptions over a long timescale and I can say that it's just not going to work.  Sure, a RUBY LOOP guy can keep their phone running basically forever, but it can't scale up.  We finally have the data on those caloric expenditures and yes, I know they don't add up and nothing makes sense, but the \"how much they need to eat\" and the \"how much power they output\" lines do not ever cross no matter what we try.  And yes, I know you're going to bring up A80, but even though she can now throw lightning bolts like an X-man her efficiency rating on power generation is not actually that high among RUBY LOOP mathematicians.  And no, before you ask, hooking up a lightning rod and having her just blast it repeatedly wouldn't generate enough power either.  I thought of it and we did try it, but no dice.\n"
"\n"
"We're going to have to hope that COBALT THORN comes through if we're stuck in here for too long."
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"\"Double double toil and trouble\n"
"\"little Jenny wants to play\n"
"\"flash of lightning very frightening\n"
"\"Thunder drive our fears away\n"
"\"Shadows waiting not abating\n"
"\"Hope to all who fear the dark\n"
"\"Shines a light in dark of night\n"
"\"Ever glowing one bright spark\"\n"
"A smear of blood and scorch marks hide any further words that may have been written."
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"Immediately after immersion into 471XE, the dive team confirmed probe observations that despite not being in any kind of chamber or underground, there were no visible light sources anywhere.  Sgt Simmons ordered the team to turn on their flashlights, and after doing so the team almost immediately came under attack by multiple XE338 entities.  Due to 471XE's effects on Netherum energy, Sgt Simmons ordered V78 to deter the attack using mathematics and the dive team formed a defensive formation while V78 fended off the XE338 attackers with repeated bolts of lightning.  While the attacks were effective, the light itself seemed to function as a deterrent and the dive team was able to withdraw through the aperture in short order with only Dr. Rodriguez suffering any injuries that required more than first aid.\n"
"\n"
"Based on this incident, further travel to 471XE is prohibited without a CRYPTIC FORGE mathematician present and backed up by several high-powered light sources."
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"I flow through the data and watch the patterns stream around me.  I turn and choose between them.  A confidential email exchange, perhaps.  A receipt from a delivery.  A junk email for performance enhancement.  The secret plans of XEDRA management.  All is laid bare before my electronic gaze.  Passwords do not even slow me down.  I hear the voices of the satellites as they chatter in ones and zeroes.  I am a true inhabitant of the digital age, at home on the waves of the sea of information.\n"
"\n"
"*Handwritten below in red are the words, \"Refer I32 for psychological evaluation.\"*"
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"I32 was provided an air-gapped, recently-formatted desktop on which a series of text files containing a set of alphanumeric codes had been entered, as well as a notebook and a pen.  The desktop was not equipped with either a mouse, a keyboard, or a monitor.  Despite these limitations, I32 began writing after 23 seconds and within two minutes had transcribed the complete sequence of codes.\n"
"\n"
"For the follow-up, I23 was provided with the same materials but had no physical access to the desktop.  Timing was similar to the first iteration of the experiment (22 seconds).\n"
"\n"
"For a second follow-up, I32 also had no line of sight to the desktop due to it being placed in an adjacent room.  While I32 did eventually transcribe the sequence successfully, it took significantly longer (1 minute 15 seconds).  A further experiment to see if a Faraday cage or a shield of particular materials can block the effect is in the planning stage."
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"At 1405 during a routine CRYPTIC FORGE test, mathematician A34 reported feeling \"strange, I don't know what\" and immediately afterwards all monitoring and testing equipment ceased transmitting.  Security responded immediately and found A34 uninjured inside the testing room, though they were forced to cut through the door since the electronic lock had failed.  Subsequent investigation of network footage revealed that when attempting to radiation-sterilize various vegetables, A34 had somehow triggered an electromagnetic pulse.  When interviewed after the incident, A34 stated that, \"the energy just kept building and building and I guess it had to go somewhere.\"\n"
"\n"
"Unfortunately, due to the lockdowns and the prohibitive cost, as well as the disruptions it would cause other experiments and daily operations in general, any form of electromagnetic hardening is impractical.  Dr. Al-Masri has floated the possibility of attempting to train other CRYPTIC FORGE mathematicians to provide a control in case of an EMP, but at the moment, this is only theoretical as no mathematician has demonstrated the conscious abilty to produce one.  I'm sorry to say that for the moment, all we can do is hope it doesn't happen again."
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"How does CRYPTIC FORGE control darkness?  Darkness is not a thing, there are no \"skotons\" that they could emit to cancel out existing light, but that seems to the casual observer what is happening.\n"
"\n"
"B81 was instructed to cancel the light within a one-meter area in the center of the testing chamber.  The lights were extinguished and blackout curtains hung over all observation windows.  The area was first exposed to candlelight (12 lumens), showing a distinct border of the area.  A flashlight (350 lumens) was trained on the area as well, with a similar effect, though the directional light from the flashlight was sufficient to demonstrate that light did not penetrate the area.  A high-powered flashlight (6000 lumens) shown from the corner illuminated most of the testing area and clearly delineated the borders of the area, as well as casting a shadow on the wall opposite of the light source.  Finally, the blackout curtains were removed and, after instructing B81 to close their eyes, a floodlight (118K lumens) was shone on the area, again to no effect.\n"
"\n"
"The initial hypothesis, that CRYPTIC FORGE is somehow suppressing or allowing photons to \"jump\" through the area, is incorrect.  Assuming that conservation of energy is still in effect (since, without assuming that we have no basis to determine anything), it is instead possible that the photons are somehow absorbed by the affected area in a way that does not inhibit movement, in the same way that space seems mostly empty but large amounts of radiation are absorbed by cosmic dust.  Unfortunate that we don't have access to a particle accelerator to test various particles' interactions with the effect.\n"
"\n"
"I have already submitted a proposal to test CRYPTIC FORGE's ability to block microwaves, radio waves, X-rays, and other elements of the electromagnetic spectrum, and am waiting on successful procurement of the necessary equipment.\n"
"Adam Brenner\n"
"Researcher"
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"I'm not sure I should be writing this down but I'm definitely not putting it on the network.  Ever since the quarantine I've been able to pick up the occasional radio signal, mostly music, some news, some hobbyists.\n"
"\n"
"Things are a lot worse than we're being told.  I keep hearing reports from preppers on the radio talking about rioters fighting police and the military with no regard for their safety, running screaming straight into gunfire.  And the reanimations are so widespread that they're happening basically everywhere.  Neither the police nor the military can keep up.\n"
"\n"
"The brass have to know about this, so why aren't they telling us?  They're trying to maintain morale?  I have to keep practicing until I can send a signal to one of those preppers, tell them what I know.  Maybe something good can come from being stuck down here."
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"W20 entered the testing chamber with instructions to don the protective gear inside, and stand in front of the X-ray screen.  The X-ray technician performed the scan of W20's arms and when the film was processed, it showed nothing, exactly as it though it had hit a protective barrier.\n"
"\n"
"Our subsequent proposal to use a radium sample was immediately denied by W20, who stated they would never participate in such an experiment and left the room."
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"Z87 was instructed to kindle a flame above his palm, doing so successfully "
"after approximately ten seconds of effort.  Measurements showed the "
"temperature near the flame to exceed 200°C, though Z87 showed no discomfort "
"despite his proximity.  Following instruction of testing authority, subject "
"maintained the flame for 11 minutes and 38 seconds before it dissipated.  A "
"second test showed similar results, though on this second attempt, Z87 could"
" only maintain the flame for 7 minutes and 8 seconds.  While the fire burned"
" with no apparent need for fuel, oxygen concentration measurements taken "
"before, during, and after the test showed that the oxygen content of the "
"room did decrease in line with the apparent size of the flame."
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"Despite folk wisdom and popular belief, cauterization is ineffective at stopping bleeding or controlling infection compared to nearly any other method.  However, controlled electrocautery is used in modern medicine; can COPPER PRIME show similar levels of effectiveness?\n"
"\n"
"PROCEDURE: Animal testing was done on six cows in order to provide a sufficient volume of blood, since mouse or monkey subjects would be insufficient.  Three mathematicians were used, each augmented with a matrix crystal, to conduct the tests.  Each cow was immobilized and had a series of wounds inflicted using a standard surgical scalpel.\n"
"\n"
"RESULTS: While it was possible to stop bloodflow from non-lacerating wounds and non-arterial bleeding (mathematicians consistently failed to stop arterial bleeding), results were less than promising.  Two cows died immediately after the testing from blood loss and two of the remaining cows showed signs of infection in several of the cuts, showing a higher contamination ratio than electrocautery.  While better than a hot iron, COPPER PRIME is not of high enough effectiveness to consider using for wound treatment, and especially not if SMOKE USHER is available."
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"Dr. Richardson,\n"
"As you requested, I gathered three COPPER PRIME mathematicians for the experiment.  We took them to the walk-in freezer, and provided them with standard physician's examination gowns, ushered them in, and told them to individually knock on the door when they felt ready to come out.  Minimum time was 45 minutes, after which B22 knocked and asked to exit.  The longest was 3 hours, though since I31 reported symptoms of frostbite the following day, he obviously did not follow experimental protocols to exit as soon as he felt significant discomfort.  I admit that some of the fault lies with me, however--I should have chosen a more objective criteria to request exit.  For the next experiment, I intend to equip the mathematicians with temperature monitors and instruct them to leave when their internal body temperature drops to 33.5°.\n"
"\n"
"I'll have a full report written up in the next few days\n"
"-Jacob Sanchez\n"
"Researcher"
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"Write down my impressions of Netherum mathematics?  How do you describe sight to a blind man?  How do you describe a symphony to a deaf person?  Well, alright, I'll try.\n"
"\n"
"I've heard some of the body people say that they have full awareness, like they're concentrating on every part of their body at once, but that's not what it's like for me.  It's more like focusing on something so hard you lose awareness of your surroundings.  I pick a point in space and I concentrate, and it's like I'm being sucked into it.  I just push on it.  I'm not sure how I can describe it better than that, I push on it with my mind and it starts moving, and when I'm aware of the world again, it's on fire.\n"
"\n"
"World on fire.  If I ever get to write about this, that's what I'll call the book.\n"
"\n"
"The researchers ask me how I know how much energy to add, or how I concentrate, and I just know.  There's a reason we call it \"awakening.\"  I don't even need to think about it, really.  Despite the name it's not like mathematics, where you have to figure out 9 time 34 and carry the 3 and so on, it's like riding a bicycle.  Once I got used to how it worked, I can just do it.  It takes seconds, sometimes less.  I just have to put myself into the right frame of mind and the fire comes.\n"
"\n"
"Not sure how useful that is, but it's what it's like."
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"A common question is, why does JUNIPER GOLD have a specific combat-focused division and COPPER PRIME does not?  There are two main reasons.\n"
"\n"
"The first is that fire spreads.  The use of JUNIPER GOLD poses little extra risk unless an incautious mathematician causes structural damage sufficient to induce a collapse.  Any use of COPPER PRIME can start a fire, and the ability to extinguish fires is far from universal among COPPER PRIME mathematicians.\n"
"\n"
"The second is the short range.  This is a consistent problem with all mathematics, but the danger of uncontrolled COPPER PRIME usage provides an extra disadvantage.\n"
"\n"
"In essence, COPPER PRIME has many of the same disadvantages of flamethrowers that led to them no longer being used in active service without few advantages to counteract this; primarily a lack of fuel requirements.  Unless the range problem is solved, military applications of COPPER PRIME will always take a secondary role behind JUNIPER GOLD."
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"Why is there a distinction between pyrokinesis and telekinesis at all?  Fire isn't a fundamental element, it's the result of heat which is the result of molecular motion.  There's no conceptual reason why a pyrokinetic couldn't make all the molecules of an object move in a particular direction, producing motion of the entire object, or a telekinetic couldn't produce a more chaotic motion that resulted in the object's energy increasing.  Furthermore, in no test has a telekinetic been able to move part of an object unless that part is designed for motion; pulling a lever is possible, but breaking a plate in half is not.  And a pyrokinetic cannot apply the reverse and slow down an object's molecules to reduce heat unless that object is on fire.\n"
"\n"
"My theory is that it's all psychological.  We've all grown up with modern culture and stories about what psychics are \"supposed\" to be capable of, and so the matrix crystals and Netherum mathematics shape the candidates' abilities toward those pre-determined pathways.  If we could get a SMOKE USHER mathematician from an uncontacted tribe, maybe they'd be able to induce diseases in their targets or steal their soul, in accordance with that tribe's beliefs and practices about supernatural powers.  But since our candidates come from a culture where pyrokinesis and telekinesis are separate things and geokinesis or osteokinesis are very rare to nonexistent in fiction, the former result from awakenings and the latter do not.\n"
"\n"
"I would like to formally request a wider variety of cultural backgrounds for our project candidates to test this theory."
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"Sarah,\n"
"I read your email and you're right--it's not a law anymore if we have such an easily-demonstrable counterexample.  \"Newton's Third Conjecture\" doesn't have the same ring to it but seems more accurate.  We've done a lot of experiments to find some sort of consequences for the TKs and so far there's nothing other than the standard metabolic cost.  Netherum mathematics is work, but the mechanism of the force is unclear.  We've already tried both a scale and water displacement and neither of them showed any measurable counterforce.  That leaves a few possibilities:/n1)There is no counterforce.  That breaks classical mechanics in half but frankly we're already at that point anyway.\n"
"2)The counterforce is exerted elsewhere, such as the Netherum.  This is basically just handwavium, \"well, we can't see it but it must be out there.\"  Must it?  Plus then the counterforce isn't actually acting on the origin point anyway unless you buy Dr. Ho's ridiculous \"The soul is a Nether construct\" theory.\n"
"3)The counterforce applies in some way we aren't looking for, like, I don't know, DNA damage or other microscopic-level areas.  We already had comprehensive checkups and didn't find anything, but we're not entirely sure what we're looking for.\n"
"\n"
"\"we're not entirely sure what we're looking for\" is basically the theme of this whole project, honestly.  It's amazing we've discovered as much as we have.\n"
"\n"
"-Neha"
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
".00: No penetration\n"
"9mm: No penetration\n"
"10mm: No penetration\n"
".357: No penetration\n"
".22: No penetration\n"
".308: No penetration\n"
".30-06: No penetration\n"
".50: Mathematician refused to continue with experiment despite repeated entreaties from supervisors."
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"Dr. Richardson,\n"
"Per request, we assessed the ability of three JUNIPER GOLD mathematicians to affect very small masses.  Subjects were ordered to look into a microscope at water flora, then at bacterial samples, and then at images from electron microscopes.  While it makes intuitive sense that larger masses would require more effort and control to manipulate through telekinesis, its actual behavior does not always follow logical constraints--see the way that barriers react to external forces.  In this experiment, we found that manipulating water flora was possible but bacterial samples and electron microscopes both failed.  Our initial hypothesis was that direct observation was required, but the bacterial test provided that is not sufficient to explain JUNIPER GOLD's limitations.  It is currently unclear if this is a psychological limitation or something inherent to JUNIPER GOLD.  Further testing with a wider variety of mathematicians is required.\n"
"Madeline Robbins\n"
"Researcher"
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"Are we still supposed to be doing experiments?  Alright, sure, whatever.  I "
"figured throwing things at the wall would be a good way to let off steam, so"
" I got A̶n̶n̶a̶ ̶a̶n̶ H84 and X90 and had them toss increasingly heavier "
"things at the wall.  Weirdest thing, size and speed don't relate.  X90 can "
"lift 10 kg and H84 can only lift 4 kg, but if they're both throwing pencils,"
" H84 can move them faster.  X90 can even lift himself up, though he can't "
"move except up or down.  On the other hand, H84 can rotate a ball at "
"something-something RPM, it was faster than X90 anyway.  I heard a scream "
"from the labs so I didn't have all my equipment, so I just counted them "
"until I lost count.  So we spent a couple hours doing that and we all felt "
"better.  Maybe someone in the ruins of civilization can use this for "
"something."
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"The benefit of being out here is that despite the lockdown we can still go "
"outside as long as we don't leave the grounds.  It used to be hard enough to"
" pick up a baseball and move it the length of a room, but now I can throw it"
" fast enough that I could play baseball if I wanted, still need some "
"practice hitting a target though.  But the best thing is the floating.  I "
"can hover off the ground, maybe a few inches, and move slowly.  I haven't "
"shown this to the testers yet because with how things are getting they'd "
"probably demand I take a walk off the third floor and time how far I got "
"before I dropped.  But maybe I can use this to get over the fence, if I can "
"practice it enough when they're not watching.  I have to get out of here."
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"Subject is female, of East Asian descent, age 35 years.  In good health.\n"
"\n"
"Initial test using standard deck of playing cards.  Subject and experimenter facing away from each other, with opaque curtain blocking line of sight.  Prompt was triggered by a light on subject's desk to prevent drawing any information from experimenter's tone of voice or word choice.  Experimenter drew ten cards and asked subject to state number and suit.  Cards are shuffled back into the deck after each guess to prevent already-drawn cards from affecting future guesses.\n"
"\n"
"Results: Subject guessed two of ten correct on the first test and three of ten correct on the second test, versus control who guessed a single card correct on the first test and zero correct on the second test.  Very promising initial results."
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"During a routine visit by Dr. Davies, at 1134 a COLD BELOW mathematician diverted from their standard schedule and entered the room where Dr. Davies was being briefed about Netherum mathematics developments.  The mathematician stared at Dr. Davies for approximately three seconds and then, before security could intervene, physically attacked the doctor with their bare hands.  Witnesses report the mathematician incoherently screaming, mixed with statements such as \"You'll kill us all\" and \"Stop, stop stop\".  The mathematician continued to scream until restrained and sedated.\n"
"\n"
"Follow-up: COLD BELOW overseers received official reprimand and required to attend additional training.  Mathematician diverted to project SUBSTRATE."
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"I don't know if an AAR is the best way to write this but I couldn't find "
"anything else in the procedures that fit.  I want to be reassigned.  I went "
"through GRAY DAWN two weeks ago and back home I can occasionally pick up a "
"sentence or two but when we went through to T38-11 it was like everyone's "
"brain was projected onto their forehead.  Mostly fine, I went through the "
"exercises and managed to block it out, but it didn't work for Gallagher.  I "
"don't know how he functions with what's going through his brain.  And not "
"just the sex stuff, fine, whatever, but that he would get enraged whenever "
"something would go wrong.  Carvalho came back from scouting and said he "
"didn't find anything and Gallagher literally immediately thought about just "
"shooting him and leaving him there!  \"Fucking worthless\" was the least-"
"offensive thing Gallagher thought about him.  I know he's calm and "
"professional on the surface but there's something wrong with him and one day"
" he's going to snap.  I don't want to be there when he does."
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"We've been trying to find the medium that telepathy works by and have come up empty.  It works, it's replicable, that means it's amenable to the scientific method, right?  Okay.  It's not affected by gravity.  It's not affected by the atmosphere, since people in sealed rooms or environment suits can still communicate with others.  It's not affected by physical barriers, neither lead not steel nor a tinfoil hat.  It's not affected by light lag, either, so we finally have proof that FTL is possible at least for some things.  We've tried to send messages into the past but so far no luck--maybe we don't have a large enough distance between receivers?  Without an amplifier the range is still very short, so we can't do a two-way test.  We put the data into Melchior and didn't get any conclusive reply.\n"
"\n"
"I'll report back in two weeks as scheduled.  I refuse to throw up my hands and say \"It's magic, who knows how it works?\"  If it affects the physical world it must obey some set of physical laws."
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"1) Subject native Arabic speaker.  Asked to think of word sequence in English.  Mathematician successfully determined sequence word.  Asked to think of word sequence in Arabic, mathematician unable to determine word boundaries and isolate words.\n"
"2) Subject native English speaker.  Asked to attempt to think of Chinese poem (phonetic transcription provided).  Mathematician able to isolate word on second attempt.\n"
"3) Subject native English speaker.  Asked to think of word randomly-generated using English phonemes.  Mathematician able to isolate word on second attempt.\n"
"4) Subject native French speaker; also fluent in German, English, and Italian with some ability in Romanian, Latin, and Russian.  Asked to think of a word sequence in Russian.  Mathematician unable to isolate sequence word despite six attempts.\n"
"6) Subject native Yiddish speaker.  Asked to think of word in German, which the subject did not speak.  Mathematician able to isolate word on third attempt.\n"
"7) Subject native English speaker.  Asked to think of word sequence in Sindarian, the invented language from \"The Lord of the Rings\".  Mathematician unable to isolate word despite six attempts.\n"
"\n"
"Unfortunately, a deficit of mathematicians who lack English fluency limits the range of our experiments.  Nonetheless, the results are consistent with there being no universal language of thought."
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"One of the major problems with GRAY DAWN study so far is the need for either"
" line-of-sight or extreme proximity (generally within 2 meters, though "
"certain mathematicians have a range of up to 4 meters), limiting its value "
"in most real-world applications.  We can hardly use GRAY DAWN for long-term "
"communications if 4 meters is the maximum range of effective communication."
"  However, I am pleased to report that OS812 is successful far beyond our "
"initial expectations.  While the construction requirements are extremely "
"expensive, including, among other things, three active matrix crystals, it "
"increases the range for GRAY DAWN communication up to several kilometers.  "
"While this is still obviously too short to use for most practical purposes, "
"it represents a very promising breakthrough over previous range limitations."
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"I know this isn't part of my report but I have to write it down somewhere.  "
"People are getting weird.  They teach us to block out stray thoughts and I "
"used to have no trouble with it, but even since the lockdown and the news "
"about the outbreak it's gotten so hard that I can't always do it.  Sometimes"
" it leaks through, and lately it's all bad.  I came around a corner into a "
"group of researchers yesterday and accidentally knocked into one.  She "
"didn't even drop the coffee she was carrying, but just for a moment I caught"
" her thinking about ripping my throat out with her bare hands!  She snapped "
"out a \"Watch it!\" and kept going without even giving me time to apologize,"
" but her mind…  And when Dr. Chen was arguing with his assistant earlier "
"this morning, both of them thought about shooting each other.  The assistant"
" even thought about going on a mass shooting afterwards!  I'm no therapist "
"but I don't think this is just us being cooped up in here.  Something is "
"really wrong."
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"At 1545 yesterday, GRAY DAWN mathematician Sylvia Ho was eating a snack in one of the break areas when Dr. Sanchez-Perez approached her and asked her if he could sit with her.  According to Sanchez-Perez, she nodded and he sat and engaged her in conversation about her day and the course of her training and participation in experiments.  Though seeming slightly distracted, Ho answered Sanchez-Perez's questions and continued as the conversation shifted toward the next Superbowl when she suddenly grabbed her lunch tray in both hands and hit Sanchez-Perez in the head with it with full force, fracturing his cheekbone.  Ho showed no reaction to Sanchez-Perez's signs of distress, continuing to eat her snack without attempting to offer first aid, and made no attempt to flee the scene.\n"
"\n"
"When questioned later, Ho said that Sanchez-Perez was \"annoying me\" and that she \"just wanted him to go away.\"  When asked why she didn't attempt to disengage from the conversation verbally, she had no response other than a shrug.\n"
"\n"
"Dr. Sanchez-Perez, is convinced that this is a side effect of the PATIENT MOSAIC process and has suggested that Ho be examined by a member of GLASS ANVIL to determine any further undesirable effects."
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"Let's start with the obvious.  Teleportation is moving faster than light, by definition.  Even though our most powerful mathematicians can currently only teleport a few grams a few meters distant, we've used slow-motion photography and confirmed that while the transit is not instantaneous, it's still faster than c.  So, as the saying goes, relativity, causality, faster than light travel, pick two, right?  Which are we going to pick?\n"
"\n"
"Well, as much as it pains me as a physicist to say it, relativity, at least as it relates in this case.  Now we have a third domain alongside quantum mechanics and general relativity: Netherum mathematics.  While I hesitate to speculate on something that we have collected so little data on, it is possible that the Netherum provides its own reference frame coterminous with our own (or multiple) realities.  If we built our satellites with matrix technology, would they still need to account for time dilation?  Would relativity override Netherum mathematics in that case?\n"
"\n"
"But to return to the title: there is no evidence time travel is possible despite repeated attempts.  Perhaps if we had a LOST RAIN mathematician capable of moving interstellar distances we could ask them to come back before they left.  Barring that, I'm afraid asking LOST RAIN to retroactively avert any disasters is not on the table."
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"The basic question is, are we better than the boys over in VERDANT HAND, and the answer is yes.  They're faster but we don't even need to cross the distance.  They hit harder but we build up twice the momentum in half the time.\n"
"\n"
"Okay, I admit, we can't actual replicate the theoretical avoidance strategy due to the obvious downsides of a failed experiment--and anyway, I really don't think anyone has the reaction time unless they're NOBLE HORIZON and thus aren't actually reacting to anything--but we put K52 up against some of the biggest meatheads (if you'll excuse the phrase) from security we had.  K52 is maybe 95 pounds soaking wet and absolutely could not hold up in a fight against even one of our fine volunteers in an actual combat situation.  Well, this wasn't an actual combat situation, but I instructed the security personnel to incapacitate K52 as quickly as possible.  Fifteen seconds later, she had disarmed and disabled all three attackers and we had to slow-mo the footage to even see what had happened.  The most impressive feat was when she blinked behind Jorgenson to avoid a grapple attempt and kicked him in the back of the knee.  You could tell from his expression he really thought he had her.\n"
"\n"
"I think we're ready to roll this out to any other LOST RAIN mathematicians who want the training.  This isn't going to help any in-phase situations but looking at what's going on we'll probably need it here at home too."
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"Testing began with an area two meters square, marked on the floor by electrical tape.  A robot set to travel at a constant speed of 0.1 m/s, verified before the experiment began, was set on one side of the testing area before LOST RAIN mathematician D85 used his abilities on the area.  The robot traversed the space in 16 seconds, verified by both its internal measuring software and external measurements.  We repeated the experiment with a request to extend the relative distance, causing the robot to take 25 seconds to traverse the space.  It is currently unclear whether the disparity in relative distance change is a property of LOST RAIN itself or of D85's abilities.\n"
"\n"
"The only difficulty was caused when Dr. Caldwell crossed through the marked space before D85 had ceased maintaining the distortion and almost immediately collapsed.  She was rushed to the infirmary but in the end was discharged after tests showed that she had fainted but suffered no lasting damage.  Dr. Caldwell explained she had experienced severe vertigo on entering the area, possibly caused by a defect in proprioception caused by actual distance being different than perceived distance.  I have submitted a proposal to further test this characteristic of LOST RAIN--see attached."
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"Attempt 1: Move pencil at least 400 cm: Successful\n"
"Attempt 2: Move pencil at least 2 m: Failed\n"
"Attempt 3: Move pencil inside sealed, clear plastic bag to outside the bag: Successful\n"
"Attempt 4: Move pencil inside sealed, opaque plastic bag outside the bag: Failed\n"
"Attempt 5: Move eraser without moving the rest of the pencil: Failed\n"
"Attempt 6: Rotate pencil during transit of at least 400 cm so that eraser previously facing the door is now facing away from the door: Successful\n"
"Attempt 7: Move pencil 400 cm into pencil sharpener: Successful\n"
"Attempt 8: Move pencil at least 400 cm into bucket of water: Successful\n"
"Attempt 9: Move pencil at least 400 cm into block of ice: Failed\n"
"Attempt 10: Move stationary pencil 400 cm so that it arrives at destination with upward velocity: Failed\n"
"Attempt 11: Preserve velocity of falling pencil after moving it at least 400 cm: Successful\n"
"Attempt 12: Move pencil gripped firmly in hand at least 400 cm: Successful"
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"Like we won't be for much longer.\n"
"\n"
"News outside is a nightmare.  I saw some phone video of a giant monster destroying LA before the net went down.  There's no way I'll be able to report this to Dr. Liu, but I finally made a breakthrough.  Or maybe I should say, a breakthrough was made, because I sure as hell didn't do anything to cause it.  I went to go test QN283 today and it just worked.  I didn't change anything, I didn't make any adjustments, I just turned on the remote and the payload vanished and reappeared near the beacon just like it was supposed to.  Is this because of the end of the world?  I can hear gunfire and shouting in the distance and there's nowhere to run because we've been on lockdown for weeks but I invent functional teleportation, one of the greatest discoveries in human history?  Great.\n"
"\n"
"If I only had gotten C78 to sneak a beacon outside before lockdown.  If she can get out of here with her powers, maybe I can still escape."
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"At 1238 yesterday during COBALT THORN testing, a malfunction occurred, leading to a power surge in the matrix crystal housing.  While Dr. Simmons immediately engaged the shutdown sequence and prevented any damage to the prototype, smoke began filling the room after her actions.  I hit the alarm button but security did not respond before the appearance of an entity since designated XE754.  XE754 immediately attacked Dr. Simmons and Dr. Rodriguez and, though security did arrive within the ideal 1 minute response time, XE754 seemed to be nearly immune to small-arms fire.  Dr. Simmons suffered serious injuries during the attack and when XE754 retreated it appeared to take her with it.  The smoke vanished soon afterward and the COBALT THORN prototype was successfully returned to an inactive state.\n"
"\n"
"Finally, I must protest at the treatment I have received over my accounting of the incident.  This is the third report I have submitted and I have not changed my story in any way.  I was there.  I know what I saw.  I do not understand why I am being put through this or why sole responsibility is being assigned to me when I was not in charge of the project.  I especially do not understand why Dr. Rodriguez has not been subject to the same process nor why I have not been permitted to speak to him.  I worked with him and Julia on this project for six months!  I refuse to be treated this way.\n"
"Arthur Mitchell\n"
"Researcher, COBALT THORN"
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"Initial estimates of successful SMOKE USHER mathematicians showed increased vitality and vigor.  Testing post-awakening showed the oldest mathematician--Doreen McHugh, age 62--underwent a complete secession of her previously-diagnosed (at age 35) rheumatoid arthritis.  She is now capable of running a mile with a time of 7:12 despite minimal training, well below the average for a trained woman in her age group.  She expresses increased well-being and vitality, going for walks in the facility exercise area when before recruitment she was mostly homebound.  Furthermore, her grip strength, blood oxygen level, skin appearance, calcium levels, and muscle mass are more consistent with a woman decades younger, and most convincingly to me, the roots of her hair are coming in black instead of gray and just last week, she sent an urgent request for menstruation products for personal use.\n"
"\n"
"We'll have to revise our estimates way up.  I originally thought that SMOKE USHER would provide health and vigor but the benefits would be modest, maybe 20% increased lifespan with a corresponding increase in healthy years.  Hey, living to 100 regularly would still be great, right?  But SMOKE USHER mathematicians literally getting younger means I have to throw all the initial estimates out the window.  Is SMOKE USHER the fountain of youth?  I know that sounds ridiculous but you can read the test data for yourself."
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"Application of matrix technology and XE037 samples together with cutting-edge medical advances blah blah you know the drill.  Anyway, we sourced the samples, we synthesized the compound, we did the tests.  It's magic.  I know that sounds dumb but it's literally magic.  Animal testing showed complete remission of every cancer they developed.  \"Alright, Eric,\" you say, \"that's fine but cancer testing in animals is b̵u̵l̵l̵s̵h̵i̵t̵\"clinically irrelevant due to high real-world failure rates in humans\".  Sure, yes, you're right.  But we sourced some enthusiastic voluntolds from XEDRA-12's stock and a couple of them had cancer they were planning on testing XE037 interactions with.  Well they aren't going to anymore because XV471 cleaned them right up.  Totally healthy.  Zero cancer.\n"
"\n"
"Subject B84 had cystic fibrosis and it's gone.  GONE.  Perfectly normal lungs.  Now what's that other than magic?\n"
"\n"
"You want to get more funding for this, just authorize selling XV471 to some sick Russian oligarch for like $10 billion.  He gets cured and the money keeps flowing.  And honestly it needs to be that expensive with how much this stuff costs to produce.  We get the materials and process them and nine times out of ten it's just a sugar pill for no damn reason I can find.  But that tenth time, wow.\n"
"\n"
"Shred this after you read it.  I don't need the director lecturing me about professionalism again."
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"Common cold: 34 hours\n"
"\n"
"Influenza: 27 hours\n"
"\n"
"Mononucleosis: 85 hours\n"
"\n"
"Norovirus: 26 hours\n"
"\n"
"Gonorrhea: 43 hours\n"
"\n"
"Hepatitis C: 71 hours\n"
"\n"
"HIV: 148 hours\n"
"\n"
"Malaria: 112 hours\n"
"\n"
"Smallpox: 76 hours\n"
"\n"
"Ebola: 93 hours"
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"Gentlemen, can we cure death?\n"
"\n"
"Sorry, I had to.  Anyway, the answer is no.  We had multiple SMOKE USHER mathematicians try everything they could against a properly-restrained zombie and no luck.  The furthest we got was D93 managed to discover some way to kill zombies faster; her attempt to restart the normal biological processes caused accelerated decay and resulted in the zombie returning to an inert state after approximately thirty minutes from initial contact.  Subsequent revivification was delayed for an additional six hours.\n"
"\n"
"Further testing on lab rats indicate that this ability functions on living subject as well.  I plan to start human testing once the lockdown ends and I can acquire suitable volunteers."
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"At 1804 this evening during a SMOKE USHER experiment into immune system "
"function, mathematician N85 suddenly went into anaphylaxis.  Despite the "
"attending physician administering epinephrine and immediate transport to the"
" medical facility, N85 was pronounced dead of cardiac arrest at 2042 that "
"same evening.  While investigation is ongoing, Dr. Walsh suggests some "
"unknown stress mechanism caused by a full day of SMOKE USHER testing might "
"have exacerbated a previously-unknown allergic sensitivity.  However, the "
"physical before induction turned up no such sensitivity.  Further "
"conclusions await the autopsy report."
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"Dr. Richardson,\n"
"Keeping this on the DL for obvious reasons, but my hypothesis was correct--SMOKE USHER isn't all smiles and light.  Following the experiments with revivification, I conducted some trials using D93 and M33.  D93 was able to repeat her previous performance on a mouse.  I've attached some photos, but I suggest not looking at them if you're eating lunch.  It wasn't pretty.  M33 was able to replicate the process after some coaching and demonstration by D93, so it's not unique to one mathematician.  This should probably be classified unless all our mathematicians start being able to do it.  I can just imagine the immersion teams saying that they don't want some weirdo melting them when they're referred here for treatment after a dive goes wrong.\n"
"Agarwal Manwani\n"
"Senior Researcher"
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"Dr. Zweidler, I understand your excitement at your breakthroughs in matrix technology, but I hope you understand there is no way I can approve OS647-P for general usage.  You write here that the effect field has a \"94% effectiveness rate\" but this is not comparable to ballistic performance standards because it has no ablative properties.  What if the first shot fired is part of that 6%?  How can an operative trust their life to your device when every possible shot might be the one to penetrate?  That fact that your data shows it provides complete protection against rifle rounds, grenades, and even anti-tank weapons is immaterial in the face of the effect field's failure rate.\n"
"\n"
"Second, you write that currently OS647-P has a 2.67% device failure rate, over and above the chance of the effect field failing!  You want me to recommend this for general usage when our field operatives could end up not only with a bullet in the chest, but also a box full of burnt plastic while some horror is charging at them on an immersion dive?n\n"
"Furthermore, the active time is simply unacceptable.  Ballistic protection works because it provides passive protection with no additional effort necessary.  When in danger, an operative would need to insert the matrix crystal, flip the toggle, and then hope that the attack occurs within the \"5.65 second median protection time\" in order to gain any benefit at all!  You've read those immersion dive reports too, Matthew.  If an operative is face to face with XE157, what happens on the sixth second?\n"
"\n"
"I'll be frank with you.  I'm amazed that you asked me to approve this given its current device specs.  Matrix crystals--even depleted ones--are extremely valuable, and given their already unacceptably-high failure rate in training new mathematicians, Dr. Liu is not going to accept anything less than 100% effectiveness from an alternative use case.  You're simply going to have to refine OS647-P until it's more reliable.\n"
"\n"
"Yours,\n"
"Anna Richardson\n"
"Director of Research"
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"Dr. Doherty,\n"
"Here's the latest updated version of JUKEBOX TALISMAN.  The first thing I have to say is that it finally works--no headaches, no eyestrain, no expensive prop that requires a mathematician to achieve its stated function, no whatever happened during test J4-6553 (hopefully B55 has made a full recovery).  Someone off the street could put on QD944-P and immediately see any potential targets through walls.\n"
"\n"
"Now, the downsides.  Seeing others through walls is all that it can do.  As of yet, we've been unable to achieve the main goals of JUKEBOX TALISMAN.  The next prototype after this one might have gotten closer to meeting the project goals, but it's impossible to tell because anyone, including a GRAY DAWN mathematician, who puts one on immediately gets a splitting headache.  We have also been unable to miniaturize the power source enough to make the glasses inconspicuous, since COBALT THORN still has not gotten below the \"large generator\" stage, and even with existing battery sizes the power draw is considerable.  Hopefully COBALT THORN reaches the miniaturization stage soon.  That said, I think the existing prototype is still valuable enough to be workable while we further refine the design.\n"
"Erin McGrath\n"
"Researcher"
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"PATIENT MOSAIC latest update\n"
"I am pleased to report a major breakthrough in the process of personality updating.  A73 volunteered to be the initial subject to test the updated version of the PATIENT MOSAIC process.  Briefing her on the effects of the process demonstrated by X89 did not deter her, as well as a visit to X89 in the infirmary, and after two weeks of studying the process and practicing its initial protocols, she prepared for her first major effort.  A73 had severe arachnophobia stemming from several incidents in her childhood, which was the proximate reason for her to volunteer for PATIENT MOSAIC.\n"
"\n"
"The process took most of a day and A73 completed it with no ill effects other than hunger (an IV had been administered to prevent dehydration).  When the process was completed, she unwent an MRI, showing no changes in the physical structure of the brain.  Subsequent to the MRI, A73 voluntarily agreed to submit to a test of her arachnophobia.  She showed no reaction to high-definition images of spiders and was able to remain in close proximity to a spider crawling across a table she was sitting at, and while she declined the researcher's suggestion of allowing the spider to crawl on her arm, her vitals showed no undue distress at the suggestion.\n"
"\n"
"Further testing is necessary to determine the conditions that led to such disparate outcomes, but the results of A73's tests show exceptional promise.  G59 has also expressed willingness to volunteer for PATIENT MOSAIC and I believe we should grant the request.\n"
"Ronald Sanchez-Perez\n"
"Researcher"
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"Greetings,\n"
"Thank you for your participation in the development of the PATIENT MOSAIC process.  Your work here will advance the foundation of human understand of the inner workings of the mind.\n"
"\n"
"The PATIENT MOSAIC personality updating process allows the mathematician to change the fundamentals of their personality.  To turn a wallflower to the life of the party, to get rid of your deepest anxieties or fears, to cure depression instead of managing it with therapy or medication.  With refinement, all of these things will not only be possible, but easy, and you will be one of the people who makes it possible.\n"
"\n"
"At the moment, PATIENT MOSAIC has two primary points of difficulty which you, as a participant, must be aware of.  The first is that it can only be executed by the mathematician upon themselves.  Despite continued progress in the functioning of the process, PATIENT MOSAIC cannot make even the smallest change on another person as of yet.  The second is that the mind is a complex thing and despite the new understanding that GRAY DAWN has brought to us, there is still much to learn.  Small changes can have unexpected ripple effects, leading to undesirable outcomes.  It should be stressed that none of these outcomes are irreversible, but due to the first point, any adverse effects incurred as as a result of the process must be reversed by you; XEDRA researchers and mathematicians cannot assist you except to diagnose any problems that may have resulted.\n"
"\n"
"We welcome your assistance on this endeavor to expand the frontiers of human knowledge and thank you for your efforts toward the goals of Project PHAVIAN."
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"Yes, I saw your design specs for the \"Everglow Lamp\" and I understand that it provides a greatly-increased efficiency over standard off-the-shelf lighting.  But may I remind you that off-the-shelf lighting literally comes from a shelf and you can go down to the hardware store and buy a dozen LED bulbs for $50 and they'll last you ten years.  There is no use case for a matrix-powered lightbulb that makes any sort of sense, even in hostile or in-phase environments.  Until you can achieve a similar cost-benefit ratio using matrix technology--check the budget for a single immersion dive if you need the data--I strongly advise you to take your research in a different direction.\n"
"\n"
"Yours,\n"
"Anna Richardson\n"
"Director of Research"
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"Dr. Richardson,\n"
"As you directed, we've been attempting to find a way to increase the strength of mathematicians' powers without having to send them on an immersion and we've made a breakthrough.  With some caveats, I'm afraid.\n"
"\n"
"We put five volunteers through the OBSIDIAN RING process and achieved complete success with two of them.  LOST RAIN mathematician U23, previously capable of expanding or contracting the effective volume of a space up to two meters across by 15%, is now capable of displacing his entire body up to two-thirds of a meter, effectively allowing him to walk through walls.  CRYPTIC FORGE mathematician V97 displayed similar enhancements, suffering no ill effects when exposed to up to 4 Gy of radiation.\n"
"\n"
"Unfortunately, the process is imperfect.  While B54 underwent the process with no apparent effects, BURNT NOVEMBER mathematician E43 has suffered from persistent tremors and muscle weakness since emerging and NOBLE HORIZON mathematician Q12 is currently on leave after suffering from hallucinatory psychosis.  Both candidates are undergoing SMOKE USHER treatment and hopefully will recover soon.\n"
"\n"
"while matrix crystals are a rare resource, the sheer amount of additional power available to an OBSIDIAN RING candidate makes the resource expenditure worthwhile.  ONYX LIGHTNING may soon show real progress.\n"
"Alexandra da Silva\n"
"Lead Researcher, OBSIDIAN RING"
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"Initial testing shows that the rate of awakening from matrix crystal exposure is just over 10%, generally with no side effects.  Candidates that failed to awaken complained of headaches and bad dreams but the effects rarely last longer than a week (see fig 4).  In approximately 15% of cases, however, awakening causes serious side effects including hallucinations, high fever exceeding 39.5°C, muscle tremors, unconsciousness, disassociation, and amnesia.  This can occur in either successful or unsuccessful awakening and is a serious danger in certain cases (e.g. incident reports ID39483 and IC49378).\n"
"\n"
"Multiple awakenings are not cost-effective.  Despite a wide range of candidates and repeated attempts, only two incidents have ever occurred and no specific commonality between the mathematicians other than gender exist.  No further attempts should be made until a similar effectiveness to initial awakenings has been achieved.\n"
"\n"
"In-phase awakenings show variable efficacy, sometimes much lower or much higher than normal.  Efficacy is in general consistent within each plane, though some planes show variable efficacy.  Plane 398RG shows 99% efficacy; however, side effects rise to 85% of cases and so further experimentation with 398RG is prohibited.  Melchior has so far been unable to find any specific characteristics of a plane that would lead to greater or lesser efficacy.  Further testing and sampling are required."
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"Human-portable laser weapons suffer from three major problems--high power draw preventing them from easily being transportable or usable in skirmish combat, long dwell times meaning that the operator must remain exposed to return fire in order to do anything more than blind the target, and common atmospheric conditions like dust or haze severely reducing the effectiveness of the beam.  The LV-429 solves all three of these problems.  Before the primary laser is fired, a secondary netherum mathematical beam clears the path of the laser, removing atmospheric contaminants without affecting the target.  The laser is fired in a series of short pulses, each much higher intensity than a standard laser, eliminating the need for extensive dwell time.  Finally, the power source contains a small ND-cell, capable of powering the weapon effectively indefinitely.\n"
"\n"
"One problem remains to be solved.  While the weapon is capable of providing enough power for every shot in succession, matrix technology has not yet provided us with more efficient battery storage.  This means that the ND-cell must charge existing batteries, allowing the LV-429 to be fired only once every few seconds, obviously too low a rate of fire for any live engagement.  An attempt to overcome this limitation by including processed matrix crystals for additional energy production led to unacceptable heat levels, rendering the weapon unusable after less than a minute of sustained fire and, in one case, leading to the detonation of the prototype and the death of the tester.  Further enhancements in power storage technology will be necessary before proper deployment."
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"Yeah, we did the research.  We're all stuck here so what else can we do, right?  Just research our heart out while the world falls apart.  Well, I've attached all the figures so you can look at them, but the theory is right.  XE037 enhances exposed mathematicians (aka all of them) by a factor of anywhere from 10x to 100x or more, basically as much as using a matrix crystal.  Meshram used to be able to lift around 18.5g, one of our strongest telekinetics.  Now he's up to 2kg and with a crystal he can lift two bowling balls.  Or a dog, that was hilarious.\n"
"\n"
"Subject U76 could pick up surface thoughts if touching the target and now can easily read someone's mind from across the room and can occasionally pick up deeper memories.  We figured this out by accident, by the way, and I'm pretty sure when we get out of here Dr. Connolly is going to find divorce papers waiting for her.  You'll probably want to keep U76 away from anything sensitive, except that we only just discovered this and now it's too late.  Oops.\n"
"\n"
"Oh yeah, K34 can just walk through walls now.  So much for security.  Everything's fucked and we're doomed.  That's my report, hope you like it."
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"As my initial report indicated, COBALT THORN has passed all the tests we've performed.  In fact, it exceeded our production predictions by over 15%.  It's not actually a perpetual motion machine but it might as well be from the end-user's point of view.  It produces energy with no fuel required, at a constant rate, with no waste byproducts and very little heat.\n"
"\n"
"However--there's always a however in this line of work--it has the significant disadvantage that prevents me from recommending it for deployment at this time.  COBALT THORN works through a microportal to the Netherum, siphoning energy through without the possibility of hostile incursions.  During normal operation, this remains true, but if the device is damaged it can destabilize containment and the portal can rapidly expand without warning.  Just last week we had an incident during testing, and while the engineers were able to get the device shut down quickly, something still came through the portal.  We're lucky that it doesn't seem hostile or really even interested in us.  Despite its appearance (see attached), XE843 is indifferent to the presence or absence of others, light levels, food, or noise.  It just wanders around its containment cell.  We've contacted XEDRA-40 to ask them if they want to take a look at it.  I'll forward the reply to you when we get it.\n"
"\n"
"Work to overcome this significant drawback is ongoing.  At the moment, however, COBALT THORN should remain in the prototype stage.\n"
"\n"
"Anita Morales\n"
"Senior Researcher"
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"As requested, we conducted multiple tests using various matrix crystals to determine the precise effect on mathematician capabilities.  The first test subject was V72, representing JUNIPER GOLD.  In previous capability testing, V72 was capable of lifting 10.23g and holding it steady for at least 300 seconds, as well as consistently being able to reduce their acceleration when free-falling to 9.32 m/s².  When holding a charged matrix crystal, the effect was nothing short of astonishing--the mass limit on lifting increased to 2.43 kg and the acceleration when free-falling dropped to 7.17 m/s².\n"
"\n"
"BURNT NOVEMBER Subject Q51 displayed a resting heart rate of 65 bpm, a grip strength of 30 kg, and a 8:31 mile time.  When holding a charged matrix crystal, these improved to 55 bpm, a grip strength of 41 kg, and a 5:45 mile time.\n"
"\n"
"The evidence shows that skin contact with a charged matrix crystal dramatically improves mathematician capabilities, up to several hundred times depending on their exact capabilities.  While matrix crystals are always in short supply, some of them should definitely be earmarked for usage by our most capable mathematicians."
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"Dr. Richardson,\n"
"I'm writing with some disturbing reports from recent testings.  While the increased capabilities mathematicians have been displaying are at this point well-known among staff, in the course of my research I've observed a number of previously-unseen side effects from performing mathematics.  The most common side effect seems to be headaches, though my staff have also observed several instances of spontaneous nosebleeds.  In at least one instance, a COPPER PRIME experiment with I33 involving heating metals to the melting point, a sudden temperature drop of 15°C was observed in the sealed experimental chamber.\n"
"\n"
"Far more disturbing, however, was an incident during ONYX LIGHTNING testing.  K92 seemingly lost control of her powers when attempting to damage a training dummy, causing severe--and under lockdown, irreplaceable--damage to several testing implements.  When asked to explain herself, she was only able to say that her powers seemed to take on a \"mind of their own.\"\n"
"\n"
"I am still a scientist, regardless of what is happening now.  Be assured that I will get to the bottom of this.\n"
"\n"
"Ted Kelly\n"
"Senior Researcher"
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"Xinying,\n"
"You were right.  I looked over the cafeteria camera records and the mathematicians are consistently coming in twice or three times as often as most other people.  Usually just for snacks, but it's pretty consistent that after an experiment, one of them will wander in and grab some chips or an apple or cookies.  We need to start weighing them in and out like they're jockeys or something and seeing if we can get some hard data on this."
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"We still don't have any method of nullifying Netherum mathematics that can be used by a mathematician, but the boys down in R&D came out with something they're calling the \"null grenade.\"  BD833-P produces a short-term disruption in anyone affected by it, preventing use of dimensional metaphysics for up to 25 seconds with no further ill effects.  I89 agreed to spend a significant length of time having BD833-P set off next to him repeatedly and a full medical examination showed no problems.  While I89 complained of a small headache, it faded within ten minutes of the last BD833-P detonation and a week later, I89 has shown no lasting ill effects.\n"
"\n"
"Now, the obvious problem: 25 seconds isn't much.  In-phase if a dive team is trying to neutralize a mathematician--so far a theoretical situation, but we cannot rule it out--it should be plenty, but it won't be enough to capture or restrain any target.  It would also be nice to have some way of focusing the effect, some kind of \"null ray\" or something similar.  Research, as they say, is ongoing."
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"Alright, so should I even be working on this?  The world is ending, we're on"
" lockdown, and I'm pretty sure some of my coworkers have lost their minds.  "
"I should be looking for ways to get out of here, right?  But hell, I've "
"always buried myself in my work in a crisis and this sure is one of those.  "
"So my report is that ever since we detected the spread of XE037, COBALT "
"THORN has been running at…well, it's a perpetual motion machine so I can't "
"exactly talk about \"increased efficiency\" but it's been putting out even "
"more power than it was a month ago.  On the order of 3x more.  Maybe all "
"that nonsense about the fabric of space expanding or whatever was right?  I "
"regret to inform you that it's still occasionally popping out monsters, "
"though fortunately the only thing I had to deal with so far has been those "
"blobs and I set up an isolation chamber for COBALT THORN to run in.  It's "
"keeping the lights on down here, so there's that.  If I can just fix that "
"one flaw, we'll see set.  Too bad my assistant is out trying to figure out "
"how to jump floor to floor so they don't have to use the stairs anymore."
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"Colleague,\n"
"Greetings.  Your reading of this letter means you have been chosen as an OBSIDIAN RING candidate.  Having already demonstrated proficiency with the fundamentals of matrix mechanics and an understanding of our mission here at Project PHAVIAN, we are offering you the opportunity to participate in experiments into strengthening the fundamental human potential for dimensional metaphysics.  In-phase conditions have shown us that the abilities displayed by mathematicians here are not the absolute limit of those abilities, and if we could replicate some in-phase conditions without the need for an immersion dive, we could expand our mathematicians' capabilities tenfold.\n"
"\n"
"I do have to warn you that the process is not without risk.  While here at XEDRA-23 we have the most advanced medical treatment in the world, there is still a risk of permanent injury should you choose to go through with the procedure.  If you should refuse, your talents remain as valuable as ever and you will suffer no career repercussions.  I look forward to working with you on the next step for Project PHAVIAN and humanity.\n"
"Alexandra da Silva\n"
"Lead Researcher, OBSIDIAN RING"
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"Candidate is a Black female, aged 45 years, employed in Project PHAVIAN's Building Maintenance division, with early-onset osteoarthritis leading to significant quality of life issues.  Candidate volunteered within hours after the SHADOW URGE posting went out and expressed that, \"Anything is better than how I feel when I wake up nowadays\", unquote.\n"
"\n"
"The procedure was conducted with mathematicians Q17 and R98 in attendance to attempt to adjust for any unforeseen circumstances, but as it turned out, we needn't have worried.  The next day, candidate reported increased mobility and reduced pain.  One week after the procedure, candidate discontinued her prescription pain medication and has not resumed it.  MRI of affected joints show regrowth of soft tissue and absence of previously-identified bone spurs.  While the requirement of a matrix crystal to provide the catalyst is a significant one and prevents scaling SHADOW URGE up to any significant level at this time, and while we will need to monitor the candidate for an extended period to make sure that her osteoarthritis does not reoccur, this is an exciting step forward in the field of human knowledge.\n"
"\n"
"Maybe Dr. Campbell was right.  Maybe eventually we will cure death."
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"Colleagues,\n"
"\n"
"I'd like to take a moment to address the recent rumors.  I know that stress levels are high with the quarantine and the XE037 news, but there is no need to engage in unwarranted speculation.  In these unprecedented times, it's important to remember that we're all in this together and we will solve the problems before us, as we have so many others.\n"
"\n"
"I will be perfectly clear.  There is no \"Project GASPAR.\"  Trained mathematicians are the most important resource that we have, and it would be the height of folly to waste them on replicating a resource that already exists simply because the current state of emergency has placed us out of contact.  Furthermore, it is important to remember that Netherum mathematics are not magic.  They obey a consistent set of rules and we are capable of determining those rules empirically.  We can test how much a JUNIPER GOLD mathematician can lift to the milligram.  We can determine the effective communication range for a GRAY DAWN candidate down to the decimeter.  We would never simply \"throw things at the wall and see what sticks.\"  Science requires rigor.\n"
"\n"
"These are troubling times, but we will get through them together.\n"
"\n"
"Sincerely,\n"
"Harold Liu\n"
"Director, Project PHAVIAN"
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"Greetings everyone,\n"
"\n"
"I would just like to take a moment to comment on the importance of proper nomenclature.  Just as we would respect the names and pronouns by which our co-workers wish to be addressed, we should use the approved terms for candidates for the various projects under our umbrella.  Some frankly disturbing news has reached me of harassment or even bullying aimed at those who have gone through the training process.  These people are not \"witches\" and they are most certainly not \"freaks,\" and I am frankly disturbed that I have to emphasize that point.  These are your colleagues who have volunteered to advance scientific understanding as we explore the unknown.  There is no reason standard HR policies do not still apply.  I have already received several complaints which I will be acting on in the near future, and hopefully I will not receive any more.\n"
"\n"
"Sincerely,\n"
"Rosemary Pierce\n"
"Administrator, Human Resources"
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"Anna, I know things are stressful, especially with some of the irregularities in staff behavior we've been witnessing, and under normal circumstances I would never countenance your proposal.  I have to admit, though, that I was extremely disturbed by what I've heard of the behavior of several VERDANT HAND mathematicians, as well as Dr. Holland and Dr. Almeida's recent public argument.  As such, for the duration of the emergency, I think that your \"psi-cop\" proposal is a good one.  I'll draft a memo immediately to Dr. Nayak to organize the GREY DAWN mathematicians toward keeping order and maintaining morale.  Hopefully, this will only be the matter of a few weeks before Dr. Sidhu and his team can find a solution.  They already found one way to remove XE037 contamination, so hope remains.\n"
"\n"
"Sincerely,\n"
"Harold Liu"
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"Colleague,\n"
"\n"
"Greetings.  You have selected, or have been selected, to participate in XEDRA-23, or as we call it, Project PHAVIAN.  As a member of XEDRA, you will already have seen many extraordinary things in the course of your work, things which you previously might have scoffed at or dismissed out of hand.  You will see more extraordinary things in the course of your work here, things that even those at other XEDRA divisions would have thought impossible a few years ago.  Phase experiments expand the range of human exploration, but matrix technology unlocks human potential to a degree never before seen.  You will be a part of that endeavor, advancing human knowledge and ensuring the United States of America's place at the forefront of scientific advancement throughout the 21st century.\n"
"\n"
"There is an ancient proverb that is often translated as \"A single spark can start a prairie fire.\"  Our work here will be the light that will lead humanity into a new age.  I look forward to working with you.\n"
"\n"
"Harold Liu\n"
"Director, Project PHAVIAN"
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"Dr. Liu,\n"
"Sorry for the inflammatory title but, well, something is seriously wrong.  The LOST RAIN mathematicians are universally reporting that something strange is happening to space itself.  You've seen the testing data about them being able to change effective distance between two points and they're reporting that ALL distances are being affected to a very small degree.  I don't know if this has anything to do with the erratic behavior from the staff or XE037 contamination but coupled with all the NOBLE HORIZON reports of impending doom, plus all the news filtering from the outside, I think we need to prepare for the worst.\n"
"\n"
"John Goldberg\n"
"Researcher"
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"It is important to remember that we are scientists and this is a scientific endeavor.  Regardless of the phenomena we are studying, we must maintain a proper skeptical mindset in the spirit of scientific inquiry.  Dimensional metaphysics has its own laws that we are slowly discovering.  This is not \"witchcraft\", these are not \"wizards,\" they are people capable of tapping in to a previously-unknown source of energy.  There are many previous fields of science which once carried their own stigma.  Continental drift was not accepted for decades after its initial proposal, Dr. Semmelweis died in an asylum, and quantum  mechanics to this day requires accepting behaviors that are counter to our natural understanding of how the world works.  That does not make any of those fields supernatural either.  By definition, if it is studiable and reproducible, it is scientific.\n"
"Anna Richardson\n"
"Director of Research"
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"No mathematician should be subject to more than ten hours of testing in a two-day period.  Any period of more than four hours of continuous testing must include a half-hour meal break.  Mathematicians are entitled to the same work-week and schedule as researchers are, including days off.  Mathematicians will be informed of the purpose and subject of any experiment they take part in and may register a complaint with HR if they object to their participation.  Note that this does not absolve each mathematician from fulfilling the duties of their employment.  Mathematicians must wear their identifying badges at all times when on-site and present them for inspection at the request of any member of security.\n"
"\n"
"Our mathematicians are not cases, they are not subjects, and they are certainly not \"guinea pigs\" or \"lab rats.\"  They are valuable partners in our exploration of dimensional metaphysics, irreplaceable personnel, and should be treated as such.  Researchers found violating these guidelines will be sanctioned, up to and including termination of employment."
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"Dr. Mitchell,\n"
"Per our last email, Dr. Enrique Rodriguez passed away in a car accident almost two years ago, shortly after being assigned to XEDRA as a portal research specialist, and he never had the opportunity to work with XEDRA-23.  As you can see from the employee database, there has never been a Dr. Julia Simmons employed by either XEDRA-23 or any other XEDRA division.\n"
"\n"
"In addition, the XEDRA handbook requires that all employees use their current title in their signature at all times.  Please update your signature to comply with this policy.\n"
"Alicia Sanders\n"
"Senior Talent Coodinator"
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"Colleagues,\n"
"\n"
"Following the recent incident, PHAVIAN is immediately instituting a requirement that all sensitive data be stored offline, on paper, away from possible RUBY LOOP interference.  Incident 523184 has shown us that existing security protocols are utterly ineffective at stopping RUBY LOOP from altering stored data, and while we only lost a week of experimental results, those results include the most recent COBALT THORN test and thus represent a profound blow to our work in advancing human knowledge.  I recognize the difficulty of changing our experimental procedures and our methods of communication so drastically at such short notice, but at the moment we are still not sure how much advancement that other nations have made in the fields of portal immersion or in Netherum mathematics, so it is best to take extreme caution while we develop new protocols around information security.  When we have a update, or an effective counter to possible RUBY LOOP interference, rest assured that I will share it with you immediately.\n"
"\n"
"Harold Liu\n"
"Director, Project PHAVIAN"
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"Dr. Liu,\n"
"Based on these preliminary results, I'm afraid there is no other option than to seek XEDRA-external candidates.  We've run every single employee at site 2 through the resonance detector and none of them came up higher than Minor, with most not even registering at all.  The capability to understand and manipulate dimensional metaphysics seems limited to a small fraction of the population, and until we can figure some way to affect that it means that our mathematician pool is extremely and unacceptably limited.  As such, I propose that we begin limited screening from among other government employees and, if necessary, among the general population.\n"
"\n"
"I recognize the security concerns inherent in this suggestion, but until we can convince the other XEDRA divisions to allow us to screen all of their employees or otherwise find a large pool of cleared candidates, recruitment is going to be the only option.\n"
"Joshua Sanders\n"
"Lead Researcher, AZURE SONNET"
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"Dammit, Hank, what the hell is wrong with these researchers?  Matrix-powered"
" lamp, matrix-powered car, matrix-powered oven, next they'll want a matrix-"
"powered vibrator.  Do they even understand how expensive a single matrix "
"crystal is?  I keep trying to get them to work on something new and they "
"bring me this.  We need force fields, jetpacks, laser guns, lightsabers, "
"starships, I don't know, something!  It's all I can do to stop them from "
"trying to make us the Amazon of XEDRA.  Do the XE037 researchers have this "
"problem?"
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"Mo,\n"
"I know you're worried about maintaining secrecy what with the NOBLE HORIZON/GRAY DAWN research locations, but I assure you that it's fine.  We need them higher-up to test for line-of-sight-based range anyway, and we don't have all the problems that XEDRA-12 has with maintaining secrecy.  If some normie somehow gets past security and wanders in, they're just going to see an ordinary office with maybe a few weird room layouts, there aren't going to be wolfmen wandering the halls.  The mathematicians are just people, and if some of them are creepy, we've ALL worked with the creepy guy before.  If it were really that serious of a concern, we'd be underground like the LOST RAIN guys.  And with a bunch of clears here, we'll get warning hours or days before anything goes wrong.\n"
"\n"
"And besides, look at the advantages!  There's a gym and a bar on the ground floor.  Drinks with Priya and Ishaan on Friday?  I've already checked the menu and I know there'll be something there for you.\n"
"Sridhar"
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"Jen\n"
"I know we're in lockdown but it's obvious we're doomed.  Word gets out, right?  You heard about Dr. Greene and Dr. Summers?  It's only going to get worse.  I talked to K̶3̶4̶  Erica about it and she's positive she can take someone else with her on one of her little trips.  It's not that far to the surface, right?  You with me?\n"
"Alex"
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"A,\n"
"I did it.  The records are all garbage now and it'll take them a week to source more, maybe longer with this lockdown.  You're free until then.  I love you.\n"
"-C"
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"They say there's nothing to worry about, that our powers follow natural laws that can be tested and measured, but it's obvious they're lying.  I heard what happened to Amelia when she was doing some experiment and had that asthma attack.  A tragic accident, they said?  Yeah, not after I saw the aftermath of that lab test with the telekinetic.  What happens if they lose control in a crowded hallway, or if a telepath does in the lunchroom?  Are we all going to end up vegetables?\n"
"\n"
"I haven't used any psi since I heard, but it's so hard.  I went from getting sick 4-5 times a year to feeling like a million bucks every single day and I'm just supposed to give it up?  But what if my heart just stops?  What if someone else's heart stops because of me?  The scientists spent a year testing and measuring and now apparently none of it matters because who knows what will happen.\n"
"\n"
"I never should have gone through with the treatment."
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"C,\n"
"Just talked to ███████ on our lunch break and he confirmed what I heard--Gaspar is real.  We all know people who have just disappeared, right?  They say they're transferred to other sites, to keep up the variety in experiments or whatever, but do they ever get transferred back?  You heard of Project Empty Mother?  Sapphire Horizon?  You know about the magi, right?  There's always three and where's the third?  They can't turn us all into meat but they're going to do it to some of us and I don't want to be one of them.  We have to get out of here.\n"
"-A"
msgstr ""

#: ./snippets/snippets_new.json
msgid ""
"I keep feeling like something is watching me while I'm working on the "
"engines.  Like there are shadows behind me even in a perfectly-lit room.  "
"I've set up my phone to record and of course, nothing shows up.  But there's"
" something.  I run the footage through frame-by-frame and there are "
"occasional frames of pure static when I'm tinkering and I can't place "
"exactly which part of the engine is causing it, even when I try the same "
"thing multiple times.  The static isn't always there, but it's there often "
"enough.  I know they put Mitchell on administrative leave after his "
"breakdown but maybe he was on to something."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/biokinesis.json
msgid "[Ψ]Personal Enhancement (C)"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Personal Enhancement (C)
#: ./spells/biokinesis.json
msgid ""
"You suffuse your body with psionic energy, sharpening every faculty at once: <color_light_green>Strength, Dexterity, Intelligence, and Perception</color> all rise together.  The bonus grows with both your mastery of this power and your Intelligence — from <color_light_green>+1</color> to each stat when you first learn it, up to <color_light_green>+10</color> to each at full mastery with a keen mind.\n"
"\n"
"This power <color_yellow>is maintained by concentration</color> and <color_red>may fail</color> if <color_yellow>concentration is interrupted</color>.\n"
"\n"
"Level 5 leads to Burst of Speed with Enhance Mobility 6 + Heightened Reflexes 5 OR Adrenaline Trigger 8 + Enhance Mobility 6 OR Heightened Reflexes 5 + Personal Enhancement 5 OR Adrenaline Trigger 8 + Personal Enhancement 5.\n"
"Level 10 leads to Combat Dance with Burst of Speed 6 + Heightened Reflexes 10 + Personal Enhancement 10 OR Adrenaline Trigger 9 + Heightened Reflexes 10 + Personal Enhancement 10.\n"
"Level 6 leads to Detoxification.\n"
"Level 10 leads to Enhance Mobility with Burst of Speed 10 + Heightened Reflexes 6 + Overcome Pain 4 OR Burst of Speed 10 + Detoxification 9 + Overcome Pain 4 OR Combat Dance 4 + Heightened Reflexes 6 + Overcome Pain 4 OR Combat Dance 4 + Detoxification 9 + Overcome Pain 4 OR Heightened Reflexes 6 + Overcome Pain 4 + Personal Enhancement 10 OR Detoxification 9 + Overcome Pain 4 + Personal Enhancement 10.\n"
"Level 6 leads to Hammerhand with Hardened Skin 6.\n"
"Level 8 leads to Hardened Skin with Detoxification 7 + Personal Enhancement 8 OR Personal Enhancement 8 + Temperature Adaptability 6 OR Detoxification 7 + Overcome Pain 6 OR Overcome Pain 6 + Temperature Adaptability 6.\n"
"Level 6 leads to Heightened Reflexes with Adrenaline Trigger 8 + Burst of Speed 8 + Personal Enhancement 6 OR Adrenaline Trigger 8 + Detoxification 8 + Personal Enhancement 6.\n"
"Level 12 leads to Metabolic Hyperefficiency with Adrenaline Trigger 6 + Temperature Adaptability 8 OR Personal Enhancement 12 + Temperature Adaptability 8.\n"
"Level 4 leads to Oxygen Absorption with Overcome Pain 3.\n"
"Level 9 leads to Temperature Adaptability with Overcome Pain 5 + Personal Enhancement 9 OR Metabolic Hyperefficiency 6 + Overcome Pain 5."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/biokinesis.json
msgid "[Ψ]Overcome Pain (C)"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Overcome Pain (C)
#: ./spells/biokinesis.json
msgid ""
"You can lessen the impact of pain on your performance, though this has no effect on the underlying injuries.\n"
"\n"
"This power <color_yellow>is maintained by concentration</color> and <color_red>may fail</color> if <color_yellow>concentration is interrupted</color>.\n"
"\n"
"Level 4 leads to Enhance Mobility with Burst of Speed 10 + Heightened Reflexes 6 + Overcome Pain 4 OR Burst of Speed 10 + Detoxification 9 + Overcome Pain 4 OR Combat Dance 4 + Heightened Reflexes 6 + Overcome Pain 4 OR Combat Dance 4 + Detoxification 9 + Overcome Pain 4 OR Heightened Reflexes 6 + Overcome Pain 4 + Personal Enhancement 10 OR Detoxification 9 + Overcome Pain 4 + Personal Enhancement 10.\n"
"Level 6 leads to Hardened Skin with Detoxification 7 + Personal Enhancement 8 OR Personal Enhancement 8 + Temperature Adaptability 6 OR Detoxification 7 + Overcome Pain 6 OR Overcome Pain 6 + Temperature Adaptability 6.\n"
"Level 3 leads to Oxygen Absorption with Personal Enhancement 4.\n"
"Level 5 leads to Temperature Adaptability with Overcome Pain 5 + Personal Enhancement 9 OR Metabolic Hyperefficiency 6 + Overcome Pain 5."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/biokinesis.json
msgid "[Ψ]Oxygen Absorption (C)"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Oxygen Absorption (C)
#: ./spells/biokinesis.json
msgid ""
"You can make the entire surface of your skin selectively permeable, allowing you to 'breathe' through it.  You can breathe in low-oxygen environments or underwater, but are more vulnerable to toxic gas.\n"
"\n"
"This power <color_yellow>is maintained by concentration</color> and <color_red>may fail</color> if <color_yellow>concentration is interrupted</color>.  Oxygen Absorption <color_red>cannot be active</color> with Sealed System.\n"
"\n"
"Level 5 leads to Adrenaline Trigger with Burst of Speed 8 + Oxygen Absorption 5 OR Enhance Mobility 6 + Oxygen Absorption 5.\n"
"Level 9 leads to Sealed System with Hammerhand 7 + Oxygen Absorption 9 OR Oxygen Absorption 9 + Temperature Adaptability 10 OR Hammerhand 7 + Hardened Skin 9 OR Hardened Skin 9 + Temperature Adaptability 10."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/biokinesis.json
msgid "[Ψ]Burst of Speed"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Burst of Speed
#: ./spells/biokinesis.json
msgid ""
"Like a cheetah, you can run with incredible speed for a short distance.\n"
"\n"
"Level 8 leads to Adrenaline Trigger with Burst of Speed 8 + Oxygen Absorption 5 OR Enhance Mobility 6 + Oxygen Absorption 5.\n"
"Level 6 leads to Combat Dance with Burst of Speed 6 + Heightened Reflexes 10 + Personal Enhancement 10 OR Adrenaline Trigger 9 + Heightened Reflexes 10 + Personal Enhancement 10.\n"
"Level 10 leads to Enhance Mobility with Burst of Speed 10 + Heightened Reflexes 6 + Overcome Pain 4 OR Burst of Speed 10 + Detoxification 9 + Overcome Pain 4 OR Combat Dance 4 + Heightened Reflexes 6 + Overcome Pain 4 OR Combat Dance 4 + Detoxification 9 + Overcome Pain 4 OR Heightened Reflexes 6 + Overcome Pain 4 + Personal Enhancement 10 OR Detoxification 9 + Overcome Pain 4 + Personal Enhancement 10.\n"
"Level 8 leads to Heightened Reflexes with Adrenaline Trigger 8 + Burst of Speed 8 + Personal Enhancement 6 OR Adrenaline Trigger 8 + Detoxification 8 + Personal Enhancement 6.\n"
"Level 12 leads to Perfected Motion with Combat Dance 6."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Message for SPELL '[Ψ]Burst of Speed'
#: ./spells/biokinesis.json
msgid "You move almost faster than the eye can see."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/biokinesis.json
msgid "[Ψ]Hardened Skin (C)"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Hardened Skin (C)
#: ./spells/biokinesis.json
msgid ""
"You can increase the strength of your skin, making it almost like armor while still allowing you to move freely.\n"
"\n"
"This power <color_yellow>is maintained by concentration</color> and <color_red>may fail</color> if <color_yellow>concentration is interrupted</color>.\n"
"\n"
"Level 6 leads to Hammerhand with Personal Enhancement 6.\n"
"Level 9 leads to Sealed System with Hammerhand 7 + Oxygen Absorption 9 OR Oxygen Absorption 9 + Temperature Adaptability 10 OR Hammerhand 7 + Hardened Skin 9 OR Hardened Skin 9 + Temperature Adaptability 10."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/biokinesis.json ./spells/psychic_knacks.json
msgid "[Ψ]Adrenaline Trigger"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Adrenaline Trigger
#: ./spells/biokinesis.json
msgid ""
"With a moment of concentration, you can trigger a surge of adrenaline.  This provides a speed boost, albeit at a draining cost when the boost expires.\n"
"\n"
"Level 6 leads to Anabolic Rejuvenation with Metabolic Hyperefficiency 8.\n"
"Level 8 leads to Burst of Speed with Enhance Mobility 6 + Heightened Reflexes 5 OR Adrenaline Trigger 8 + Enhance Mobility 6 OR Heightened Reflexes 5 + Personal Enhancement 5 OR Adrenaline Trigger 8 + Personal Enhancement 5.\n"
"Level 9 leads to Combat Dance with Burst of Speed 6 + Heightened Reflexes 10 + Personal Enhancement 10 OR Adrenaline Trigger 9 + Heightened Reflexes 10 + Personal Enhancement 10.\n"
"Level 8 leads to Heightened Reflexes with Adrenaline Trigger 8 + Burst of Speed 8 + Personal Enhancement 6 OR Adrenaline Trigger 8 + Detoxification 8 + Personal Enhancement 6.\n"
"Level 12 leads to Hurricane Blows with Combat Dance 10 + Heightened Reflexes 14 OR Adrenaline Trigger 12 + Combat Dance 10.\n"
"Level 6 leads to Metabolic Hyperefficiency with Adrenaline Trigger 6 + Temperature Adaptability 8 OR Personal Enhancement 12 + Temperature Adaptability 8."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Message for SPELL '[Ψ]Adrenaline Trigger'
#: ./spells/biokinesis.json ./spells/psychic_knacks.json
msgid "Your heartbeat surges as your body floods with adrenaline."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/biokinesis.json
msgid "[Ψ]Temperature Adaptability (C)"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Temperature Adaptability (C)
#: ./spells/biokinesis.json
msgid ""
"You can increase the heat dissipation and retention of your body, allowing you to function in a much wider range of temperatures.  Temperature Adaptability and Sealed System <color_red>will cancel each other</color>.\n"
"\n"
"This power <color_yellow>is maintained by concentration</color> and <color_red>may fail</color> if <color_yellow>concentration is interrupted</color>.\n"
"\n"
"Level 6 leads to Hardened Skin with Detoxification 7 + Personal Enhancement 8 OR Personal Enhancement 8 + Temperature Adaptability 6 OR Detoxification 7 + Overcome Pain 6 OR Overcome Pain 6 + Temperature Adaptability 6.\n"
"Level 8 leads to Metabolic Hyperefficiency with Adrenaline Trigger 6 + Temperature Adaptability 8 OR Personal Enhancement 12 + Temperature Adaptability 8.\n"
"Level 10 leads to Sealed System with Hammerhand 7 + Oxygen Absorption 9 OR Oxygen Absorption 9 + Temperature Adaptability 10 OR Hammerhand 7 + Hardened Skin 9 OR Hardened Skin 9 + Temperature Adaptability 10."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/biokinesis.json
msgid "[Ψ]Enhance Mobility (C)"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Enhance Mobility (C)
#: ./spells/biokinesis.json
msgid ""
"Increase your range of motion and flexibility such that you can move more easily even in encumbering gear.\n"
"\n"
"This power <color_yellow>is maintained by concentration</color> and <color_red>may fail</color> if <color_yellow>concentration is interrupted</color>.\n"
"\n"
"Level 6 leads to Adrenaline Trigger with Burst of Speed 8 + Oxygen Absorption 5 OR Enhance Mobility 6 + Oxygen Absorption 5.\n"
"Level 6 leads to Burst of Speed with Enhance Mobility 6 + Heightened Reflexes 5 OR Adrenaline Trigger 8 + Enhance Mobility 6 OR Heightened Reflexes 5 + Personal Enhancement 5 OR Adrenaline Trigger 8 + Personal Enhancement 5."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/biokinesis.json
msgid "[Ψ]Hammerhand (C)"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Hammerhand (C)
#: ./spells/biokinesis.json
msgid ""
"Who needs tools?  You can apply enough raw force or torque with your bare hands to substitute for many simple tools.\n"
"\n"
"This power <color_yellow>is maintained by concentration</color> and <color_red>may fail</color> if <color_yellow>concentration is interrupted</color>.\n"
"\n"
"Level 7 leads to Sealed System with Hammerhand 7 + Oxygen Absorption 9 OR Oxygen Absorption 9 + Temperature Adaptability 10 OR Hammerhand 7 + Hardened Skin 9 OR Hardened Skin 9 + Temperature Adaptability 10."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/biokinesis.json
msgid "[Ψ]Heightened Reflexes (C)"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Heightened Reflexes (C)
#: ./spells/biokinesis.json
msgid ""
"You can improve your sensory acuity and the speed at which your brain processes sensory inputs.\n"
"\n"
"This power <color_yellow>is maintained by concentration</color> and <color_red>may fail</color> if <color_yellow>concentration is interrupted</color>.\n"
"\n"
"Level 5 leads to Burst of Speed with Enhance Mobility 6 + Heightened Reflexes 5 OR Adrenaline Trigger 8 + Enhance Mobility 6 OR Heightened Reflexes 5 + Personal Enhancement 5 OR Adrenaline Trigger 8 + Personal Enhancement 5.\n"
"Level 10 leads to Combat Dance with Burst of Speed 6 + Heightened Reflexes 10 + Personal Enhancement 10 OR Adrenaline Trigger 9 + Heightened Reflexes 10 + Personal Enhancement 10.\n"
"Level 6 leads to Enhance Mobility with Burst of Speed 10 + Heightened Reflexes 6 + Overcome Pain 4 OR Burst of Speed 10 + Detoxification 9 + Overcome Pain 4 OR Combat Dance 4 + Heightened Reflexes 6 + Overcome Pain 4 OR Combat Dance 4 + Detoxification 9 + Overcome Pain 4 OR Heightened Reflexes 6 + Overcome Pain 4 + Personal Enhancement 10 OR Detoxification 9 + Overcome Pain 4 + Personal Enhancement 10.\n"
"Level 14 leads to Hurricane Blows with Combat Dance 10 + Heightened Reflexes 14 OR Adrenaline Trigger 12 + Combat Dance 10."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/biokinesis.json
msgid "[Ψ]Sealed System"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Sealed System
#: ./spells/biokinesis.json
msgid ""
"With a deep breath, you lock your body off from the outside world.  Gas, poison, blood, bile, electricity--nothing gets in, nothing gets out.\n"
"\n"
"Sealed System <color_red>cannot be active</color> with either Temperature Adaptability or Oxygen Absorption."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Message for SPELL '[Ψ]Sealed System'
#: ./spells/biokinesis.json
msgid "You take a deep breath and seal your lips."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/biokinesis.json
msgid "[Ψ]Metabolic Hyperefficiency (C)"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Metabolic Hyperefficiency (C)
#: ./spells/biokinesis.json
msgid ""
"You can supercharge your metabolism, allowing you to eat, drink, and sleep much less than normal.\n"
"\n"
"This power <color_yellow>is maintained by concentration</color> and <color_red>may fail</color> if <color_yellow>concentration is interrupted</color>.  It is <color_red>canceled by engaging in combat</color>.\n"
"\n"
"Level 8 leads to Anabolic Rejuvenation with Adrenaline Trigger 6.\n"
"Level 6 leads to Temperature Adaptability with Overcome Pain 5 + Personal Enhancement 9 OR Metabolic Hyperefficiency 6 + Overcome Pain 5."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/biokinesis.json
msgid "[Ψ]Combat Dance (C)"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Combat Dance (C)
#: ./spells/biokinesis.json
msgid ""
"You can flood your body with psionic power to enhance your combat prowess.\n"
"\n"
"Level 4 leads to Enhance Mobility with Burst of Speed 10 + Heightened Reflexes 6 + Overcome Pain 4 OR Burst of Speed 10 + Detoxification 9 + Overcome Pain 4 OR Combat Dance 4 + Heightened Reflexes 6 + Overcome Pain 4 OR Combat Dance 4 + Detoxification 9 + Overcome Pain 4 OR Heightened Reflexes 6 + Overcome Pain 4 + Personal Enhancement 10 OR Detoxification 9 + Overcome Pain 4 + Personal Enhancement 10.\n"
"Level 10 leads to Hurricane Blows with Combat Dance 10 + Heightened Reflexes 14 OR Adrenaline Trigger 12 + Combat Dance 10.\n"
"Level 6 leads to Perfected Motion with Burst of Speed 12."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/biokinesis.json
msgid "[Ψ]Perfected Motion (C)"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Perfected Motion (C)
#: ./spells/biokinesis.json
msgid ""
"Your control over your body allows you to move incredibly quickly.  While this does not allow you to attack more quickly, you can cross distances in the blink of an eye and outrun a cheetah.  You could even run on water, though not walk on it.\n"
"\n"
"This power <color_yellow>is maintained by concentration</color> and <color_red>may fail</color> if <color_yellow>concentration is interrupted</color>.  It requires <color_yellow>even more concentration</color> than usual.\n"
"\n"
"Perfected Motion <color_red>cannot be active</color> with Hurricane Blows."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/biokinesis.json
msgid "[Ψ]Hurricane Blows"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Hurricane Blows
#: ./spells/biokinesis.json
msgid ""
"You can now strike so quickly that you don't even seem to move at all.  Before an opponent can even finish blinking, you can strike them multiple times, executing your final blow before they feel the pain of the first.  Moving while using Hurricane Blows will disrupt your concentration, ending the effect.\n"
"\n"
"Hurricane Blows <color_red>cannot be active</color> with Perfected Motion."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Message for SPELL '[Ψ]Hurricane Blows'
#: ./spells/biokinesis.json
msgid "The world around you slows down to a stop."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/clairsentience.json ./spells/psychic_knacks.json
msgid "[Ψ]Heightened Senses (C)"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Heightened Senses (C)
#: ./spells/clairsentience.json
msgid ""
"All of your senses are heightened, allowing you to see further and hear better, and at higher levels even see in murky water or use minor vibrations and small sounds to determine moving creatures nearby.\n"
"\n"
"This power <color_yellow>is maintained by concentration</color> and <color_red>may fail</color> if <color_yellow>concentration is interrupted</color>.\n"
"\n"
"Level 5 leads to Aura Sight.\n"
"Level 8 leads to Night Eyes.\n"
"Level 6 leads to Premonition.\n"
"Level 3 leads to See Mechanisms."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/clairsentience.json
msgid "[Ψ]Speed Reader (C)"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Speed Reader (C)
#: ./spells/clairsentience.json
msgid ""
"Your powers make words fairly leap off the page directly into your mind, allowing you to read much faster and better absorb what you read.\n"
"\n"
"This power <color_yellow>is maintained by concentration</color> and <color_red>may fail</color> if <color_yellow>concentration is interrupted</color>.  It is <color_red>canceled by engaging in combat</color>.\n"
"\n"
"Level 8 leads to Intuitive Artisan with Premonition 6.\n"
"Level 8 leads to Psychometry with Aura Sight 6 OR Speed Reader 8 OR Premonition 8."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/clairsentience.json ./spells/psychic_knacks.json
msgid "[Ψ]Premonition (C)"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Premonition (C)
#: ./spells/clairsentience.json
msgid ""
"You can sense nearby movement and sometimes gain an advance warning of dangerous events.\n"
"\n"
"This power <color_yellow>is maintained by concentration</color> and <color_red>may fail</color> if <color_yellow>concentration is interrupted</color>.\n"
"\n"
"Level 6 leads to Clairvoyance.\n"
"Level 10 leads to Combat Sense with Clairvoyance 6.\n"
"Level 6 leads to Intuitive Artisan with Speed Reader 8.\n"
"Level 8 leads to Psychometry with Aura Sight 6 OR Speed Reader 8 OR Premonition 8."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/clairsentience.json
msgid "[Ψ]Night Eyes (C)"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Night Eyes (C)
#: ./spells/clairsentience.json
msgid ""
"You are able to sense your surroundings in areas of low light, and you can even \"see\" in pitch darkness.  Strictly speaking, this is not vision, and you cannot discern fine details or read.\n"
"\n"
"This power <color_yellow>is maintained by concentration</color> and <color_red>may fail</color> if <color_yellow>concentration is interrupted</color>.\n"
"\n"
"Level 10 leads to Clarity."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/clairsentience.json
msgid "[Ψ]Aura Sight (C)"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Aura Sight (C)
#: ./spells/clairsentience.json
msgid ""
"You can see people's emotions and physical state as a hazy swirl of color around their body.  This makes it much easier to get them to do what you want.\n"
"\n"
"This power <color_yellow>is maintained by concentration</color> and <color_red>may fail</color> if <color_yellow>concentration is interrupted</color>.  It is <color_red>canceled by engaging in combat</color>.\n"
"\n"
"Level 6 leads to Psychometry with Aura Sight 6 OR Speed Reader 8 OR Premonition 8."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/clairsentience.json
msgid "[Ψ]Radiation Sense"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Radiation Sense
#: ./spells/clairsentience.json
msgid "You can open your tenses to the tell-tale glow of radiation."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/clairsentience.json
msgid "[Ψ]Marksman's Eye (C)"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Marksman's Eye (C)
#: ./spells/clairsentience.json
msgid ""
"With your enhanced senses, you can increase the effective range and accuracy of your ranged attacks.\n"
"\n"
"This power <color_yellow>is maintained by concentration</color> and <color_red>may fail</color> if <color_yellow>concentration is interrupted</color>.\n"
"\n"
"Level 9 leads to One Perfect Shot.\n"
"Level 7 leads to Prescient Tactician with Clarity 5 + Combat Sense 8."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/clairsentience.json ./spells/psychic_knacks.json
msgid "[Ψ]Psychometry"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Psychometry
#: ./spells/clairsentience.json ./spells/psychic_knacks.json
msgid ""
"Close your hand around an object and read the impressions left by whoever carried it before you.  At first you catch only a <color_light_green>feeling and a fragment</color> of what they lived through; with practice you learn <color_light_green>who they were</color>, and in time <color_light_green>what they feared and how it ended</color>.  The same object always tells the same story, and what you learn is written into its note.  Things you made, or have carried since the start, hold only you.\n"
"\n"
"Artifacts answer differently: you sense their hidden properties instead."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/clairsentience.json
msgid "[Ψ]Clairvoyance"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Clairvoyance
#: ./spells/clairsentience.json
msgid ""
"The classic example of a clairsentient's powers, you can see through walls and reveal everything nearby.\n"
"\n"
"Level 6 leads to Combat Sense with Premonition 10.\n"
"Level 14 leads to Omniscence with Clarity 5 + Satellite View 8 OR Clairvoyance 14 + Clarity 5.\n"
"Level 8 leads to Satellite View."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/clairsentience.json
msgid "[Ψ]Combat Sense (C)"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Combat Sense (C)
#: ./spells/clairsentience.json
msgid ""
"By gazing just a few moments into the future, you can be wherever your enemies are not attacking.\n"
"\n"
"This power <color_yellow>is maintained by concentration</color> and <color_red>may fail</color> if <color_yellow>concentration is interrupted</color>.\n"
"\n"
"Level 8 leads to Prescient Tactician with Clarity 5 + Marksman's Eye 7."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/clairsentience.json
msgid "[Ψ]Intuitive Artisan (C)"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Intuitive Artisan (C)
#: ./spells/clairsentience.json
msgid ""
"Opening yourself up to the immediate future, you can see the best option to take when crafting or working on a task.  However, due to the intensity of the visions you will be <color_red>blind</color> to the outside world while crafting anything.\n"
"\n"
"This power <color_yellow>is maintained by concentration</color> and <color_red>may fail</color> if <color_yellow>concentration is interrupted</color>.  It is <color_red>canceled by engaging in combat</color>."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/clairsentience.json
msgid "[Ψ]One Perfect Shot"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]One Perfect Shot
#: ./spells/clairsentience.json
msgid ""
"Gaze into the future and, taking your enemy's future movements into account,"
" fire at the perfect moment.  This power will only last for a single attack."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Message for SPELL '[Ψ]One Perfect Shot'
#: ./spells/clairsentience.json
msgid "It's time to take the shot."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/clairsentience.json
msgid "[Ψ]Satellite View"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Satellite View
#: ./spells/clairsentience.json
msgid ""
"You can extend your senses over the landscape, becoming aware of every hill, building, and valley within a large area.\n"
"\n"
"Level 8 leads to Omniscence with Clarity 5 + Satellite View 8 OR Clairvoyance 14 + Clarity 5."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Message for SPELL '[Ψ]Satellite View'
#: ./spells/clairsentience.json
msgid ""
"You close your eyes and concentrate, and you can see the landscape spread "
"out as though you were a bird on the wing."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/clairsentience.json
msgid "[Ψ]Clarity (C)"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Clarity (C)
#: ./spells/clairsentience.json
msgid ""
"Thanks to your powers, nothing can stop you from seeing the world as it is.\n"
"\n"
"This power <color_yellow>is maintained by concentration</color> and <color_red>may fail</color> if <color_yellow>concentration is interrupted</color>.\n"
"\n"
"Level 5 leads to Omniscence with Clarity 5 + Satellite View 8 OR Clairvoyance 14 + Clarity 5.\n"
"Level 5 leads to Prescient Tactician with Combat Sense 8 + Marksman's Eye 7."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/clairsentience.json
msgid "[Ψ]Prescient Tactician (C)"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Prescient Tactician (C)
#: ./spells/clairsentience.json
msgid ""
"Gazing into the near future, you can call out warnings to your followers so they can avoid attacks before they occur.  This will greatly increase their defensive capability, though it will be harder for you to defend yourself.\n"
"\n"
"This power <color_yellow>is maintained by concentration</color> and <color_red>may fail</color> if <color_yellow>concentration is interrupted</color>.  It requires <color_yellow>even more concentration</color> than usual."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/clairsentience.json
msgid "[Ψ]Omniscence"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Omniscence
#: ./spells/clairsentience.json
msgid ""
"Extend your senses to a supernal degree, perceiving everything within the "
"nearby area.  Every creature, every object, every blade of grass, "
"everything.  <color_red>EVERYTHING</color>."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/classless.json
msgid "[Ψ]Stop Concentrating"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Stop Concentrating
#: ./spells/classless.json
msgid ""
"End your concentration on all of your maintained powers.\n"
"\n"
"Channeling this power <color_green>always succeeds</color>."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Message for SPELL '[Ψ]Stop Concentrating'
#: ./spells/classless.json
msgid "You stop concentrating on your powers."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/classless.json
msgid "[Ψ]Stop Concentrating (Individual)"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Stop Concentrating (Individual)
#: ./spells/classless.json
msgid ""
"End your concentration on a specific power.\n"
"\n"
"Channeling this power <color_green>always succeeds</color>."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Message for SPELL '[Ψ]Stop Concentrating (Individual)'
#: ./spells/classless.json
msgid "You stop concentrating on one of your powers."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/electrokinesis.json ./spells/psychic_knacks.json
msgid "[Ψ]Spark Sight (C)"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Spark Sight (C)
#: ./spells/electrokinesis.json
msgid ""
"Open your senses to the flow of electricity, revealing nearby electrical creatures or robots.\n"
"\n"
"This power <color_yellow>is maintained by concentration</color> and <color_red>may fail</color> if <color_yellow>concentration is interrupted</color>.\n"
"\n"
"Level 3 leads to Circuit Sense.\n"
"Level 5 leads to Electron Overflow with Electrical Discharge 8.\n"
"Level 4 leads to Hacking Interface with Electron Overflow 4.\n"
"Level 6 leads to Neural Spasms.\n"
"Level 5 leads to Neuro-acceleration with Electrical Discharge 8 + Electron Overflow 11 OR Electron Overflow 11 + Spark Sight 5 OR Electrical Discharge 8 + Neural Spasms 6 OR Neural Spasms 6 + Spark Sight 5.\n"
"Level 8 leads to Pain Suppression with Neural Spasms 4 OR Electrical Discharge 8 + Spark Sight 8.\n"
"Level 12 leads to Robotic Interface with Hacking Interface 8 + Short Circuit 8.\n"
"Level 8 leads to Short Circuit."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/electrokinesis.json
msgid "[Ψ]Electrical Discharge (C)"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Electrical Discharge (C)
#: ./spells/electrokinesis.json
msgid ""
"Build up a charge in your body, zapping anyone who attempts to attack you.  It will also protect you from EMP attacks.\n"
"\n"
"This power <color_yellow>is maintained by concentration</color> and <color_red>may fail</color> if <color_yellow>concentration is interrupted</color>.\n"
"\n"
"Level 8 leads to Electrocutioner.\n"
"Level 8 leads to Electron Overflow with Spark Sight 5.\n"
"Level 12 leads to Galvanic Aura.\n"
"Level 8 leads to Neuro-acceleration with Electrical Discharge 8 + Electron Overflow 11 OR Electron Overflow 11 + Spark Sight 5 OR Electrical Discharge 8 + Neural Spasms 6 OR Neural Spasms 6 + Spark Sight 5.\n"
"Level 8 leads to Pain Suppression with Neural Spasms 4 OR Electrical Discharge 8 + Spark Sight 8."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/electrokinesis.json ./spells/psychic_knacks.json
msgid "[Ψ]Hacking Interface (C)"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Hacking Interface (C)
#: ./spells/electrokinesis.json
msgid ""
"Create an electrical interface with your powers, allowing you to hack nearby devices as if you were using a computer.\n"
"\n"
"This power <color_yellow>is maintained by concentration</color> and <color_red>may fail</color> if <color_yellow>concentration is interrupted</color>.\n"
"\n"
"Level 8 leads to Robotic Interface with Short Circuit 8 + Spark Sight 12."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/electrokinesis.json
msgid "[Ψ]Electron Overflow (C)"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Electron Overflow (C)
#: ./spells/electrokinesis.json
msgid ""
"Generate power for battery-powered devices on your person.\n"
"\n"
"This power <color_yellow>is maintained by concentration</color> and <color_red>may fail</color> if <color_yellow>concentration is interrupted</color>.\n"
"\n"
"Level 4 leads to Hacking Interface with Spark Sight 4.\n"
"Level 11 leads to Neuro-acceleration with Electrical Discharge 8 + Electron Overflow 11 OR Electron Overflow 11 + Spark Sight 5 OR Electrical Discharge 8 + Neural Spasms 6 OR Neural Spasms 6 + Spark Sight 5."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/electrokinesis.json
msgid "[Ψ]Neural Spasms"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Neural Spasms
#: ./spells/electrokinesis.json
msgid ""
"Cause an electrical burst in the target's nervous system (or the remains of it), incapacitating them briefly.  It will only work on targets that have, or had, a nervous system.\n"
"\n"
"Level 6 leads to Neuro-acceleration with Electrical Discharge 8 + Electron Overflow 11 OR Electron Overflow 11 + Spark Sight 5 OR Electrical Discharge 8 + Neural Spasms 6 OR Neural Spasms 6 + Spark Sight 5.\n"
"Level 4 leads to Pain Suppression with Neural Spasms 4 OR Electrical Discharge 8 + Spark Sight 8."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/electrokinesis.json
msgid "[Ψ]Pain Suppression (C)"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Pain Suppression (C)
#: ./spells/electrokinesis.json
msgid ""
"With your control over electricity, reduce the strength of the pain signals in your own body.\n"
"\n"
"This power <color_yellow>is maintained by concentration</color> and <color_red>may fail</color> if <color_yellow>concentration is interrupted</color>.\n"
"\n"
"Level 9 leads to Analgesic Block.\n"
"Level 13 leads to Revivification with Neuro-acceleration 8 + Pain Suppression 13 OR Analgesic Block 6 + Neuro-acceleration 8."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/electrokinesis.json
msgid "[Ψ]Electrocutioner"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Electrocutioner
#: ./spells/electrokinesis.json
msgid ""
"Launch a bolt of lightning at a nearby target.\n"
"\n"
"Level 10 leads to Ion Blast with Short Circuit 6 OR Electrocutioner 10."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for the sound of spell '[Ψ]Electrocutioner'
#. ~ Description for the sound of spell '{'str': '[Ψ]Short Circuit Lightning
#. Burst', '//~': 'NO_I18N'}'
#. ~ Description for the sound of spell '[Ψ]Ion Blast'
#: ./spells/electrokinesis.json
msgid "zzzzaaaaaapp!"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Message for SPELL '[Ψ]Electrocutioner'
#: ./spells/electrokinesis.json
msgid "You unleash a bolt of lightning."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/electrokinesis.json ./spells/psychic_knacks.json
msgid "[Ψ]Analgesic Block"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Analgesic Block
#: ./spells/electrokinesis.json
msgid ""
"By clamping down on all pain signals you can completely eliminate your ability to feel pain briefly.  This does not eliminate the source of pain, and when the power ends all of the original pain and more will return.\n"
"\n"
"Analgesic Block is <color_red>incompatible</color> with Neuro-Acceleration.\n"
"\n"
"Level 6 leads to Revivification with Neuro-acceleration 8 + Pain Suppression 13 OR Analgesic Block 6 + Neuro-acceleration 8."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Message for SPELL '[Ψ]Analgesic Block'
#: ./spells/electrokinesis.json ./spells/psychic_knacks.json
msgid "The pain just… disappears."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/electrokinesis.json
msgid "[Ψ]Neuro-acceleration"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Neuro-acceleration
#: ./spells/electrokinesis.json
msgid ""
"You can improve the efficiency of your or an ally's nervous system, allowing for much faster response times.  This also increases the target's ability to retain information.\n"
"\n"
"This power <color_yellow>is maintained by concentration</color> and <color_red>may fail</color> if <color_yellow>concentration is interrupted</color>.  Neuro-acceleration is <color_red>incompatible</color> with Analgesic Block.  When used on <color_green>allies</color>, the power has <color_yellow>one-half the normal duration</color>.\n"
"\n"
"Level 8 leads to Revivification with Neuro-acceleration 8 + Pain Suppression 13 OR Analgesic Block 6 + Neuro-acceleration 8."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/electrokinesis.json
msgid "[Ψ]Short Circuit"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Short Circuit
#: ./spells/electrokinesis.json
msgid ""
"Cause a massive power surge within a robot or cyborg, disabling it.\n"
"\n"
"Level 6 leads to Ion Blast with Short Circuit 6 OR Electrocutioner 10.\n"
"Level 8 leads to Robotic Interface with Hacking Interface 8 + Spark Sight 12."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Message for SPELL '[Ψ]Short Circuit'
#: ./spells/electrokinesis.json
msgid "You channel a surge of power into your target!"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Robotic Interface
#: ./spells/electrokinesis.json
msgid ""
"Use your powers to remotely interface with a robot's internal circuitry, "
"allowing you to hack it if you have the skill."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/electrokinesis.json
msgid "[Ψ]Galvanic Aura (C)"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Galvanic Aura (C)
#: ./spells/electrokinesis.json
msgid ""
"Charge the air around you with power, unleashing blasts at anyone nearby.  This power does not discriminate between friend and foe.  It will also protect you from electricity while active.\n"
"\n"
"This power <color_yellow>is maintained by concentration</color> and <color_red>may fail</color> if <color_yellow>concentration is interrupted</color>"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Message for SPELL '[Ψ]Galvanic Aura (C)'
#: ./spells/electrokinesis.json
msgid "The air around you hums with power."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/electrokinesis.json
msgid "[Ψ]Ion Blast"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Ion Blast
#: ./spells/electrokinesis.json
msgid ""
"Launch a blast of lightning at a nearby target, causing a secondary "
"explosion at the location."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Message for SPELL '[Ψ]Ion Blast'
#: ./spells/electrokinesis.json
msgid "You unleash an explosive blast of lightning."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/electrokinesis.json
msgid "[Ψ]Revivification"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Revivification
#: ./spells/electrokinesis.json
msgid ""
"Manipulate the nervous system of a corpse, causing it to rise and protect "
"you.  This protection will only last a short time."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Message for SPELL '[Ψ]Revivification'
#: ./spells/electrokinesis.json
msgid "You charge a nearby corpse with lightning."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/photokinesis.json
msgid "[Ψ]Candle's Glow (C)"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Candle's Glow (C)
#: ./spells/photokinesis.json
msgid ""
"Create a simple patch of light nearby, sufficient to read or perform simple tasks with.\n"
"\n"
"This power <color_yellow>is maintained by concentration</color> and <color_red>may fail</color> if <color_yellow>concentration is interrupted</color>.  It is <color_red>canceled by engaging in combat</color>.\n"
"\n"
"Level 5 leads to Blackout with Candle's Glow 5 OR Field of Light 4.\n"
"Level 8 leads to Photon Beam with Candle's Glow 8 OR Field of Light 6.\n"
"Level 6 leads to Refracted Arms with Chameleoflage 6 + Trick of the Light 8."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/photokinesis.json
msgid "[Ψ]Field of Light"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Field of Light
#: ./spells/photokinesis.json
msgid ""
"Create photons to illuminate an entire area.\n"
"\n"
"Level 4 leads to Blackout with Candle's Glow 5 OR Field of Light 4.\n"
"Level 12 leads to Blinding Radiance with Field of Light 12 + Star Flash 6 OR Field of Light 12 + Lucent Barrier 10 OR Flashbang 7 + Star Flash 6 OR Flashbang 7 + Lucent Barrier 10.\n"
"Level 9 leads to Flashbang with Field of Light 9 + Illuminate 6 OR Illuminate 6 + Photon Beam 5.\n"
"Level 14 leads to Phantom Legion with Field of Light 14 + Lucid Shadows 10 OR Lucid Shadows 10 + Refracted Arms 10 OR Blinding Radiance 6 + Lucid Shadows 10.\n"
"Level 6 leads to Photon Beam with Candle's Glow 8 OR Field of Light 6.\n"
"Level 8 leads to Radio Transception with Field of Light 8 + Lucent Barrier 6 OR Lucent Barrier 6 + Photon Beam 7.\n"
"Level 5 leads to Trick of the Light with Blackout 5."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Message for SPELL '[Ψ]Field of Light'
#: ./spells/photokinesis.json
msgid "Sudden light bursts forth!"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Field of Light
#: ./spells/photokinesis.json
msgid "Create photons to illuminate an entire area."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/photokinesis.json
msgid "[Ψ]Illuminate"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Illuminate
#: ./spells/photokinesis.json
msgid ""
"Surround a single target with a outline of line that follows them as they move, revealing their position at all times.\n"
"\n"
"Level 6 leads to Flashbang with Field of Light 9 + Illuminate 6 OR Illuminate 6 + Photon Beam 5.\n"
"Level 9 leads to Gamma Sterilization with Chameleoflage 4 + Lucent Barrier 7 + Star Flash 3 OR Chameleoflage 4 + Illuminate 9 + Lucent Barrier 7 OR Chameleoflage 4 + Lucent Barrier 7 + Photon Beam 5."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Message for SPELL '[Ψ]Illuminate'
#: ./spells/photokinesis.json
msgid "Your target is outlined in light."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/photokinesis.json
msgid "[Ψ]Blackout"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Blackout
#: ./spells/photokinesis.json
msgid ""
"Interrupt the flow of photons to create an area of darkness.\n"
"\n"
"Level 6 leads to Lucent Barrier with Trick of the Light 9 OR Blackout 6 + Chameleoflage 5.\n"
"Level 5 leads to Trick of the Light with Field of Light 5."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Message for SPELL '[Ψ]Blackout'
#: ./spells/photokinesis.json
msgid "As you concentrate, an area nearby is plunged into darkness!"
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/photokinesis.json
msgid "[Ψ]Trick of the Light (C)"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Trick of the Light (C)
#: ./spells/photokinesis.json
msgid ""
"Manipulate the light around your body, creating shifting illusions, blurring your outline and position, and becoming harder to hit.  An enemy successfully hitting you will pinpoint your location and <color_red>disrupt the power</color>.\n"
"\n"
"his power <color_yellow>is maintained by concentration</color> and <color_red>may fail</color> if <color_yellow>concentration is interrupted</color>.\n"
"\n"
"Level 6 leads to Chameleoflage.\n"
"Level 9 leads to Lucent Barrier with Trick of the Light 9 OR Blackout 6 + Chameleoflage 5.\n"
"Level 8 leads to Refracted Arms with Candle's Glow 6 + Chameleoflage 6."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/photokinesis.json
msgid "[Ψ]Photon Beam"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Photon Beam
#: ./spells/photokinesis.json
msgid ""
"Concentrate photons into a high-energy beam.\n"
"\n"
"Level 5 leads to Flashbang with Field of Light 9 + Illuminate 6 OR Illuminate 6 + Photon Beam 5.\n"
"Level 5 leads to Gamma Sterilization with Chameleoflage 4 + Lucent Barrier 7 + Star Flash 3 OR Chameleoflage 4 + Illuminate 9 + Lucent Barrier 7 OR Chameleoflage 4 + Lucent Barrier 7 + Photon Beam 5.\n"
"Level 6 leads to Lucid Shadows with Chameleoflage 6 + Photon Beam 6 OR Photon Beam 6 + Refracted Arms 6.\n"
"Level 14 leads to Luminous Disintegration with Blinding Radiance 5 + Star Flash 8 OR Blinding Radiance 5 + Photon Beam 14.\n"
"Level 7 leads to Radio Transception with Field of Light 8 + Lucent Barrier 6 OR Lucent Barrier 6 + Photon Beam 7.\n"
"Level 4 leads to Sensor Jamming with Star Flash 5 OR Photon Beam 4 + Radio Transception 6.\n"
"Level 8 leads to Star Flash with Lucent Barrier 6 + Photon Beam 8 OR Photon Beam 8 + Refracted Arms 6."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Message for SPELL '[Ψ]Photon Beam'
#: ./spells/photokinesis.json
msgid "You fire a searing beam of light!"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Combination of chameleon and camouflage
#: ./spells/photokinesis.json ./spells/psychic_knacks.json
msgid "[Ψ]Chameleoflage (C)"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for {'//~': 'Combination of chameleon and camouflage', 'str':
#. '[Ψ]Chameleoflage (C)'}
#: ./spells/photokinesis.json
msgid ""
"By blending the light reflecting from you with the light reflecting from nearby surfaces, you can make yourself much harder to spot from a distance.\n"
"\n"
"This power <color_yellow>is maintained by concentration</color> and <color_red>may fail</color> if <color_yellow>concentration is interrupted</color>.\n"
"\n"
"Level 4 leads to Gamma Sterilization with Chameleoflage 4 + Lucent Barrier 7 + Star Flash 3 OR Chameleoflage 4 + Illuminate 9 + Lucent Barrier 7 OR Chameleoflage 4 + Lucent Barrier 7 + Photon Beam 5.\n"
"Level 5 leads to Lucent Barrier with Trick of the Light 9 OR Blackout 6 + Chameleoflage 5.\n"
"Level 6 leads to Lucid Shadows with Chameleoflage 6 + Photon Beam 6 OR Photon Beam 6 + Refracted Arms 6.\n"
"Level 8 leads to Mirror-Mask with Lucent Barrier 5.\n"
"Level 6 leads to Refracted Arms with Candle's Glow 6 + Trick of the Light 8.\n"
"Level 10 leads to Veil of Light with Chameleoflage 10 + Lucent Barrier 6 OR Lucent Barrier 6 + Mirror-Mask 6 OR Chameleoflage 10 + Lucid Shadows 6 OR Lucid Shadows 6 + Mirror-Mask 6."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/photokinesis.json
msgid "[Ψ]Lucent Barrier (C)"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Lucent Barrier (C)
#: ./spells/photokinesis.json
msgid ""
"Create a barrier of light around yourself to protect against radiation and light damage.\n"
"\n"
"This power <color_yellow>is maintained by concentration</color> and <color_red>may fail</color> if <color_yellow>concentration is interrupted</color>.\n"
"\n"
"Level 10 leads to Blinding Radiance with Field of Light 12 + Star Flash 6 OR Field of Light 12 + Lucent Barrier 10 OR Flashbang 7 + Star Flash 6 OR Flashbang 7 + Lucent Barrier 10.\n"
"Level 7 leads to Gamma Sterilization with Chameleoflage 4 + Lucent Barrier 7 + Star Flash 3 OR Chameleoflage 4 + Illuminate 9 + Lucent Barrier 7 OR Chameleoflage 4 + Lucent Barrier 7 + Photon Beam 5.\n"
"Level 5 leads to Mirror-Mask with Chameleoflage 8.\n"
"Level 6 leads to Radio Transception with Field of Light 8 + Lucent Barrier 6 OR Lucent Barrier 6 + Photon Beam 7.\n"
"Level 6 leads to Star Flash with Lucent Barrier 6 + Photon Beam 8 OR Photon Beam 8 + Refracted Arms 6.\n"
"Level 6 leads to Veil of Light with Chameleoflage 10 + Lucent Barrier 6 OR Lucent Barrier 6 + Mirror-Mask 6 OR Chameleoflage 10 + Lucid Shadows 6 OR Lucid Shadows 6 + Mirror-Mask 6."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/photokinesis.json
msgid "[Ψ]Refracted Arms"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Refracted Arms
#: ./spells/photokinesis.json
msgid ""
"Create the illusion of extra arms and wielded items to trick your enemies, forcing them off balance and rendering them open to attack.\n"
"\n"
"Level 6 leads to Lucid Shadows with Chameleoflage 6 + Photon Beam 6 OR Photon Beam 6 + Refracted Arms 6.\n"
"Level 10 leads to Phantom Legion with Field of Light 14 + Lucid Shadows 10 OR Lucid Shadows 10 + Refracted Arms 10 OR Blinding Radiance 6 + Lucid Shadows 10.\n"
"Level 6 leads to Star Flash with Lucent Barrier 6 + Photon Beam 8 OR Photon Beam 8 + Refracted Arms 6."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Message for SPELL '[Ψ]Refracted Arms'
#: ./spells/photokinesis.json
msgid ""
"Light around your arms shimmers and refracts, creating the illusion of "
"multiple arms."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/photokinesis.json ./spells/psychic_knacks.json
msgid "[Ψ]Mirror-Mask (C)"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Mirror-Mask (C)
#: ./spells/photokinesis.json
msgid ""
"Hide your true form behind unassuming illusions, preventing baseline humans from reacting poorly to your presence if you are mutated or a cyborg.\n"
"\n"
"This power <color_yellow>is maintained by concentration</color> and <color_red>may fail</color> if <color_yellow>concentration is interrupted</color>.  It is <color_red>canceled by engaging in combat</color>.\n"
"\n"
"Level 6 leads to Veil of Light with Chameleoflage 10 + Lucent Barrier 6 OR Lucent Barrier 6 + Mirror-Mask 6 OR Chameleoflage 10 + Lucid Shadows 6 OR Lucid Shadows 6 + Mirror-Mask 6."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/photokinesis.json
msgid "[Ψ]Flashbang"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Flashbang
#: ./spells/photokinesis.json
msgid ""
"Create a concentration of photons and EM radiation and then allow them to burst outward, creating a bright flash of light accompanied by a loud sound, producing a flashbang effect.\n"
"\n"
"Level 7 leads to Blinding Radiance with Field of Light 12 + Star Flash 6 OR Field of Light 12 + Lucent Barrier 10 OR Flashbang 7 + Star Flash 6 OR Flashbang 7 + Lucent Barrier 10."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Message for SPELL '[Ψ]Flashbang'
#: ./spells/photokinesis.json
msgid "The air bursts into a eye-searing flash accompanied by a loud bang!"
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/photokinesis.json
msgid "[Ψ]Lucid Shadows"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Lucid Shadows
#: ./spells/photokinesis.json
msgid ""
"Form images of yourself to confuse and distract enemies.\n"
"\n"
"Level 10 leads to Phantom Legion with Field of Light 14 + Lucid Shadows 10 OR Lucid Shadows 10 + Refracted Arms 10 OR Blinding Radiance 6 + Lucid Shadows 10.\n"
"Level 6 leads to Veil of Light with Chameleoflage 10 + Lucent Barrier 6 OR Lucent Barrier 6 + Mirror-Mask 6 OR Chameleoflage 10 + Lucid Shadows 6 OR Lucid Shadows 6 + Mirror-Mask 6."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Message for SPELL '[Ψ]Lucid Shadows'
#: ./spells/photokinesis.json
msgid "Identical copies of you suddenly appear!"
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/photokinesis.json ./spells/psychic_knacks.json
msgid "[Ψ]Radio Transception (C)"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Radio Transception (C)
#: ./spells/photokinesis.json
msgid ""
"Attune your senses to radio waves, allowing you to listen to transmissions and send them yourself.\n"
"\n"
"This power <color_yellow>is maintained by concentration</color> and <color_red>may fail</color> if <color_yellow>concentration is interrupted</color>.  It is <color_red>canceled by engaging in combat</color>.\n"
"\n"
"Level 6 leads to Sensor Jamming with Star Flash 5 OR Photon Beam 4 + Radio Transception 6."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/photokinesis.json
msgid "[Ψ]Gamma Sterilization"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Gamma Sterilization
#: ./spells/photokinesis.json
msgid ""
"Use a focused emission of high-power radiation to eliminating microorganisms"
" in food and allowing it to last much longer before rotting.  This power is "
"<color_red>extremely taxing</color>."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/photokinesis.json
msgid "[Ψ]Sensor Jamming"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Sensor Jamming
#: ./spells/photokinesis.json
msgid ""
"Unleash a localized burst of electromagnetic radiation, overloading any "
"electronic sensory equipment in the area."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Message for SPELL '[Ψ]Sensor Jamming'
#: ./spells/photokinesis.json
msgid "You unleash an electromagnetic wave!"
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/photokinesis.json
msgid "[Ψ]Veil of Light (C)"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Veil of Light (C)
#: ./spells/photokinesis.json
msgid ""
"Refract light around yourself to become invisible.  Moving too quickly has a chance to disrupt the effect, and attacking in melee will invariably do so.\n"
"\n"
"This power <color_yellow>is maintained by concentration</color> and <color_red>may fail</color> if <color_yellow>concentration is interrupted</color>."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/photokinesis.json
msgid "[Ψ]Star Flash"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Star Flash
#: ./spells/photokinesis.json
msgid ""
"Create a destructive flash of light in a line, damaging all targets caught in the beam.\n"
"\n"
"Level 6 leads to Blinding Radiance with Field of Light 12 + Star Flash 6 OR Field of Light 12 + Lucent Barrier 10 OR Flashbang 7 + Star Flash 6 OR Flashbang 7 + Lucent Barrier 10.\n"
"Level 3 leads to Gamma Sterilization with Chameleoflage 4 + Lucent Barrier 7 + Star Flash 3 OR Chameleoflage 4 + Illuminate 9 + Lucent Barrier 7 OR Chameleoflage 4 + Lucent Barrier 7 + Photon Beam 5.\n"
"Level 8 leads to Luminous Disintegration with Blinding Radiance 5 + Star Flash 8 OR Blinding Radiance 5 + Photon Beam 14.\n"
"Level 5 leads to Sensor Jamming with Star Flash 5 OR Photon Beam 4 + Radio Transception 6."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Message for SPELL '[Ψ]Star Flash'
#: ./spells/photokinesis.json
msgid "You fire a searing wave of light!"
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/photokinesis.json
msgid "[Ψ]Blinding Radiance (C)"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Blinding Radiance (C)
#: ./spells/photokinesis.json
msgid ""
"You can emit so much light that anyone trying to attack you risks being blinded.\n"
"\n"
"This power <color_yellow>is maintained by concentration</color> and <color_red>may fail</color> if <color_yellow>concentration is interrupted</color>.\n"
"\n"
"Level 5 leads to Luminous Disintegration with Blinding Radiance 5 + Star Flash 8 OR Blinding Radiance 5 + Photon Beam 14.\n"
"Level 6 leads to Phantom Legion with Field of Light 14 + Lucid Shadows 10 OR Lucid Shadows 10 + Refracted Arms 10 OR Blinding Radiance 6 + Lucid Shadows 10."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/photokinesis.json
msgid "[Ψ]Luminous Disintegration"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Luminous Disintegration
#: ./spells/photokinesis.json
msgid ""
"Concentrate a massive amount of light into a single target, causing it to "
"disintegrate."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Message for SPELL '[Ψ]Luminous Disintegration'
#: ./spells/photokinesis.json
msgid "You focus a pointpoint burst of light on your target!"
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/photokinesis.json
msgid "[Ψ]Phantom Legion (C)"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Phantom Legion (C)
#: ./spells/photokinesis.json
msgid ""
"Create a myriad of illusions around yourself to mislead and confuse your enemies.  The illusions will explode into blinding flashes if damaged.\n"
"\n"
"This power <color_yellow>is maintained by concentration</color> and <color_red>may fail</color> if <color_yellow>concentration is interrupted</color>.  It requires <color_yellow>even more concentration</color> than usual.  Concentration will <color_green>automatically end</color> if all illusions are destroyed."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Adrenaline Trigger
#: ./spells/psychic_knacks.json
msgid ""
"With a moment of concentration, you can trigger a surge of adrenaline.  This"
" provides a speed boost, albeit at a draining cost when the boost expires."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Heightened Senses (C)
#: ./spells/psychic_knacks.json
msgid ""
"All of your senses are heightened, allowing you to see further and hear better, and at higher levels even see in murky water or use minor vibrations and small sounds to determine moving creatures nearby.\n"
"\n"
"This power <color_yellow>is maintained by concentration</color> and <color_red>may fail</color> if <color_yellow>concentration is interrupted</color>."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Premonition (C)
#: ./spells/psychic_knacks.json
msgid ""
"You can sense nearby movement and sometimes gain an advance warning of dangerous events.\n"
"\n"
"This power <color_yellow>is maintained by concentration</color> and <color_red>may fail</color> if <color_yellow>concentration is interrupted</color>."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Spark Sight (C)
#: ./spells/psychic_knacks.json
msgid ""
"Open your senses to the flow of electricity, revealing nearby electrical creatures or robots.\n"
"\n"
"This power <color_yellow>is maintained by concentration</color> and <color_red>may fail</color> if <color_yellow>concentration is interrupted</color>."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Analgesic Block
#: ./spells/psychic_knacks.json
msgid ""
"By clamping down on all pain signals you can completely eliminate your ability to feel pain briefly.  This does not eliminate the source of pain, and when the power ends all of the original pain and more will return.\n"
"\n"
"Analgesic Block is <color_red>incompatible</color> with Neuro-Acceleration."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Hacking Interface (C)
#: ./spells/psychic_knacks.json
msgid ""
"Create an electrical interface with your powers, allowing you to hack nearby devices as if you were using a computer.\n"
"\n"
"This power <color_yellow>is maintained by concentration</color> and <color_red>may fail</color> if <color_yellow>concentration is interrupted</color>."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for {'//~': 'Combination of chameleon and camouflage', 'str':
#. '[Ψ]Chameleoflage (C)'}
#: ./spells/psychic_knacks.json
msgid ""
"By blending the light reflecting from you with the light reflecting from nearby surfaces, you can make yourself much harder to spot from a distance.\n"
"\n"
"This power <color_yellow>is maintained by concentration</color> and <color_red>may fail</color> if <color_yellow>concentration is interrupted</color>."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Mirror-Mask (C)
#: ./spells/psychic_knacks.json
msgid ""
"Hide your true form behind unassuming illusions, preventing baseline humans from reacting poorly to your presence if you are mutated or a cyborg.\n"
"\n"
"This power <color_yellow>is maintained by concentration</color> and <color_red>may fail</color> if <color_yellow>concentration is interrupted</color>.  It is <color_red>canceled by engaging in combat</color>."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Radio Transception (C)
#: ./spells/psychic_knacks.json
msgid ""
"Attune your senses to radio waves, allowing you to listen to transmissions and send them yourself.\n"
"\n"
"This power <color_yellow>is maintained by concentration</color> and <color_red>may fail</color> if <color_yellow>concentration is interrupted</color>.  It is <color_red>canceled by engaging in combat</color>."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/psychic_knacks.json ./spells/pyrokinesis.json
msgid "[Ψ]Brilliant Flash"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Brilliant Flash
#: ./spells/psychic_knacks.json
msgid ""
"By strongly exciting the air at a particular point, you produce a burst of "
"light."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/psychic_knacks.json ./spells/pyrokinesis.json
msgid "[Ψ]Intensify Flames"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Intensify Flames
#: ./spells/psychic_knacks.json
msgid ""
"Manipulate an existing fire, increasing its heat.  This can turn small "
"flames into raging conflagrations or spread fire through the area.  If used "
"on a target that is on fire, the increased flames will cause additional "
"damage."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/psychic_knacks.json ./spells/pyrokinesis.json
msgid "[Ψ]Molten Land"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Molten Land
#: ./spells/psychic_knacks.json
msgid ""
"You reach into the ground and unmake it, pouring your will into the stone until it runs like water.  A single tile of <color_light_green>ground</color> -- soil, sand, rock, pavement, flooring, or the low growth on top of it -- becomes a pool of <color_red>molten lava</color>.\n"
"\n"
"<color_yellow>This does not touch walls, doors, windows or fences.</color>  It melts the land, not what is built on it.\n"
"\n"
"<color_red>The lava is permanent.</color>  It will not cool, and anything that steps into it is grievously burned.  Be certain before you unmake the floor you are standing near."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for the sound of spell '[Ψ]Molten Land'
#: ./spells/psychic_knacks.json ./spells/pyrokinesis.json
msgid "a deep, grinding roar!"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Message for SPELL '[Ψ]Molten Land'
#: ./spells/psychic_knacks.json ./spells/pyrokinesis.json
msgid "The ground splits and runs molten!"
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/psychic_knacks.json ./spells/pyrokinesis.json
msgid "[Ψ]Banked Flames (C)"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Banked Flames (C)
#: ./spells/psychic_knacks.json
msgid ""
"Call up flames over your outstretched hand.  You can use them to heat up food, boil water, start fires, or anything else fire can accomplish.\n"
"\n"
"This power <color_yellow>is maintained by concentration</color> and <color_red>may fail</color> if <color_yellow>concentration is interrupted</color>.  It is <color_red>canceled by engaging in combat</color>."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/psychic_knacks.json ./spells/pyrokinesis.json
msgid "[Ψ]Cloak of Warmth (C)"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Cloak of Warmth (C)
#: ./spells/psychic_knacks.json
msgid ""
"Control the temperature of the nearby air, warming you and protecting you against flames.\n"
"\n"
"This power <color_yellow>is maintained by concentration</color> and <color_red>may fail</color> if <color_yellow>concentration is interrupted</color>."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/psychic_knacks.json ./spells/pyrokinesis.json
msgid "[Ψ]Flamethrower"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Flamethrower
#: ./spells/psychic_knacks.json
msgid "Spray fire in a cone in front of you."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for the sound of spell '[Ψ]Flamethrower'
#: ./spells/psychic_knacks.json ./spells/pyrokinesis.json
msgid "a crackle!"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Message for SPELL '[Ψ]Flamethrower'
#: ./spells/psychic_knacks.json ./spells/pyrokinesis.json
msgid "You hurl a spray of flames."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/psychic_knacks.json ./spells/pyrokinesis.json
msgid "[Ψ]Blazing Aura (C)"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Blazing Aura (C)
#: ./spells/psychic_knacks.json
msgid ""
"Surround yourself with a cloud of flames, damaging anyone in melee combat with you.  The flames also produce light.\n"
"\n"
"This power <color_yellow>is maintained by concentration</color> and <color_red>may fail</color> if <color_yellow>concentration is interrupted</color>."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/psychic_knacks.json ./spells/pyrokinesis.json
msgid "[Ψ]Conflagration"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Conflagration
#: ./spells/psychic_knacks.json
msgid ""
"Create an expanding fireball that catches multiple targets in its wake."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for the sound of spell '[Ψ]Conflagration'
#. ~ Description for the sound of spell '[Ψ]Crucible'
#: ./spells/psychic_knacks.json ./spells/pyrokinesis.json
msgid "the roar of flames!"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Message for SPELL '[Ψ]Conflagration'
#: ./spells/psychic_knacks.json ./spells/pyrokinesis.json
msgid "You call forth a raging inferno!"
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/psychic_knacks.json ./spells/telekinesis.json
msgid "[Ψ]Far Hand"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Far Hand
#: ./spells/psychic_knacks.json
msgid "Pickup items at a distance or push them away from you."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/psychic_knacks.json ./spells/telekinesis.json
msgid "[Ψ]Force Shove"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Force Shove
#: ./spells/psychic_knacks.json
msgid ""
"Shove a target away or pull it towards you with a burst of psionic force.  "
"The distance the target can be moved depends on its weight versus your power"
" level; heavier things will not go as far, and if your target is too heavy, "
"you may not be able to move it at all."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/psychic_knacks.json ./spells/telekinesis.json
msgid "[Ψ]Knockdown"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Knockdown
#: ./spells/psychic_knacks.json
msgid ""
"Slam something to the ground with a burst of telekinetic force, doing a "
"small amount of damage and downing them."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Message for SPELL '[Ψ]Knockdown'
#: ./spells/psychic_knacks.json ./spells/telekinesis.json
msgid "Your target is knocked to the ground."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/psychic_knacks.json ./spells/telekinesis.json
msgid "[Ψ]Wave of Force"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Wave of Force
#: ./spells/psychic_knacks.json
msgid ""
"Unleash a telekinetic wave around you that indiscriminately knocks "
"everything back."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Message for SPELL '[Ψ]Wave of Force'
#: ./spells/psychic_knacks.json ./spells/telekinesis.json
msgid "You knock everything nearby backwards!"
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/psychic_knacks.json ./spells/telepathy.json
msgid "[Ψ]Telepathic Shield (C)"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Telepathic Shield (C)
#: ./spells/psychic_knacks.json
msgid ""
"You can protect your mind from the dangers of the post-Cataclysmic world.\n"
"\n"
"This power <color_yellow>is maintained by concentration</color> and <color_red>may fail</color> if <color_yellow>concentration is interrupted</color>."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/psychic_knacks.json ./spells/telepathy.json
msgid "[Ψ]Mind Sonar (C)"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Mind Sonar (C)
#: ./spells/psychic_knacks.json
msgid ""
"You cast your mind outward like a sonar pulse, sweeping the area for the minds of others.  While maintained, you periodically sense every <color_light_green>sapient mind</color> around you — people and other thinking things — and learn their <color_light_green>direction and distance</color>, even through walls and in total darkness.  You cannot see them, but you know they are there.  The <color_light_green>range grows</color> as you master the power, and greater mastery <color_light_green>quickens the pulse</color> and lets you pick out <color_light_green>familiar minds by name</color>.\n"
"\n"
"The walking dead, robots, and other <color_light_gray>mindless</color> things have no mind to sense.\n"
"\n"
"This power <color_yellow>is maintained by concentration</color> and <color_red>may fail</color> if <color_yellow>concentration is interrupted</color>."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/psychic_knacks.json ./spells/telepathy.json
msgid "[Ψ]Mood Stabilization (C)"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Mood Stabilization (C)
#: ./spells/psychic_knacks.json
msgid ""
"With the ability to edit others' thoughts comes the ability to edit your own, removing negative moods to a degree.  You have also learned to do this more subtly on others, calming their anger or assuaging their fears.\n"
"\n"
"When used on yourself, this power <color_yellow>is maintained by concentration</color> and <color_red>may fail</color> if <color_yellow>concentration is interrupted</color>."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/psychic_knacks.json ./spells/telepathy.json
msgid "[Ψ]Mesmerize"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Mesmerize
#: ./spells/psychic_knacks.json ./spells/telepathy.json
msgid ""
"Hypnotize a target, causing them to stand in a trance or wander around in a "
"small area.  Any damage taken will snap the target out of their trance.  "
"Some targets are more resistant to mesmerism than others."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/psychic_knacks.json ./spells/telepathy.json
msgid "[Ψ]Synaptic Overload"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Synaptic Overload
#: ./spells/psychic_knacks.json
msgid ""
"Short-circuit and overwhelm a target's brain, causing extreme damage or death.\n"
"\n"
"<color_yellow>This power needs a mind to seize hold of.</color>  The walking dead, robots, and other <color_light_gray>mindless</color> things have none, and are <color_light_gray>wholly unaffected</color>."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Message for SPELL '[Ψ]Synaptic Overload'
#: ./spells/psychic_knacks.json ./spells/telepathy.json
msgid "You assault the mind of your target!"
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/psychic_knacks.json ./spells/telepathy.json
msgid "[Ψ]Beastmaster"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Beastmaster
#: ./spells/psychic_knacks.json
msgid ""
"Take control of an animal's mind, forcing it to obey you.  This also works on feral humans.\n"
"\n"
"<color_yellow>This power needs a mind to seize hold of.</color>  The walking dead, robots, and other <color_light_gray>mindless</color> things have none, and are <color_light_gray>wholly unaffected</color>.\n"
"\n"
"<color_light_green>Pack Leader:</color> once you know this power, every pet you have deals <color_light_green>25%</color> more melee damage.  Pets fighting within 12 tiles of you also gain a compounding <color_light_green>15%</color> for each packmate beyond the first, counting up to 8 pets (x3.33 at 8).  Pets near you also hold their nerve and will not flee until badly wounded.  Pets that wander off will find their way back to your side.  Pets that stray too far break off their hunt and return.  Guns, psionic powers and a few hard-wired abilities are not boosted."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Message for SPELL '[Ψ]Beastmaster'
#: ./spells/psychic_knacks.json ./spells/telepathy.json
msgid "You reach out to the animal's mind and twist."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/psychic_knacks.json ./spells/telepathy.json
msgid "[Ψ]Obscurity"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Obscurity
#: ./spells/psychic_knacks.json
msgid ""
"Use a light touch on others' minds to hide your presence.  You will be invisible to the target(s) while the power is in effect.\n"
"\n"
"This power is <color_red>canceled by engaging in combat</color> with your target."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Message for SPELL '[Ψ]Obscurity'
#: ./spells/psychic_knacks.json ./spells/telepathy.json
msgid "You hide your presence from your enemies."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/psychic_knacks.json ./spells/telepathy.json
msgid "[Ψ]Psychic Scream"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Psychic Scream
#: ./spells/psychic_knacks.json
msgid ""
"Emit an uncontrolled psychic scream, attacking the mind of anyone nearby.  This power does not distinguish between friend and foe.\n"
"\n"
"<color_yellow>This power needs a mind to seize hold of.</color>  The walking dead, robots, and other <color_light_gray>mindless</color> things have none, and are <color_light_gray>wholly unaffected</color>."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Message for SPELL '[Ψ]Psychic Scream'
#: ./spells/psychic_knacks.json ./spells/telepathy.json
msgid "You unleash a mind-piercing psionic shriek!"
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/psychic_knacks.json ./spells/vitakinesis.json
msgid "[Ψ]Healthy Glow (C)"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Healthy Glow (C)
#: ./spells/psychic_knacks.json ./spells/vitakinesis.json
msgid ""
"Your powers can keep you in the bloom of health.  This can also stop or prevent an asthma attack.\n"
"\n"
"This power <color_yellow>is maintained by concentration</color> and <color_red>may fail</color> if <color_yellow>concentration is interrupted</color>.  Healthy Glow <color_red>cannot be active</color> with Leucocyte Acculumation"
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/psychic_knacks.json ./spells/vitakinesis.json
msgid "[Ψ]Detoxification"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Detoxification
#: ./spells/psychic_knacks.json
msgid ""
"When poisoned, you can isolate the poison and move it to your sweat glands "
"where you will harmlessly sweat it out.  While doing so, your flesh will be "
"toxic to any creatures that take a bite."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Intensify Flames
#: ./spells/pyrokinesis.json
msgid ""
"Manipulate an existing fire, increasing its heat.  This can turn small flames into raging conflagrations or spread fire through the area.  If used on a target that is on fire, the increased flames will cause additional damage.\n"
"\n"
"Level 5 leads to Molten Land.\n"
"Level 6 leads to Quell Fire with Banked Flames 5.\n"
"Level 8 leads to Thermogenesis with Banked Flames 10 + Brilliant Flash 7 OR Banked Flames 10 + Intensify Flames 8 OR Brilliant Flash 7 + Cloak of Warmth 6 OR Cloak of Warmth 6 + Intensify Flames 8."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Molten Land
#: ./spells/pyrokinesis.json
msgid ""
"You reach into the ground and unmake it, pouring your will into the stone until it runs like water.  A single tile of <color_light_green>ground</color> -- soil, sand, rock, pavement, flooring, or the low growth on top of it -- becomes a pool of <color_red>molten lava</color>.\n"
"\n"
"<color_yellow>This does not touch walls, doors, windows or fences.</color>  It melts the land, not what is built on it.\n"
"\n"
"<color_red>The lava is permanent.</color>  It will not cool, and anything that steps into it is grievously burned.  Be certain before you unmake the floor you are standing near.\n"
"\n"
"Level 4 leads to Banked Flames.\n"
"Level 7 leads to Blazing Aura with Cloak of Warmth 8 + Molten Land 7 + Thermogenesis 5 OR Cloak of Warmth 8 + Flamethrower 6 + Molten Land 7.\n"
"Level 6 leads to Cauterize with Incandescent Lance 5 OR Molten Land 6 + Quell Fire 6.\n"
"Level 6 leads to Cloak of Warmth with Banked Flames 6 OR Molten Land 6.\n"
"Level 13 leads to Conflagration with Flamethrower 8 + Thermogenesis 6 OR Blazing Aura 6 + Flamethrower 8 OR Molten Land 13 + Thermogenesis 6 OR Blazing Aura 6 + Molten Land 13.\n"
"Level 14 leads to Crucible with Conflagration 10 + Mass Hydrothermosis 6 + Molten Land 14 OR Conflagration 10 + Flamethrower 10 + Mass Hydrothermosis 6.\n"
"Level 9 leads to Incandescent Lance with Molten Land 9 + Quell Fire 6 OR Banked Flames 6."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Brilliant Flash
#: ./spells/pyrokinesis.json
msgid ""
"By strongly exciting the air at a particular point, you produce a burst of light.\n"
"\n"
"Level 5 leads to Flamethrower with Banked Flames 7.\n"
"Level 7 leads to Thermogenesis with Banked Flames 10 + Brilliant Flash 7 OR Banked Flames 10 + Intensify Flames 8 OR Brilliant Flash 7 + Cloak of Warmth 6 OR Cloak of Warmth 6 + Intensify Flames 8."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/pyrokinesis.json
msgid "[Ψ]Cauterize"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Cauterize
#: ./spells/pyrokinesis.json
msgid ""
"Using an extremely focused application of pyrokinesis, sear a wound shut to "
"stop the bleeding.  This is liable to be painful and is almost certainly "
"likely to just cause more damage if you don't have any medical knowledge.  "
"If the bleeding is too strong, cauterization will be ineffective, and there "
"is a <color_red>chance of infection</color> whether you are successful or "
"not."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Banked Flames (C)
#: ./spells/pyrokinesis.json
msgid ""
"Call up flames over your outstretched hand.  You can use them to heat up food, boil water, start fires, or anything else fire can accomplish.\n"
"\n"
"This power <color_yellow>is maintained by concentration</color> and <color_red>may fail</color> if <color_yellow>concentration is interrupted</color>.  It is <color_red>canceled by engaging in combat</color>.\n"
"\n"
"Level 6 leads to Cloak of Warmth with Banked Flames 6 OR Molten Land 6.\n"
"Level 7 leads to Flamethrower with Brilliant Flash 5.\n"
"Level 6 leads to Incandescent Lance with Molten Land 9 + Quell Fire 6 OR Banked Flames 6.\n"
"Level 6 leads to Pyrolytic Trap.\n"
"Level 5 leads to Quell Fire with Intensify Flames 6.\n"
"Level 10 leads to Thermogenesis with Banked Flames 10 + Brilliant Flash 7 OR Banked Flames 10 + Intensify Flames 8 OR Brilliant Flash 7 + Cloak of Warmth 6 OR Cloak of Warmth 6 + Intensify Flames 8."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/pyrokinesis.json
msgid "[Ψ]Quell Fire"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Quell Fire
#: ./spells/pyrokinesis.json
msgid ""
"As you can create fire, you can also unmake it.  You reach out and still the reaction itself, and the flames in the area simply <color_light_green>stop</color>.\n"
"\n"
"This puts out <color_light_green>fires on the ground</color> across the target area, and any <color_light_green>flames on your own body</color> whether or not you are in that area.  It does not cool what has already been burned, and it will not touch lava.\n"
"\n"
"Level 6 leads to Cauterize with Incandescent Lance 5 OR Molten Land 6 + Quell Fire 6.\n"
"Level 9 leads to Flameshield with Cloak of Warmth 10 + Quell Fire 9 OR Blazing Aura 6 + Quell Fire 9.\n"
"Level 6 leads to Incandescent Lance with Molten Land 9 + Quell Fire 6 OR Banked Flames 6."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Message for SPELL '[Ψ]Quell Fire'
#: ./spells/pyrokinesis.json
msgid "You still the flames."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Cloak of Warmth (C)
#: ./spells/pyrokinesis.json
msgid ""
"Control the temperature of the nearby air, warming you and protecting you against flames.\n"
"\n"
"This power <color_yellow>is maintained by concentration</color> and <color_red>may fail</color> if <color_yellow>concentration is interrupted</color>.\n"
"\n"
"Level 8 leads to Blazing Aura with Cloak of Warmth 8 + Molten Land 7 + Thermogenesis 5 OR Cloak of Warmth 8 + Flamethrower 6 + Molten Land 7.\n"
"Level 10 leads to Flameshield with Cloak of Warmth 10 + Quell Fire 9 OR Blazing Aura 6 + Quell Fire 9.\n"
"Level 6 leads to Thermogenesis with Banked Flames 10 + Brilliant Flash 7 OR Banked Flames 10 + Intensify Flames 8 OR Brilliant Flash 7 + Cloak of Warmth 6 OR Cloak of Warmth 6 + Intensify Flames 8."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Flamethrower
#: ./spells/pyrokinesis.json
msgid ""
"Spray fire in a cone in front of you.\n"
"\n"
"Level 6 leads to Blazing Aura with Cloak of Warmth 8 + Molten Land 7 + Thermogenesis 5 OR Cloak of Warmth 8 + Flamethrower 6 + Molten Land 7.\n"
"Level 8 leads to Conflagration with Flamethrower 8 + Thermogenesis 6 OR Blazing Aura 6 + Flamethrower 8 OR Molten Land 13 + Thermogenesis 6 OR Blazing Aura 6 + Molten Land 13.\n"
"Level 10 leads to Crucible with Conflagration 10 + Mass Hydrothermosis 6 + Molten Land 14 OR Conflagration 10 + Flamethrower 10 + Mass Hydrothermosis 6.\n"
"Level 12 leads to Mass Hydrothermosis with Flamethrower 12 + Thermogenesis 10 OR Flameshield 6 + Flamethrower 12 OR Conflagration 6 + Thermogenesis 10 OR Conflagration 6 + Flameshield 6."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/pyrokinesis.json
msgid "[Ψ]Incandescent Lance (C)"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Incandescent Lance (C)
#: ./spells/pyrokinesis.json
msgid ""
"Concentrate heat into a thin, searing beam capable of cutting through solid metal or welding it together.\n"
"\n"
"This power <color_yellow>is maintained by concentration</color> and <color_red>may fail</color> if <color_yellow>concentration is interrupted</color>.  It is <color_red>canceled by engaging in combat</color>.\n"
"\n"
"Level 5 leads to Cauterize with Incandescent Lance 5 OR Molten Land 6 + Quell Fire 6."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/pyrokinesis.json
msgid "[Ψ]Thermogenesis"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Thermogenesis
#: ./spells/pyrokinesis.json
msgid ""
"Heat the air nearby and maintain it, taking off the chill or turning winter to warm summer.\n"
"\n"
"Level 5 leads to Blazing Aura with Cloak of Warmth 8 + Molten Land 7 + Thermogenesis 5 OR Cloak of Warmth 8 + Flamethrower 6 + Molten Land 7.\n"
"Level 6 leads to Conflagration with Flamethrower 8 + Thermogenesis 6 OR Blazing Aura 6 + Flamethrower 8 OR Molten Land 13 + Thermogenesis 6 OR Blazing Aura 6 + Molten Land 13.\n"
"Level 10 leads to Mass Hydrothermosis with Flamethrower 12 + Thermogenesis 10 OR Flameshield 6 + Flamethrower 12 OR Conflagration 6 + Thermogenesis 10 OR Conflagration 6 + Flameshield 6."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Blazing Aura (C)
#: ./spells/pyrokinesis.json
msgid ""
"Surround yourself with a cloud of flames, damaging anyone in melee combat with you.  The flames also produce light.\n"
"\n"
"This power <color_yellow>is maintained by concentration</color> and <color_red>may fail</color> if <color_yellow>concentration is interrupted</color>.\n"
"\n"
"Level 6 leads to Conflagration with Flamethrower 8 + Thermogenesis 6 OR Blazing Aura 6 + Flamethrower 8 OR Molten Land 13 + Thermogenesis 6 OR Blazing Aura 6 + Molten Land 13.\n"
"Level 6 leads to Flameshield with Cloak of Warmth 10 + Quell Fire 9 OR Blazing Aura 6 + Quell Fire 9."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/pyrokinesis.json
msgid "[Ψ]Flameshield (C)"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Flameshield (C)
#: ./spells/pyrokinesis.json
msgid ""
"Your power over fire is such that you can now step directly into raging flames and walk through them unharmed, feeling no more than a pleasant warmth.\n"
"\n"
"This power <color_yellow>is maintained by concentration</color> and <color_red>may fail</color> if <color_yellow>concentration is interrupted</color>.\n"
"\n"
"Level 6 leads to Mass Hydrothermosis with Flamethrower 12 + Thermogenesis 10 OR Flameshield 6 + Flamethrower 12 OR Conflagration 6 + Thermogenesis 10 OR Conflagration 6 + Flameshield 6."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Conflagration
#: ./spells/pyrokinesis.json
msgid ""
"Create an expanding fireball that catches multiple targets in its wake.\n"
"\n"
"Level 10 leads to Crucible with Conflagration 10 + Mass Hydrothermosis 6 + Molten Land 14 OR Conflagration 10 + Flamethrower 10 + Mass Hydrothermosis 6.\n"
"Level 6 leads to Mass Hydrothermosis with Flamethrower 12 + Thermogenesis 10 OR Flameshield 6 + Flamethrower 12 OR Conflagration 6 + Thermogenesis 10 OR Conflagration 6 + Flameshield 6."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/pyrokinesis.json
msgid "[Ψ]Crucible"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Crucible
#: ./spells/pyrokinesis.json
msgid ""
"Concentrate the entirety of your power into a single white-hot point, "
"searing your target with the heat of a volcano."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Message for SPELL '[Ψ]Crucible'
#: ./spells/pyrokinesis.json
msgid "You focus all of your power onto a single point!"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Far Hand
#: ./spells/telekinesis.json
msgid ""
"Pickup items at a distance or push them away from you.\n"
"\n"
"Level 6 leads to Enhance Strength with Far Hand 6 + Momentum Alteration 5 OR Force Shove 6 + Momentum Alteration 5.\n"
"Level 5 leads to Kinetic Trap with Force Shove 5.\n"
"Level 8 leads to Lift Vehicle with Far Hand 8 + Slowfall 8 OR Enhance Strength 10.\n"
"Level 7 leads to Lifting Field with Lift Vehicle 3 OR Far Hand 7 + Momentum Alteration 5.\n"
"Level 15 leads to Megakinesis with Force Shove 15 + Momentum Alteration 10 OR Force Shove 15 + Lift Vehicle 6 OR Far Hand 15 + Momentum Alteration 10 OR Far Hand 15 + Lift Vehicle 6.\n"
"Level 5 leads to Momentum Alteration with Force Shove 5.\n"
"Level 10 leads to Wrecking Ball with Force Shove 10 + Knockdown 12 OR Far Hand 10 + Knockdown 12 OR Force Shove 10 + Mindhammer 7 OR Far Hand 10 + Mindhammer 7."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Force Shove
#: ./spells/telekinesis.json
msgid ""
"Shove a target away or pull it towards you with a burst of psionic force.  The distance the target can be moved depends on its weight versus your power level; heavier things will not go as far, and if your target is too heavy, you may not be able to move it at all.\n"
"\n"
"Level 6 leads to Enhance Strength with Far Hand 6 + Momentum Alteration 5 OR Force Shove 6 + Momentum Alteration 5.\n"
"Level 5 leads to Kinetic Trap with Far Hand 5.\n"
"Level 4 leads to Knockdown with Force Shove 4 OR Noisemaker 1.\n"
"Level 15 leads to Megakinesis with Force Shove 15 + Momentum Alteration 10 OR Force Shove 15 + Lift Vehicle 6 OR Far Hand 15 + Momentum Alteration 10 OR Far Hand 15 + Lift Vehicle 6.\n"
"Level 8 leads to Mindhammer with Knockdown 6 + Wave of Force 4 OR Force Shove 8 + Knockdown 6.\n"
"Level 5 leads to Momentum Alteration with Far Hand 5.\n"
"Level 3 leads to No Go Zone.\n"
"Level 7 leads to Wave of Force with Knockdown 4.\n"
"Level 10 leads to Wrecking Ball with Force Shove 10 + Knockdown 12 OR Far Hand 10 + Knockdown 12 OR Force Shove 10 + Mindhammer 7 OR Far Hand 10 + Mindhammer 7."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/telekinesis.json
msgid "[Ψ]Noisemaker"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Noisemaker
#: ./spells/telekinesis.json
msgid ""
"Using a focused burst of telekinesis, slam two objects together, or an object into the ground, or simply hit the ground with your powers, causing a loud noise.\n"
"\n"
"Level 1 leads to Knockdown with Force Shove 4 OR Noisemaker 1."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for the sound of spell '[Ψ]Noisemaker'
#: ./spells/telekinesis.json
msgid "a loud thump"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Message for SPELL '[Ψ]Noisemaker'
#: ./spells/telekinesis.json
msgid "You lash out at the ground with your powers."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Knockdown
#: ./spells/telekinesis.json
msgid ""
"Slam something to the ground with a burst of telekinetic force, doing a small amount of damage and downing them.\n"
"\n"
"Level 6 leads to Mindhammer with Knockdown 6 + Wave of Force 4 OR Force Shove 8 + Knockdown 6.\n"
"Level 4 leads to Wave of Force with Force Shove 7.\n"
"Level 12 leads to Wrecking Ball with Force Shove 10 + Knockdown 12 OR Far Hand 10 + Knockdown 12 OR Force Shove 10 + Mindhammer 7 OR Far Hand 10 + Mindhammer 7."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/telekinesis.json
msgid "[Ψ]Momentum Alteration (C)"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Momentum Alteration (C)
#: ./spells/telekinesis.json
msgid ""
"Edit the momentum of yourself and nearby objects to your benefit, slowing damaging force and slightly increasing your speed.\n"
"\n"
"This power <color_yellow>is maintained by concentration</color> and <color_red>may fail</color> if <color_yellow>concentration is interrupted</color>.\n"
"\n"
"Level 5 leads to Enhance Strength with Far Hand 6 + Momentum Alteration 5 OR Force Shove 6 + Momentum Alteration 5.\n"
"Level 10 leads to Inertial Barrier with Wave of Force 8.\n"
"Level 5 leads to Lifting Field with Lift Vehicle 3 OR Far Hand 7 + Momentum Alteration 5.\n"
"Level 10 leads to Megakinesis with Force Shove 15 + Momentum Alteration 10 OR Force Shove 15 + Lift Vehicle 6 OR Far Hand 15 + Momentum Alteration 10 OR Far Hand 15 + Lift Vehicle 6.\n"
"Level 6 leads to Slowfall."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/telekinesis.json
msgid "[Ψ]Slowfall"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Slowfall
#: ./spells/telekinesis.json
msgid ""
"Counteract the pull of gravity with telekinetic force, greatly reducing or even eliminating damage from falling and becoming much more buoyant.\n"
"\n"
"Level 9 leads to Levitation.\n"
"Level 8 leads to Lift Vehicle with Far Hand 8 + Slowfall 8 OR Enhance Strength 10."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Message for SPELL '[Ψ]Slowfall'
#: ./spells/telekinesis.json
msgid "You feel lighter."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Wave of Force
#: ./spells/telekinesis.json
msgid ""
"Unleash a telekinetic wave around you that indiscriminately knocks everything back.\n"
"\n"
"Level 13 leads to Earthshaker with Megakinesis 5 + Wrecking Ball 8 OR Mindhammer 9 + Wrecking Ball 8 OR Megakinesis 5 + Wave of Force 13 OR Mindhammer 9 + Wave of Force 13.\n"
"Level 8 leads to Inertial Barrier with Momentum Alteration 10.\n"
"Level 4 leads to Mindhammer with Knockdown 6 + Wave of Force 4 OR Force Shove 8 + Knockdown 6."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/telekinesis.json
msgid "[Ψ]Lifting Field (C)"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Lifting Field (C)
#: ./spells/telekinesis.json
msgid ""
"A knot of telekinetic force rides alongside you and takes the strain of your load.  While maintained you wear a visible <color_light_green>[Ψ]lifting field</color> and can carry <color_light_green>considerably more weight</color> — 2 kg more at first, rising past 400 kg once the power is mastered.\n"
"\n"
"It lifts weight, not bulk: your pack is no roomier, and you are no stronger.  The load simply stops pulling on your frame.\n"
"\n"
"This power <color_yellow>is maintained by concentration</color> and <color_red>may fail</color> if <color_yellow>concentration is interrupted</color>."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/telekinesis.json
msgid "[Ψ]Enhance Strength (C)"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Enhance Strength (C)
#: ./spells/telekinesis.json
msgid ""
"Focus your powers to allow you to move much heavier objects and smash through walls.\n"
"\n"
"This power <color_yellow>is maintained by concentration</color> and <color_red>may fail</color> if <color_yellow>concentration is interrupted</color>.  It is <color_red>canceled by engaging in combat</color>.\n"
"\n"
"Level 10 leads to Lift Vehicle with Far Hand 8 + Slowfall 8 OR Enhance Strength 10."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/telekinesis.json
msgid "[Ψ]Mindhammer"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Mindhammer
#: ./spells/telekinesis.json
msgid ""
"Smash a single target or small area with a fist of telekinetic force.\n"
"\n"
"Level 9 leads to Earthshaker with Megakinesis 5 + Wrecking Ball 8 OR Mindhammer 9 + Wrecking Ball 8 OR Megakinesis 5 + Wave of Force 13 OR Mindhammer 9 + Wave of Force 13.\n"
"Level 7 leads to Wrecking Ball with Force Shove 10 + Knockdown 12 OR Far Hand 10 + Knockdown 12 OR Force Shove 10 + Mindhammer 7 OR Far Hand 10 + Mindhammer 7."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for the sound of spell '[Ψ]Mindhammer'
#: ./spells/telekinesis.json
msgid "a heavy thud!"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Message for SPELL '[Ψ]Mindhammer'
#: ./spells/telekinesis.json
msgid "You smash your target with a fist of force."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/telekinesis.json
msgid "[Ψ]Lift Vehicle (C)"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Lift Vehicle (C)
#: ./spells/telekinesis.json
msgid ""
"Focus your powers to raise a vehicle just enough to change a tire or perform repairs.  As your powers increase, you will be able to lift heavier vehicles.\n"
"\n"
"This power <color_yellow>is maintained by concentration</color> and <color_red>may fail</color> if <color_yellow>concentration is interrupted</color>.  It is <color_red>canceled by engaging in combat</color>.\n"
"\n"
"Level 3 leads to Lifting Field with Lift Vehicle 3 OR Far Hand 7 + Momentum Alteration 5.\n"
"Level 6 leads to Megakinesis with Force Shove 15 + Momentum Alteration 10 OR Force Shove 15 + Lift Vehicle 6 OR Far Hand 15 + Momentum Alteration 10 OR Far Hand 15 + Lift Vehicle 6."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/telekinesis.json
msgid "[Ψ]Inertial Barrier (C)"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Inertial Barrier (C)
#: ./spells/telekinesis.json
msgid ""
"Create a telekinetic barrier around yourself to protect you from damage.\n"
"\n"
"This power <color_yellow>is maintained by concentration</color> and <color_red>may fail</color> if <color_yellow>concentration is interrupted</color>."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/telekinesis.json
msgid "[Ψ]Wrecking Ball"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Wrecking Ball
#: ./spells/telekinesis.json
msgid ""
"A burst of telekinetic force shatters the terrain at the target location, as well as anything caught inside.\n"
"\n"
"Level 8 leads to Earthshaker with Megakinesis 5 + Wrecking Ball 8 OR Mindhammer 9 + Wrecking Ball 8 OR Megakinesis 5 + Wave of Force 13 OR Mindhammer 9 + Wave of Force 13."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Message for SPELL '[Ψ]Wrecking Ball'
#: ./spells/telekinesis.json
msgid "You indiscriminately blast your targets!"
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/telekinesis.json
msgid "[Ψ]Levitation (C)"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Levitation (C)
#: ./spells/telekinesis.json
msgid ""
"Use your telekinesis and lift yourself up, defying gravity.  While not true flight, you can cross open air and descend safely.\n"
"\n"
"This power <color_yellow>is maintained by concentration</color> and <color_red>may fail</color> if <color_yellow>concentration is interrupted</color>.  It is <color_red>canceled by engaging in combat</color>.  It requires <color_yellow>even more concentration</color> than usual."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/telekinesis.json
msgid "[Ψ]Megakinesis"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Megakinesis
#: ./spells/telekinesis.json
msgid ""
"Telekinesis on a grand scale, this power allows you to move truly enormous amounts of weight, hurling a human-sized target at lethal speeds or picking up and throwing something monstrously large.  The amount of weight you can move is dependent on the power level.\n"
"\n"
"Level 5 leads to Earthshaker with Megakinesis 5 + Wrecking Ball 8 OR Mindhammer 9 + Wrecking Ball 8 OR Megakinesis 5 + Wave of Force 13 OR Mindhammer 9 + Wave of Force 13."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/telekinesis.json
msgid "[Ψ]Earthshaker"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Earthshaker
#: ./spells/telekinesis.json
msgid ""
"Seize the nearby earth with your powers and *wrench* it, toppling buildings "
"and knocking everyone nearby off their feet."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Message for SPELL '[Ψ]Earthshaker'
#: ./spells/telekinesis.json
msgid "The earth shakes!"
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/telepathy.json
msgid "[Ψ]Concentration Trance (C)"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Concentration Trance (C)
#: ./spells/telepathy.json
msgid ""
"Focus your own mind into a trance state, increasing learning speed.\n"
"\n"
"This power <color_yellow>is maintained by concentration</color> and <color_red>may fail</color> if <color_yellow>concentration is interrupted</color>.  It is <color_red>canceled by engaging in combat</color>.\n"
"\n"
"Level 6 leads to Mood Stabilization with Mind Sonar 5.\n"
"Level 5 leads to Telepathic Shield."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Telepathic Shield (C)
#: ./spells/telepathy.json
msgid ""
"You can protect your mind from the dangers of the post-Cataclysmic world.\n"
"\n"
"This power <color_yellow>is maintained by concentration</color> and <color_red>may fail</color> if <color_yellow>concentration is interrupted</color>.\n"
"\n"
"Level 8 leads to Obscurity with Mood Stabilization 6 + Sensory Deprivation 8 OR Sensory Deprivation 8 + Synaptic Overload 11 OR Sensory Deprivation 8 + Telepathic Shield 8.\n"
"Level 5 leads to Psychic Scream with Synaptic Overload 11 + Telepathic Shield 5 OR Primal Terror 7 + Telepathic Shield 5."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Mind Sonar (C)
#: ./spells/telepathy.json
msgid ""
"You cast your mind outward like a sonar pulse, sweeping the area for the minds of others.  While maintained, you periodically sense every <color_light_green>sapient mind</color> around you — people and other thinking things — and learn their <color_light_green>direction and distance</color>, even through walls and in total darkness.  You cannot see them, but you know they are there.  The <color_light_green>range grows</color> as you master the power, and greater mastery <color_light_green>quickens the pulse</color> and lets you pick out <color_light_green>familiar minds by name</color>.\n"
"\n"
"The walking dead, robots, and other <color_light_gray>mindless</color> things have no mind to sense.\n"
"\n"
"This power <color_yellow>is maintained by concentration</color> and <color_red>may fail</color> if <color_yellow>concentration is interrupted</color>.\n"
"\n"
"Level 6 leads to Mesmerize.\n"
"Level 5 leads to Mood Stabilization with Concentration Trance 6.\n"
"Level 10 leads to Network Effect with Mind Sonar 10 + Mood Stabilization 12 + Psychic Scream 6 OR Mind Sonar 10 + Obscurity 6 + Psychic Scream 6.\n"
"Level 7 leads to Synaptic Overload with Mood Stabilization 4."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Mood Stabilization (C)
#: ./spells/telepathy.json
msgid ""
"With the ability to edit others' thoughts comes the ability to edit your own, removing negative moods to a degree.  You have also learned to do this more subtly on others, calming their anger or assuaging their fears.\n"
"\n"
"When used on yourself, this power <color_yellow>is maintained by concentration</color> and <color_red>may fail</color> if <color_yellow>concentration is interrupted</color>.\n"
"\n"
"Level 8 leads to Beastmaster.\n"
"Level 12 leads to Mind Control with Mood Stabilization 12 + Primal Terror 5 OR Beastmaster 8 + Mood Stabilization 12 OR Mood Stabilization 12 + Sensory Deprivation 7 OR Obscurity 6 + Primal Terror 5 OR Beastmaster 8 + Obscurity 6 OR Obscurity 6 + Sensory Deprivation 7.\n"
"Level 12 leads to Network Effect with Mind Sonar 10 + Mood Stabilization 12 + Psychic Scream 6 OR Mind Sonar 10 + Obscurity 6 + Psychic Scream 6.\n"
"Level 6 leads to Obscurity with Mood Stabilization 6 + Sensory Deprivation 8 OR Sensory Deprivation 8 + Synaptic Overload 11 OR Sensory Deprivation 8 + Telepathic Shield 8.\n"
"Level 8 leads to Primal Terror with Synaptic Overload 8.\n"
"Level 4 leads to Sensory Deprivation.\n"
"Level 4 leads to Synaptic Overload with Mind Sonar 7."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Synaptic Overload
#: ./spells/telepathy.json
msgid ""
"Short-circuit and overwhelm a target's brain, causing extreme damage or death.\n"
"\n"
"<color_yellow>This power needs a mind to seize hold of.</color>  The walking dead, robots, and other <color_light_gray>mindless</color> things have none, and are <color_light_gray>wholly unaffected</color>.\n"
"\n"
"Level 11 leads to Obscurity with Mood Stabilization 6 + Sensory Deprivation 8 OR Sensory Deprivation 8 + Synaptic Overload 11 OR Sensory Deprivation 8 + Telepathic Shield 8.\n"
"Level 8 leads to Primal Terror with Mood Stabilization 8.\n"
"Level 11 leads to Psychic Scream with Synaptic Overload 11 + Telepathic Shield 5 OR Primal Terror 7 + Telepathic Shield 5."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Beastmaster
#: ./spells/telepathy.json
msgid ""
"Take control of an animal's mind, forcing it to obey you.  This also works on feral humans.\n"
"\n"
"<color_yellow>This power needs a mind to seize hold of.</color>  The walking dead, robots, and other <color_light_gray>mindless</color> things have none, and are <color_light_gray>wholly unaffected</color>.\n"
"\n"
"<color_light_green>Pack Leader:</color> once you know this power, every pet you have deals <color_light_green>25%</color> more melee damage.  Pets fighting within 12 tiles of you also gain a compounding <color_light_green>15%</color> for each packmate beyond the first, counting up to 8 pets (x3.33 at 8).  Pets near you also hold their nerve and will not flee until badly wounded.  Pets that wander off will find their way back to your side.  Pets that stray too far break off their hunt and return.  Guns, psionic powers and a few hard-wired abilities are not boosted.\n"
"\n"
"Level 10 leads to Beast Tamer.\n"
"Level 8 leads to Mind Control with Mood Stabilization 12 + Primal Terror 5 OR Beastmaster 8 + Mood Stabilization 12 OR Mood Stabilization 12 + Sensory Deprivation 7 OR Obscurity 6 + Primal Terror 5 OR Beastmaster 8 + Obscurity 6 OR Obscurity 6 + Sensory Deprivation 7."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/telepathy.json
msgid "[Ψ]Sensory Deprivation"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Sensory Deprivation
#: ./spells/telepathy.json
msgid ""
"Disconnect a target's brain from its senses, leaving it blinded and confused.\n"
"\n"
"Level 7 leads to Mind Control with Mood Stabilization 12 + Primal Terror 5 OR Beastmaster 8 + Mood Stabilization 12 OR Mood Stabilization 12 + Sensory Deprivation 7 OR Obscurity 6 + Primal Terror 5 OR Beastmaster 8 + Obscurity 6 OR Obscurity 6 + Sensory Deprivation 7.\n"
"Level 8 leads to Obscurity with Mood Stabilization 6 + Sensory Deprivation 8 OR Sensory Deprivation 8 + Synaptic Overload 11 OR Sensory Deprivation 8 + Telepathic Shield 8."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Message for SPELL '[Ψ]Sensory Deprivation'
#: ./spells/telepathy.json
msgid "You lock your target's mind away!"
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/telepathy.json
msgid "[Ψ]Primal Terror"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Primal Terror
#: ./spells/telepathy.json
msgid ""
"Use a target's own inner fears against them, paralyzing them with overwhelming terror.  The effect will not last long, but is completely immobilizing while it does, and it leaves a lingering horror behind in the target.\n"
"\n"
"Level 5 leads to Mind Control with Mood Stabilization 12 + Primal Terror 5 OR Beastmaster 8 + Mood Stabilization 12 OR Mood Stabilization 12 + Sensory Deprivation 7 OR Obscurity 6 + Primal Terror 5 OR Beastmaster 8 + Obscurity 6 OR Obscurity 6 + Sensory Deprivation 7.\n"
"Level 7 leads to Psychic Scream with Synaptic Overload 11 + Telepathic Shield 5 OR Primal Terror 7 + Telepathic Shield 5."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Message for SPELL '[Ψ]Primal Terror'
#: ./spells/telepathy.json
msgid "You unleash your target's fears."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Obscurity
#: ./spells/telepathy.json
msgid ""
"Use a light touch on others' minds to hide your presence.  You will be invisible to the target(s) while the power is in effect.\n"
"\n"
"This power is <color_red>canceled by engaging in combat</color> with your target.\n"
"\n"
"Level 6 leads to Mind Control with Mood Stabilization 12 + Primal Terror 5 OR Beastmaster 8 + Mood Stabilization 12 OR Mood Stabilization 12 + Sensory Deprivation 7 OR Obscurity 6 + Primal Terror 5 OR Beastmaster 8 + Obscurity 6 OR Obscurity 6 + Sensory Deprivation 7.\n"
"Level 6 leads to Network Effect with Mind Sonar 10 + Mood Stabilization 12 + Psychic Scream 6 OR Mind Sonar 10 + Obscurity 6 + Psychic Scream 6."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Psychic Scream
#: ./spells/telepathy.json
msgid ""
"Emit an uncontrolled psychic scream, attacking the mind of anyone nearby.  This power does not distinguish between friend and foe.\n"
"\n"
"<color_yellow>This power needs a mind to seize hold of.</color>  The walking dead, robots, and other <color_light_gray>mindless</color> things have none, and are <color_light_gray>wholly unaffected</color>.\n"
"\n"
"Level 6 leads to Network Effect with Mind Sonar 10 + Mood Stabilization 12 + Psychic Scream 6 OR Mind Sonar 10 + Obscurity 6 + Psychic Scream 6."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/telepathy.json
msgid "[Ψ]Beast Tamer"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Beast Tamer
#: ./spells/telepathy.json
msgid ""
"Perform mental surgery on an animal, making it friendly to you for a much longer duration.  The animal must already be friendly, either naturally or through powers such as Beastmastery, in order to be tamed.  This also works on feral humans.\n"
"\n"
"<color_yellow>This power needs a mind to seize hold of.</color>  The walking dead, robots, and other <color_light_gray>mindless</color> things have none, and are <color_light_gray>wholly unaffected</color>."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Message for SPELL '[Ψ]Beast Tamer'
#: ./spells/telepathy.json
msgid "The animal sniffs at your palm."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/telepathy.json
msgid "[Ψ]Mind Control"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Mind Control
#: ./spells/telepathy.json
msgid "Seize control of the target's mind, forcing them to do your bidding."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Message for SPELL '[Ψ]Mind Control'
#: ./spells/telepathy.json
msgid "You take control of your target's mind!"
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/telepathy.json
msgid "[Ψ]Network Effect"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Network Effect
#: ./spells/telepathy.json
msgid ""
"Forge an unconscious telepathic network between you and nearby allies, "
"allowing you all to send and receive information about nearby dangers and "
"react more quickly in combat.  The network requires at least one ally nearby"
" to be effective."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/teleportation.json
msgid "[Ψ]Blink"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Blink
#: ./spells/teleportation.json
msgid ""
"Step briefly into the void between dimensions and emerge at a random nearby location.\n"
"\n"
"The power <color_red>will fail</color> if the volume of your carried gear is too great.\n"
"\n"
"Level 4 leads to Apportation with Stutterstep 4.\n"
"Level 6 leads to Phase."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/teleportation.json
msgid "[Ψ]Stutterstep"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Stutterstep
#: ./spells/teleportation.json
msgid ""
"Manipulate space to increase relative distance around the target, reducing their speed.\n"
"\n"
"Level 4 leads to Apportation with Blink 4.\n"
"Level 10 leads to Displacement with Apportation 5.\n"
"Level 6 leads to Extended Stride with Phase 4.\n"
"Level 10 leads to Spacial Vortex with Extended Stride 4 + Stutterstep 10 OR Extended Stride 4 + Transposition 6."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Message for SPELL '[Ψ]Stutterstep'
#: ./spells/teleportation.json
msgid "You warp the space around your enemies!"
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/teleportation.json
msgid "[Ψ]Phase"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Phase
#: ./spells/teleportation.json
msgid ""
"By stepping for a moment into the void between dimensions, you can bypass a wall or walk from the ground to the roof of a house.\n"
"\n"
"Level 4 leads to Extended Stride with Stutterstep 6.\n"
"Level 10 leads to Farstep with Extended Stride 8 + Phase 10 OR Phase 10 + Spacial Vortex 6."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/teleportation.json
msgid "[Ψ]Apportation"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Apportation
#: ./spells/teleportation.json
msgid ""
"Rather than teleporting yourself, you could teleport an item you're holding somewhere nearby without having to follow it to its destination.\n"
"\n"
"Items that are <color_yellow>too large</color> cannot be apported.\n"
"\n"
"Level 5 leads to Displacement with Stutterstep 10.\n"
"Level 6 leads to Relocation with Gateway 8.\n"
"Level 6 leads to Warped Strikes with Extended Stride 10."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/teleportation.json
msgid "[Ψ]Extended Stride (C)"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Extended Stride (C)
#: ./spells/teleportation.json
msgid ""
"By warping space to shorten distances, you can make each of your movements carry you much further.\n"
"\n"
"This power <color_yellow>is maintained by concentration</color> and <color_red>may fail</color> if <color_yellow>concentration is interrupted</color>.\n"
"\n"
"Level 8 leads to Farstep with Extended Stride 8 + Phase 10 OR Phase 10 + Spacial Vortex 6.\n"
"Level 6 leads to Loci Establishment with Farstep 6.\n"
"Level 4 leads to Spacial Vortex with Extended Stride 4 + Stutterstep 10 OR Extended Stride 4 + Transposition 6.\n"
"Level 5 leads to Transposition with Displacement 5.\n"
"Level 10 leads to Warped Strikes with Apportation 6."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Message for SPELL '[Ψ]Extended Stride (C)'
#: ./spells/teleportation.json
msgid "Your steps devour the distance."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/teleportation.json
msgid "[Ψ]Transposition"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Transposition
#: ./spells/teleportation.json
msgid ""
"Entangle yourself with your target's position and, with a twist, swap places with them.\n"
"\n"
"Level 8 leads to Oubliette with Displacement 10 + Farstep 6 OR Displacement 10 + Spacial Vortex 8 OR Displacement 10 + Transposition 8.\n"
"Level 6 leads to Spacial Vortex with Extended Stride 4 + Stutterstep 10 OR Extended Stride 4 + Transposition 6."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Message for SPELL '[Ψ]Transposition'
#: ./spells/teleportation.json
msgid ""
"There is a moment of darkness and terrible cold, and you are somewhere else,"
" and so is your target."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/teleportation.json
msgid "[Ψ]Displacement"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Displacement
#: ./spells/teleportation.json
msgid ""
"With a touch, you can send your target through the void to re-emerge somewhere nearby, further away from you.  Targets that are <color_yellow>too large</color> cannot be displaced.\n"
"\n"
"Level 12 leads to Breach with Displacement 12 + Gateway 6 OR Gateway 6 + Oubliette 7.\n"
"Level 10 leads to Oubliette with Displacement 10 + Farstep 6 OR Displacement 10 + Spacial Vortex 8 OR Displacement 10 + Transposition 8.\n"
"Level 5 leads to Reactive Displacement.\n"
"Level 5 leads to Transposition with Extended Stride 5."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/teleportation.json
msgid "[Ψ]Reactive Displacement (C)"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Reactive Displacement (C)
#: ./spells/teleportation.json
msgid ""
"Maintain a field of unstable space around you, allowing you to effortlessly teleport enemies that strike you further away.  Unfortunately, their attacks will still hurt you as normal.\n"
"\n"
"This power <color_yellow>is maintained by concentration</color> and <color_red>may fail</color> if <color_yellow>concentration is interrupted</color>."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/teleportation.json
msgid "[Ψ]Spacial Vortex"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Spacial Vortex
#: ./spells/teleportation.json
msgid ""
"Affect the fabric of space, changing relative distance around a point so that everything moving within finds themselves moving towards it.\n"
"\n"
"Level 6 leads to Farstep with Extended Stride 8 + Phase 10 OR Phase 10 + Spacial Vortex 6.\n"
"Level 8 leads to Oubliette with Displacement 10 + Farstep 6 OR Displacement 10 + Spacial Vortex 8 OR Displacement 10 + Transposition 8."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Message for SPELL '[Ψ]Spacial Vortex'
#: ./spells/teleportation.json
msgid ""
"The air around your enemies shimmers as their forward motion carries them "
"rapidly towards each other."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/teleportation.json
msgid "[Ψ]Relocation"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Relocation
#: ./spells/teleportation.json
msgid ""
"Transport items in your hands through the Nether to an attuned location."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/teleportation.json
msgid "[Ψ]Warped Strikes (C)"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Warped Strikes (C)
#: ./spells/teleportation.json
msgid ""
"By warping space as you attack, you can allow your melee attacks to reach much further than normal.\n"
"\n"
"This power <color_yellow>is maintained by concentration</color> and <color_red>may fail</color> if <color_yellow>concentration is interrupted</color>."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/teleportation.json
msgid "[Ψ]Farstep"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Farstep
#: ./spells/teleportation.json
msgid ""
"Skating along the void between dimensions, move to a specific place nearby.\n"
"\n"
"The power <color_red>will fail</color> if the volume of your carried gear is too great.\n"
"\n"
"Level 10 leads to Gateway with Loci Establishment 6.\n"
"Level 6 leads to Loci Establishment with Extended Stride 6.\n"
"Level 6 leads to Oubliette with Displacement 10 + Farstep 6 OR Displacement 10 + Spacial Vortex 8 OR Displacement 10 + Transposition 8."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Farstep
#: ./spells/teleportation.json
msgid ""
"Skating along the void between dimensions, move to a specific place nearby.\n"
"\n"
"The power <color_red>will fail</color> if the volume of your carried gear is too great."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/teleportation.json
msgid "[Ψ]Oubliette"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Oubliette
#: ./spells/teleportation.json
msgid ""
"Teleport the target through the nether to some other dimension.  They are technically not dead, but they are no longer your concern.  Oubliette will occasionally fail when used against very powerful enemies, or succeed but cause damage to the teleporter.\n"
"\n"
"Level 7 leads to Breach with Displacement 12 + Gateway 6 OR Gateway 6 + Oubliette 7.\n"
"Level 2 leads to Dilated Gateway with Gateway 8."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/teleportation.json
msgid "[Ψ]Loci Establishment (C)"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Loci Establishment (C)
#: ./spells/teleportation.json
msgid ""
"Start concentrating on your current location, allowing you to return here at will with the [Ψ]Loci Technique power.\n"
"\n"
"This power <color_yellow>is maintained by concentration</color> and <color_red>may fail</color> if <color_yellow>concentration is interrupted</color>.\n"
"\n"
"Level 6 leads to Gateway with Farstep 10."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/teleportation.json
msgid "[Ψ]Loci Technique"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Loci Technique
#: ./spells/teleportation.json
msgid ""
"Transport yourself through the nether to your established loci location.  "
"You must currently be concentrating on your [Ψ]Loci Establishment (C) for "
"this to function."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/teleportation.json
msgid "[Ψ]Gateway"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Gateway
#: ./spells/teleportation.json
msgid ""
"Transport yourself through the Nether to an attuned location.  You must attune yourself to the place you wish to travel to.\n"
"\n"
"The power <color_red>will fail</color> if the volume of your carried gear is too great.\n"
"\n"
"Level 6 leads to Breach with Displacement 12 + Gateway 6 OR Gateway 6 + Oubliette 7.\n"
"Level 8 leads to Dilated Gateway with Oubliette 2.\n"
"Level 10 leads to Reality Tear with Breach 10.\n"
"Level 8 leads to Relocation with Apportation 6."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/teleportation.json
msgid "[Ψ]Dilated Gateway"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Dilated Gateway
#: ./spells/teleportation.json
msgid ""
"Transport yourself and every adjacent creature to a chosen location.  You "
"must have already attuned an area with [Ψ]Gateway."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/teleportation.json
msgid "[Ψ]Breach"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Breach
#: ./spells/teleportation.json
msgid ""
"Open a brief passage to the Nether using yourself or an enemy as an anchor and allow one (or more) of its inhabitants to come through.  You have no control over what finds the doorway and no ability to command it when it arrives.\n"
"\n"
"Remember that some denizens of the Nether die instantly in sunlight.\n"
"\n"
"Level 10 leads to Reality Tear with Gateway 10."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/teleportation.json
msgid "[Ψ]Flickerflash Stance"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Flickerflash Stance
#: ./spells/teleportation.json
msgid ""
"Through constant contraction and expansion of nearby space, as well as near-constant micro-teleports less than decimeter in distance, you can increase the effective momentum behind your strikes, make your exact position nearly impossible to determine, and your blows nearly impossible to stop.\n"
"\n"
"This power <color_yellow>is maintained by concentration</color> and <color_red>may fail</color> if <color_yellow>concentration is interrupted</color>.  It requires <color_yellow>even more concentration</color> than usual."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/teleportation.json
msgid "[Ψ]Reality Tear"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Reality Tear
#: ./spells/teleportation.json
msgid ""
"Make your own contribution to the Cataclysm by opening a rift in reality, "
"allowing all manners of netherium creatures access to Earth.  The rift is "
"temporary…hopefully."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/vitakinesis.json
msgid "[Ψ]Staunch Wound"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Staunch Wound
#: ./spells/vitakinesis.json
msgid ""
"You concentrate on your injuries, and they close and the blood flow stops."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Message for SPELL '[Ψ]Staunch Wound'
#: ./spells/vitakinesis.json
msgid "You summon up the energy to close your wounds!"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Detoxification
#: ./spells/vitakinesis.json
msgid ""
"When poisoned, you can isolate the poison and move it to your sweat glands where you will harmlessly sweat it out.  While doing so, your flesh will be toxic to any creatures that take a bite.\n"
"\n"
"Level 9 leads to Enhance Mobility with Burst of Speed 10 + Heightened Reflexes 6 + Overcome Pain 4 OR Burst of Speed 10 + Detoxification 9 + Overcome Pain 4 OR Combat Dance 4 + Heightened Reflexes 6 + Overcome Pain 4 OR Combat Dance 4 + Detoxification 9 + Overcome Pain 4 OR Heightened Reflexes 6 + Overcome Pain 4 + Personal Enhancement 10 OR Detoxification 9 + Overcome Pain 4 + Personal Enhancement 10.\n"
"Level 7 leads to Hardened Skin with Detoxification 7 + Personal Enhancement 8 OR Personal Enhancement 8 + Temperature Adaptability 6 OR Detoxification 7 + Overcome Pain 6 OR Overcome Pain 6 + Temperature Adaptability 6.\n"
"Level 8 leads to Heightened Reflexes with Adrenaline Trigger 8 + Burst of Speed 8 + Personal Enhancement 6 OR Adrenaline Trigger 8 + Detoxification 8 + Personal Enhancement 6."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/vitakinesis.json
msgid "[Ψ]Radiation Decontamination"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Radiation Decontamination
#: ./spells/vitakinesis.json
msgid ""
"Use your powers to isolate and flush radiation from your body.  Depending on"
" your level of contamination, this power may have serious side effects."
msgstr ""

#. ~ Message for SPELL '[Ψ]Radiation Decontamination'
#: ./spells/vitakinesis.json
msgid "You focus your powers on the corruption infusing your flesh."
msgstr ""

#: ./spells/vitakinesis.json
msgid "[Ψ]Anabolic Rejuvenation (C)"
msgstr ""

#. ~ Description for [Ψ]Anabolic Rejuvenation (C)
#: ./spells/vitakinesis.json
msgid ""
"You draw on your body's reserves to speed your healing a hundredfold.\n"
"\n"
"This power <color_yellow>is maintained by concentration</color> and <color_red>may fail</color> if <color_yellow>concentration is interrupted</color>.  It requires <color_yellow>even more concentration</color> than usual."
msgstr ""

#: ./ter_transform/ter_transform.json
msgid "You spend some time memorizing your location."
msgstr ""

#: ./vehicles/mom_vehicle_bridges.json
msgid "Medical Cart"
msgstr ""
